window.AKK_AFTER_TRANSMIGRATING_AS_A_TYCOONS_WIFE_MY_THOUGHTS_ARE_HEARD_BY_THE_WHOLE_FAMILY_CHAPTERS=(window.AKK_AFTER_TRANSMIGRATING_AS_A_TYCOONS_WIFE_MY_THOUGHTS_ARE_HEARD_BY_THE_WHOLE_FAMILY_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":401,"title":"Chapter 401: Shame on You for Pointing at Fifth Aunt and Saying She Doesn't Love Enough","paragraphs":["Although Qin Yi said that, Ji Fei still tilted her head inadvertently and asked, \"So, is this Lu Yunqing married? Is it really convenient for her to follow someone else's family like this?\"","Why did she always feel something was off?","Qin Yi paused for a moment and replied, \"She's not wearing a ring, so it seems like she's not married. Besides, although she's a close friend, she's about seven or eight years younger than Fifth Aunt Qin.\"","Ji Fei and Qin Yi exchanged glances, feeling guilty for their inappropriate thoughts and realizing it was rude to overanalyze.","Then they heard Qin Xian chime in,","\"She's Fifth Aunt's best friend, so why would she advise against divorce?\" Qin Xian said.","This remark immediately jolted both Qin Yi and Ji Fei.","That's right, they hadn't thought of that earlier.","Ji Fei considered that if it were her best friend, and the friend's husband had cheated, unless she was afraid of becoming the bad guy, she would definitely advise a breakup. It all depended on the best friend's character, but there was no way she would advise staying together.","Thinking about it, it did seem quite peculiar.","But if Lu Yunqing had ulterior motives, she wouldn't be advising reconciliation, would she? That didn't make sense either.","Oh well, since they hadn't met her yet, they shouldn't jump to conclusions.","Qin Yi stepped in to smooth things over, \"Let's not discuss this for now. She rushed over to break up the fight earlier and got caught in the crossfire. She seems kind-hearted. Also, I noticed Zhao Chengle is taking good care of Lu Yunqing, suggesting they have a good relationship. He likely treats her like a godmother. He even helped her go rest just now. She'll be back soon. Let's go first.\"","The three of them quickly headed toward the main building's grand hall. As soon as they arrived, they heard a teacup shatter on the floor.","From outside the crowd, they saw that it was indeed Grandpa who had thrown the teacup in anger, and it had directly hit Zhao Jianghe on the forehead. His forehead was now red and swollen.","Zhao Jianghe was kneeling on the ground, apparently acknowledging his guilt and not attempting to dodge.","Ji Fei looked closely and found him to be a handsome middle-aged man. Sitting beside him on the sofa was a pale, expressionless beauty.","Her cold and indifferent demeanor suggested she had completely lost heart and cared nothing for the trouble her husband was experiencing.","[Wow, Fifth Aunt Qin is so beautiful. What kind of woman would Zhao Jianghe need to see to betray her?]","Hearing Ji Fei's thoughts, the Qin Second family couldn't help but start paying attention.","Soon, Ji Fei, as expected, came to a conclusion.","[Not bad, Fifth Aunt Qin and her ex-husband didn't have any major issues. As for the cousin, Zhao Chengle, he's too young, so we don't need to consider him.]","The Qin Second family breathed a sigh of relief but at the same time became tense. That left only Sixth Uncle and the step-sister, didn't it?","A stern interrogation in the hall brought everyone back to reality.","\"Back then, at the same place, you knelt here and served me tea. What promises did you make? Have you forgotten them? Now you tell me you've fallen in love with someone else. How do you expect to face the wife who has been with you all these years, managing your business and raising your children?\" Grandpa scolded.","\"I've wronged Auntie Yu, I admit it, and you can punish me however you like.\" Zhao Jianghe's expression stiffened, but he didn't try to weasel out of it. \"I didn't want things to turn out this way, but before meeting her, I had never felt such intense love. I'm getting old, and I want to live for myself once, free from these rigid constraints.\"","\"Hah! Back then, we were both determined to spend our lives together. Now you're telling me that before meeting her, you never experienced true love? Bullshit 'true love'.\" Fifth Aunt Qin burst out. \"Don't think you can make your betrayal and infidelity sound so poetic and noble that it will make people think you have any morals or limits. Disgusting to the core! Before marrying me, you knew our family values. You thought you could uphold them, so you married me. Now you want to say you were naive and innocent?\"","Zhao Jianghe's face paled but he didn't refute her words.","Fifth Aunt Qin looked at her husband and finally couldn't be bothered to argue further. \"There's nothing left to say. Let's get a divorce.\"","Zhao Jianghe's face showed a brief flicker of pain but eventually, he nodded.","\"Since you're the one at fault, you should leave with nothing,\" Fifth Aunt Qin continued coldly.","Zhao Jianghe's eyes widened in surprise, clearly not expecting such ruthless words from her.","\"How could you cheat and then not be willing to face the consequences?\"","But Zhao Jianghe's face darkened, \"A complete loss of everything is unacceptable. I can give you more compensation, but you can't take my entire business away. That was built through my hard work.\"","\"What did you just say? Are you saying your business has nothing to do with me?\" Fifth Aunt Qin instantly erupted in anger. Her brothers also shot fierce glares at him.","Zhao Jianghe suddenly felt self-righteous, \"Yes, it was you who held the fort so I could focus on work without worries. You do have a share, but you can't make me lose everything. That would ruin my business!\"","\"You destroyed my marriage, so why can't I ruin your business? After all, I treated this marriage like a business, managing it carefully!\" Fifth Aunt Qin declared coldly.","Zhao Jianghe suddenly became furious, \"Auntie Yu, I cheated and I'm sorry for that, so I've tolerated a lot without complaint. But did you ever fulfill your role as a wife? Do you know how dangerous my work is? Did you ever care about me? You were only concerned with your social circle and being a wealthy socialite. Tell me, where were you when I was in danger? Safe at home, while I was risking my life. It was her who disregarded all danger to come to my side, enduring hardships together, surviving the ordeal. Otherwise, you wouldn't just be divorced, but a widow! Hah, perhaps you would have preferred that.\"","His words were extremely cutting, as if Fifth Aunt Qin only cared about status and reputation and completely disregarded her husband's safety.","Others who knew the details finally understood. Perhaps this crisis was what revealed Zhao Jianghe's infidelity, and he didn't care at all, wanting nothing more than to be with the one who'd gone through hardships with him.","He felt that person loved him more than his wife, even to the extent of risking her life, so he was prepared to break ties with the Qin family and dissolve the marriage.","Fifth Aunt Qin was so furious she laughed, \"So it was on your own that you two made it out? Wasn't it my rescue team who saved you?\"","Zhao Jianghe retorted, \"There were plenty of people who could have called for a rescue team. Only she was willing to die with me. She is the one who truly loves me. I don't deny you cared for me, but it's far less than what she did. Isn't it all right to choose the one who loves me the most?\"","By this point, Fifth Aunt Qin was too exhausted to argue any further.","[Damn, keep arguing, Fifth Aunt Qin! Don't you have anything to say about what you've done? Don't you need to tell him? Wasn't all that socializing in the high society for his sake? If it weren't for your maneuvering with those powerful factions, his business would have been even more precarious. Besides, who was it that calmed the family when things went south, who stabilized the company, who recovered the lost goods, who relentlessly contacted the embassy, who closely monitored the rescue team's movements to adjust the plan, who prepared medical supplies in advance for timely treatment? If it weren't for Fifth Aunt Qin's tireless efforts, you and your mistress would have died out there, and you still have the nerve to point a finger at Fifth Aunt Qin and say she didn't love enough? How do you think just saying the word 'love' could summon a saint to save you?]"]},{"number":402,"title":"Chapter 402: How Strange, This Son, and This Best Friend","paragraphs":["Ji Fei's rant directly left Qin Second's family speechless.","Initially, they had almost been swayed by Zhao Jianghe’s blatant bias, nearly letting their thoughts be twisted into thinking his actions were somewhat justified. Granted, their Fifth Aunt Qin was already wonderful, but it seemed like this other woman had given even more, so what could they do if Zhao Jianghe’s heart had wandered?","But now, listening to Ji Fei’s words, they felt absolutely livid.","The younger generation couldn’t speak up, but Qin's Father and Qin's Mom were not going to let Zhao Jianghe off the hook.","Qin's Father spoke coldly, “Heh, Zhao Jianghe, you should really get your eyes checked—no, better yet, get your brain checked!”","Zhao Jianghe was startled and looked unconvinced at Qin's father, convinced that he wasn’t in the wrong.","“Let me ask you,” Qin's Father continued, “Fifth Aunt Qin wasn’t into socializing back at home, so why did she suddenly need to integrate into some so-called ‘Ladies' Circle’ over there, just to socialize and indulge in her hobbies? Even if I don’t know the specifics, I can guess it was all for your sake, wasn’t it?”","Zhao Jianghe’s expression subtly changed.","Fourth Uncle Qin had the most authority on the matter. “When I first arrived in G City, it was my wife who helped me expand my network. She said she wanted to introduce me to more influential people so that I wouldn’t get stifled by local snakes in my business. But after she got involved, I encountered numerous stubborn hurdles. I’m grateful for all she did, even though all I ever wanted was for her to do what she enjoyed.”","If Fourth Uncle Qin was wielding a soft knife, then Third Uncle Qin was using a hard one. He bluntly analyzed, “So, the safety of your business now—does it have something to do with my sister’s social connections?”","This time, Zhao Jianghe’s face completely paled. He had to admit that the men behind those women were indeed powerful, with connections that ran both black and white...","“What’s even funnier,” Qin's Mom chipped in coldly, “is your claim that our family’s sister only needs to make phone calls. I don’t know the exact details, but I’m guessing when Fifth Aunt Qin heard about your troubles, she couldn’t have been sleeping soundly or enjoying her meals, could she? And after you got out, all you did was marvel at how others risked their lives for you? Never once did you wonder why everything at home was stable, why the company was still intact. In a place as chaotic as yours, do you really think the rescue teams would be so thorough and quick? If no one had been monitoring the situation and taking action, do you think you’d have been rescued so promptly?”","Zhao Jianghe’s eyes flickered uncertainly as he glanced at Fifth Aunt Qin.","Even the Eldest Brother-in-law couldn’t hold back and chimed in, “That place must have had terrible signal, making it extremely inconvenient to stay in touch. If Fifth Aunt Qin wanted to get you rescued as fast as possible, she had to arrange for external help, didn’t she? Are you saying you’re blaming her for not dropping everything and coming to find you herself? Our Fifth Aunt Qin isn’t some clueless idiot who’d do something so counterproductive.”","Zhao Jianghe’s face turned a shade of green.","“Honey, don’t be too harsh,” Auntie smirked. “Maybe his mistress is some kind of superman who can save him with just love, right? No mess, no foul. But I wonder... while my unassuming sister was tirelessly arranging rescue operations, what exactly were you and your lover doing? Were you exchanging sweet nothings, swearing eternal love? Or were you cozy and cuddly, waiting for some miracle to happen?”","Wow, absolute annihilation! This is so satisfying to listen to. It’s clear that everyone is sharp—Zhao Jianghe deserved every bit of this verbal beating for being blind and clueless. Deserved it!","Meanwhile, Qin's Father and Qin's Mom secretly applauded Ji Fei in their hearts. If it weren’t for her, they might have also been misled. Thankfully, they brought up the doubts, and others followed suit. Otherwise, their sister would have been left feeling disheartened.","At this point, Zhao Jianghe couldn’t help but think back to those days, but he couldn’t recall the hardships—only the moments of emotional bonding. Even though she was so delicate and had suffered for him, as a man, how could he not be moved?","Yet, what everyone said made sense. Still, he felt their words exaggerated. Their strenuous efforts to survive were the main story, and what Yu did was more like a nice touch—not the lifeline.","Even without her, someone else would have stepped up. But only one person was willing to risk everything for him.","No one had experienced the same despair he had, which was why they could speak so flippantly.","“I... I know Yu did a lot. I’m not denying that, but... I can’t lose everything and start over. I need to give her a stable life. At least leave me a company team—you can take everything else.” Zhao Jianghe said in a defeated tone.","Fifth Aunt Qin’s eyes reddened slightly. “You really are quite the romantic, aren’t you? I...”","【Argh, don’t back down! Why give them anything? If the company is left intact, the Zhao family can easily step in and restore everything. Letting them live comfortably is just adding fuel to your own misery. A woman must be ruthless to hold her ground!】","Qin's Father and Qin's Mom heard this and hesitated to speak, as this was Fifth Aunt Qin’s decision. But judging from Ji Fei’s words, it seemed Fifth Aunt Qin was planning to let him off the hook.","Just as they were thinking, a voice suddenly interrupted.","“Mom, since Dad’s demands are so low, if you don’t agree, aren’t you being a bit unreasonable?”","【Huh?】","Ji Fei was stunned and turned to see a young man who looked quite similar to the Qin cousins, all of whom were quite good-looking. He was supporting a frail woman with a sad expression.","The woman had long flowing hair and wore a pure white dress, like a serene daffodil in a tranquil room.","At that moment, Lu Yunqing’s eyes were red and swollen.","Fifth Aunt Qin was about to ask about her injuries when Zhao Jianghe interrupted.","“Are you hurt?” Zhao Jianghe suddenly asked.","The surrounding people found the question momentarily strange but quickly got distracted, as Lu Yunqing had rushed to Fifth Aunt Qin’s side, her tears brimming. “You really want a divorce? After all these years together, how can you just say you’re leaving? Don’t be impulsive—many wealthy families go through this kind of thing!”","Facing her, Fifth Aunt Qin’s expression softened slightly. “I know you’re worried about me, but I don’t want to continue like this.”","But Lu Yunqing turned to Zhao Jianghe. \"Brother Zhao, please reconsider!\"","Zhao Jianghe’s face was bitter, but he insisted, “I want to give her a home.”","Tears streamed down from Lu Yunqing’s eyes.","“I don’t oppose your divorce, but regarding the property division you mentioned earlier, I don’t agree.” Zhao Chengle stepped forward again to voice his opinion.","【What a great son. Apparently, sons just can’t sympathize with their mothers, huh?】","Qin Xian and Qin Zhao immediately sided with their mother, making it clear they were nothing like that!","【Though, something feels... off. This son, and this best friend... it feels like there’s something strange going on. Is this just a regular affair-induced divorce? I need to check it out.】"]},{"number":403,"title":"Chapter 403: What Did October Pregnancy Give Birth To","paragraphs":["Ji Fei's sudden outburst left the Qin Second family in a state of uncertainty, trying to piece together what was happening.","But similar to Ji Fei's earlier reaction, it couldn't be possible that someone would openly bring a mistress along, right? That would be too absurd and jaw-dropping. No way, absolutely impossible!","However, they hadn't heard Fifth Aunt Qin mention anything about a mistress. Could it be that she hadn't even met her?","Wait, something seemed off here.","Meanwhile, upon hearing her son's words, Fifth Aunt Qin was furious. She had already given up on having the last word, but her son's stance deeply upset her. She felt that her son should unconditionally stand by her side, after all, it was his father who had torn the family apart.","But now, her son believed she was being too extreme.","\"You think I should just step aside for that mistress? Let them live happily ever after?\" Fifth Aunt Qin exclaimed in disbelief.","Lu Yunqing shuddered beside her, and Zhao Chengle's face tightened momentarily. Zhao Jianghe, on the other hand, suddenly snapped, \"Don't say that! I was wrong to you, but don't call her a mistress. She hasn't done anything wrong; it's all my fault!\"","Fifth Aunt Qin looked at Zhao Jianghe in confusion, snorting in disbelief. She then turned to her son, as if silently asking, \"Are you going to defend her like this?\"","Zhao Chengle, feeling irritated, scratched his head. \"I didn't mean it that way. It's my dad's fault, but... he's still my dad. Do you want him to have nothing at all? Rebuilding the family business from scratch would be tough after returning to the Zhao family. Just consider it for my sake, and leave him some chance to rise again.\"","Clearly, this son genuinely cared for his father.","Fifth Aunt Qin was willing to let go, but she didn't want her son to beg for it. It felt like her son was betraying her by siding with his father. So in that moment, Fifth Aunt Qin couldn't help but act stubbornly. \"I won't give it to you. What are you going to do about it?\"","\"Mom!\" Zhao Chengle frowned. \"Dad's not easy either. He finally managed to return peacefully, and that woman did play a role in it. You can't be so unsympathetic!\"","Fifth Aunt Qin was stunned, almost thinking she was hallucinating. Her son not only defended his father but also spoke up for the mistress who had destroyed their family. It was utterly baffling.","Perhaps in her son's eyes, that woman really had saved his father.","Fifth Aunt Qin began to wonder if she was being too stubborn.","Was it possible that even with her plans, if that woman hadn't gone to Zhao Jianghe, he would have died for sure?","Fifth Aunt Qin fell into internal turmoil, while the rest of the Qin family was seething. Zhao Chengle, despite having Qin blood, was spouting nonsense.","[Oh my God! I need to restrain myself, can't just lash out without evidence. Why am I always stuck dealing with a bunch of lunatics? And why do they always flare up right in front of me? Your mom must not have thought it through before giving birth to you; she probably regretted it and wished she could shove you back inside for a reboot!]","The Qin Second family: ...that was quite a nasty rant! Was she cursing at Zhao Chengle for those provoking words of his?","[What a beast, a complete beast! Nine months of pregnancy and look what she gave birth to!]","The Qin Second family was dying of curiosity. What exactly was going on? This seemed more complicated than it appeared.","[You three are ganging up on the outsider together? But that outsider is your own mother!]","The Qin Second family: ...this was some serious gossip.","Their eyes uncontrollably drifted toward the woman standing there, looking innocent and harmless.","[Zhao Chengle, if you still have any shred of humanity, you should have told your mom the moment you found out about your dad's affair with her best friend. Is it because your mom was a bit strict with you, while this so-called aunt showered you with affection, covering for your laziness at every turn? Do you think she cares more for you than your own mother? You're just like your dad, both blind and foolish!]","The Qin Second family gasped, feeling their blood boil, struggling to catch their breath.","What a spineless, traitorous kid!","[Just because this aunt cried and confessed in front of you, taking all the blame on herself and talking about true love, you believed her? And you feel sorry for her and your dad, thinking it was a love that couldn't be suppressed? Wow, your mom became the evil stepmother, huh?]","The Qin Second family felt their blood pressure skyrocket.","[Watching this aunt sob about leaving and not entangling anymore, you couldn't bear it and even argued with your dad, saying he wasn't responsible enough. And now here you are, convinced that your dad needs to take responsibility. She pulls off this grand gesture of chasing after him across the country, and you completely side with her, indifferent to how much your mom hurts. You even think that since your dad doesn't love your mom, divorce is the right choice. True, divorce might be the right call, but you need to figure out whose side you're on. Who's the real victim here?]","[You sure have some nerve! Now you're arguing for your dad's sake, but it's really about wanting your dad and that aunt to live happily ever after. I see it now. You're tired of your current mom and want a younger, prettier one who'll spoil you endlessly, right?]","The Qin Second family: We want to hit someone. Seriously, we want to hit someone. No wonder Ji Fei had to restrain herself earlier; it must be driving her insane seeing this wretch in front of her.","[Oh my god, I've never seen such a bold mistress. Someone who befriended Fifth Aunt Qin wholeheartedly while secretly gazing at her husband. Are you starring in some tragic love drama? You played the seductress but felt so innocent, like it wasn't your fault but a love that couldn't be resisted. Zhao Jianghe is just as ridiculous, unable to resist the constant temptation of a young, beautiful face. Probably never cheated before because he didn't have the chance. Now that a ripe opportunity presented itself, he took it. Is this his midlife crisis?]","The Qin Second family felt spiritually poisoned, unable to imagine how these two could have carried on so blatantly under Fifth Aunt Qin's nose. The way they seemed so torn yet hooking up right in front of her, didn't they feel disgusted with themselves?","[After being caught by Zhao Chengle, they played the \"tortured love\" card, acting aloof and rejecting each other while constantly falling back into each other's arms, right? Pretending to leave, but as soon as one got into trouble, the other came running with no hesitation. I'll give them credit for boldness, but it's so disgusting. The funniest part is, now that they've decided to never part, they're convincing the victim not to divorce. What's the deal? Trying to seem noble and innocent? Oh, you don't want them to divorce because then you might feel like a real homewrecker. Aren't you just trying to be the discreet lover, living secretly with Zhao Jianghe somewhere, away from Fifth Aunt Qin's reach?]","The Qin Second family: What a hypocritical, revolting duo.","So Lu Yunqing doesn't want them to divorce and prefers to keep her role as the secret lover, living separately from Fifth Aunt Qin?","Wait... so the rest of the Zhao family knew about this, and only Fifth Aunt Qin was kept in the dark?","This is utterly outrageous!","Just as the Qin Second family was about to lose control and explode,","a loud thud suddenly echoed through the hall.","It was the sound of the grandfather's cane hitting the floor.","Apparently, Zhao Chengle's words had also stirred the old man's anger."]},{"number":404,"title":"Chapter 404: How Dare You Be Such a Bold Homewrecker","paragraphs":["The entire household fell into complete silence because of this statement.","Zhao Chengle, Zhao Jianghe, and Lu Yunqing all couldn't help but feel nervous.","The pressure was naturally extraordinary.","\"Chengle,\" the Old Master spoke slowly.","Zhao Chengle thought the Old Master was going to reprimand him, but he didn't think he had said anything wrong. His father and the stepmother had already been through a lot, and it wasn't their fault to fall in love with each other. Love was uncontrollable, and the stepmother was willing to die for his father. If he could meet such a gentle, thoughtful, and kind woman who devoted herself entirely to him, he would also be fearless.","Coming from a family like theirs, it was already difficult to find true love. If they found it, cherishing it wasn't wrong.","Moreover, after the divorce, his mother could have received the greatest compensation, yet she chose to take everything away. What would happen to his father and the stepmother afterward? The Zhao family would surely strongly rebuke them and even attempt to break them up, forcing his father to placate his mother.","Since they had already come this far, there was no need to continue the entanglement. He didn't want to see a resentful mother and a pitiful father in the future.","\"Grandpa,\" Zhao Chengle said, \"Dad has been very good to Mom for so many years. Even if he made the last mistake, is it really so unforgivable? No one is perfect!\"","The Old Master said, \"I'm not here to preach. I'm giving you a choice.\"","\"What? I'm an adult; I don't need to choose between my parents.\" Zhao Chengle thought the Old Master was talking about this.","But the Old Master directly said, \"I'm giving you a choice. If you support your father keeping one-tenth of the property, then you will lose all inheritance rights to everything your mother possesses! If you choose to help your mother and make your father penniless, then everything your mother gets, including part of the Qin Family's assets, will be yours. You choose.\"","【Heh heh, Grandpa is doing great. Making him choose between his father and mother. Choose wrong, and let this ungrateful brat taste some bitter consequences.】","As soon as the Old Master said this, not only did Zhao Chengle's face change, but so did Zhao Jianghe's and Lu Yunqing's.","【Zhao Jianghe's face changed; I can understand that, as it's his son's interests. But why did your face change, little mistress? Do you really regard Zhao Jianghe as your own son? Hmm? Wait, oh, I see. You must think that being penniless isn't so bad. If Zhao Jianghe really can't make it, there's still his son to fill in. But if the son also ends up with nothing, then both father and son will have to bow to the Zhao family. Seems you're not purely innocent either. You're quite swift in analyzing the pros and cons.】","Zhao Chengle came to his senses and became somewhat resentful, feeling that his grandfather was insulting him, believing that money could sway his decision. How could he be such a person?","\"Grandpa, I always thought you were a just and strict elder. How could you force me to make such a choice? They are my parents; I don't want to hurt either of them,\" Zhao Chengle said, his eyes red. \"Dad has already promised to compensate. Is that not enough? Do you have to drive us to such an absolute break, forcing me to take sides with Mom? That's really too much!\"","\"Dad, it's my fault. There's no need to treat Lele like this,\" Zhao Jianghe said. \"You're forcing him to choose between me and Auntie Yu. That's too cruel for the child.\"","\"He's not a child anymore. He's an adult, and adults have the right to discern right from wrong and make choices,\" the Old Master said coldly.","Zhao Chengle, also stubborn, said directly, \"I am discerning right from wrong. I think Dad made a mistake, but it wasn't that big of a mistake. That person saved Dad, and Dad wants to be with her. Is that so unbearable? Is it better for Mom and Dad to be entangled without feelings?\"","The Old Master looked at Zhao Chengle, his expression becoming increasingly cold. \"I don't deny that, from your perspective, what you're saying might make some sense. But our Qin Family has one principle: we protect our own unconditionally. If we don't side with our own family, what's the point of staying in the family? Remember, you can be our grandson, or you can choose not to be! We recently kicked out a grandson; we don't mind losing another one. If you continue to disrespect your mother and show her no affection, you don't have to acknowledge us as your relatives!\"","\"Master!\" Grandma Lv, who had been quiet all along, grew anxious. She had always cared for every younger generation.","The Old Master waved his hand, signaling Grandma Lv not to intervene, and directly said, \"In this matter, your mother is the sole victim. As a Zhao family wife and your mother, she hasn't made a single wrong step. You can't bully her just because she doesn't act as you wish. Old man, I'm still alive, and no one can bully my child like this.\"","\"Dad~\" Fifth Aunt Qin's tears streamed down her face.","The Old Master turned to the two pale-faced men and said, \"You can't empathize with my daughter's grievances, so why should I care if you think the punishment is too harsh? Regarding the divorce, these are my words: my daughter says you're penniless, and you will be penniless. Unless the Zhao family wants to clash with the Qin family!\"","Zhao Jianghe's face turned completely pale.","Fifth Aunt Qin, who had initially wanted to be lenient, now felt supported by her father, and her brothers in the family were backing her up. Why should she constrict herself? If it made her feel better to make Zhao Jianghe suffer, then so be it. Let them say she was being excessive.","\"And you!\" The Old Master looked at the already pale Zhao Chengle. \"I'm giving you a choice. Do you still want to fight for your father?\"","Fifth Aunt Qin also looked at her son, truly hurt by him today.","Zhao Chengle said with resentment, \"Grandpa, do I even have a choice? Aren't you insisting on making my father penniless?\"","\"Heh, you do. If you support your father, maybe the court will rule differently, but the Qin family won't back down,\" the Old Master said, then directly ordered, \"Choose!\"","Zhao Chengle shuddered.","Lu Yunqing also couldn't help but pull on Fifth Aunt Qin's arm, subtly hinting to her not to escalate the matter so much; after all, it was her son.","Ji Fei now felt very annoyed when she saw Lu Yunqing still acting as a close friend. How could she be so thick-skinned?","Ji Fei's eyes suddenly lit up, and a wicked smile appeared on her lips. She directly said, \"Hey, you little third party, how dare you be so bold? The matter has escalated so much, yet you still have the audacity to cling to our Fifth Aunt Qin!\""]},{"number":405,"title":"Chapter 405: I Promise, I Will Leave with Nothing","paragraphs":["Upon hearing this, the entire room fell into silence, and all eyes turned to Ji Fei.","Especially the new family of three, their pupils constricted in shock.","Ji Fei immediately leaned closer to her husband, as if startled.","Qin Xian calmly wrapped an arm around his wife.","The Qin second family was almost scared to death, thinking Ji Fei had accidentally blurted out her true thoughts.","The most shocked person present was undoubtedly Qin Yi.","After all, Qin Yi had just introduced them moments ago.","\"You... are you talking about me?\" Lu Yunqing was the first to react, her eyes brimming with aggrieved tears.","\"Yes, I'm talking about you. Aren't you the mistress? I just saw you exchanging glances with your former brother-in-law.\" Ji Fei continued, unfazed.","Now, the eyes of those around her were filled with suspicion.","You... you misunderstood. I was talking to A Yu!\" Lu Yunqing quickly glanced at her best friend, feeling anxious.","But her best friend's eyes flashed with doubt.","“Are you Qin Xian's wife? How can you speak like this? She... she is a friend of your aunt!” Zhao Jianghe regained his composure and immediately questioned, after all, he was an elder, how could he be humiliated by a young person like this.","\"Ah? Really?\" Ji Fei looked skeptical.","\"Ahem, show some respect to our daughter-in-law. They weren't here earlier, and this is Ji Fei's first time here, she hasn't even met you, let alone others. She's still a child, how can she tell the difference?\" Qin's mother immediately defended her daughter-in-law.","Ji Fei immediately nodded aggrievedly.","Others: Still a child?","Though Ji Fei's actions were a bit peculiar just now. Could it really have been a misunderstanding?","“She's my very good friend from over there, her name is Lu Yunqing.” Fifth Aunt Qin spoke up: “You must be Ji Fei. This is an awkward first meeting; I'll properly greet you later.”","Seeing Fifth Aunt Qin forcing a smile, Ji Fei became even more unconvinced, \"Auntie, I'm sorry, I thought the former brother-in-law brought the mistress to apologize. I really didn't expect she'd be your close friend.\"","Hearing this, the few people relaxed a bit, and Fifth Aunt Qin forced a smile as well.","But the next moment, they heard Ji Fei say, \"I'm really envious of Auntie for having such a close friend. This kind of family matter, even a close friend isn't at ease and has to come along to accompany you. People might think our Qin Family is very discordant, and doesn't stand up for Auntie at all.\"","With that remark, those who hadn't heard Ji Fei's thoughts immediately sensed something was off.","Indeed, even if the relationship was good, it wasn't appropriate to get involved in divorce matters. Auntie had plenty of family members to rely on; there was really no need for a well-meaning friend to cross half the world to accompany her. Does she not have a job? No other matters to attend to?","However, it was improper to speculate. There were few here with their own close friends, who knew if some close friendships were like this.","Fifth Aunt Qin's complexion became subtly complex, as if she couldn't quite figure it out.","\"That's... I didn't feel at ease with A Yu. I've witnessed their happy family life, and I truly don’t want such a life to be broken. Any marriage's maintenance is not easy, how can A Yu leave this family? That would make A Yu too pitiful! Why can't she just take a step back?\" Lu Yunqing, her back drenched in cold sweat, still couldn't help but plead.","Fifth Aunt Qin couldn't help but furrow her brows, feeling somewhat despondent.","\"I don't like what you're saying. It feels like you're not here to support Auntie, but to act as a mediator for the former brother-in-law. Did the Zhao family bribe you, or is it that you actually have a better relationship with the former brother-in-law than with Auntie?\" Ji Fei said as if puzzled, \"As a best friend, shouldn't you be helping Auntie punch the cheating scumbag? Why are you constantly advising Auntie to forgive and let go?\"","Lu Yunqing was now truly shedding tears, \"What’s wrong with you, a junior like this? I came here with good intentions to mediate. Even the Buddha says it's better to not destroy a marriage than to destroy ten temples. Does my approach offend you? My parents divorced, so of course, I understand the pain of a broken family.\"","Ji Fei was dumbfounded. How could she have the audacity to say something like, \"It's better to not destroy a marriage than to destroy ten temples\"?!","Lu Yunqing was very good at crying, her tears fell like pear blossoms in the rain, making her pitiful and eliciting care and sympathy. It seemed as if she had truly been wronged.","Ji Fei noticed the former brother-in-law beside her, who seemed eager to embrace and comfort Lu Yunqing.","Zhao Chengle also appeared impatient.","“She came to help, what's wrong with you, always nitpicking and slandering, deliberately looking for her trouble, causing trouble on purpose?” Zhao Chengle shouted directly. The elders didn’t dare to speak; could he still be timid with his peers?","An aunt who was so gentle and kind, being bullied to tears, how vicious must this person’s mouth be! Wanting to continue scolding, he felt almost suffocating under the gaze that followed.","Qin Xian suddenly looked over with cold eyes, \"My wife is not causing trouble; she's speaking up for Auntie. It’s better than some sons, who are no better than a dog. At least a dog will unconditionally be loyal and protect its master!\"","Qin Xian rarely spoke so bluntly about someone, which shows that he was really angry.","The reasons could be many, but everyone sensed that the most was because of Ji Fei, someone said Ji Fei, and he lost his usual calmness.","Unknown why Qin Lao Er's family feels a sense of comfort and wants to smile at this scene. If it weren’t for Ji Fei, they might never have seen Qin Xian show such vivid emotions or speak such human-like words.","It’s just... the occasion wasn't right. Qin Xian cursed a bit too much, even equating his cousin to not being as good as a dog. It's fine to disregard the blood relation, but think of Auntie, she still sees him as her own son and he should at least save some face.","However, the other relatives all had indifferent expressions; in fact, they had been wanting to scold for a long time.","Zhao Chengle hadn’t seen Qin Xian many times, since Qin Xian rarely came to Y City, and Zhao Chengle lived abroad most of the time, occasionally meeting in the city where Qin Xian resided. Although they were not familiar, he knew Qin Xian's temperament, always distant and hard to approach, speaking in a cool tone, neither hurried nor slow, making people feel they could only observe from a distance.","Later, his reputation grew even more prominent, and the Zhao family often mentioned him, saying he had an extraordinary cousin, with the Qin family likely to become even more powerful.","So Zhao Chengle always had an inexplicable awe and admiration towards Qin Xian.","Previously, hearing that he was deceived in marriage, he was very angry and scolded that person.","And now his cousin was reprimanding him for that same person?","Hearing such a reprimand for the first time, Zhao Chengle's face reddened instantly, his eyes glistening with tears of grievance.","\"It was clearly her...\"","\"Ah, I had no ill intentions, I just found it strange.\" Ji Fei innocently said, then smiled again, \"Why are you so sensitive?\"","Ji Fei's seemingly all-seeing gaze instantly startled Zhao Chengle, making him begin to doubt whether his reaction was indeed too sensitive. After all, he had a guilty conscience, as if walking on a tightrope over a cliff, always worried about being seen through.","It was also because Auntie Lu was too kind-hearted, afraid of ruining her parents' marriage and feeling guilty, wanting to come along to dissuade; she’d rather be an unseen mistress than make her mother sad. Such a person who couldn't bear to hurt others, Zhao Chengle naturally also wanted to protect her, after all, Auntie was the one who played with him the best.","\"Alright, it's all a misunderstanding, let's not discuss this further. I agree, I will leave with nothing.\" Zhao Jianghe spoke up."]},{"number":406,"title":"Chapter 406: Could you do better if it were you","paragraphs":["It seems he's afraid of saying more and making mistakes, also to preserve his son's future right to inherit the property, after all, it's something he's worked hard for. Passing it down to his son is acceptable, but it’s a pity that Lu Yunqing has to accompany him in rebuilding his fortunes.","However, he believes that Lu Yunqing loves him so much, she will surely agree.","Lu Yunqing only feels a sense of loss within her, yet she doesn't say anything more. After all, even if she wanted to stop the divorce, she can't. And if she continues to persuade, there's a risk of exposing the truth. Although sooner or later, she will have to apologize to Yu.","But she hopes that day comes later rather than sooner.","For the remaining time, she’ll spend more time with Yu, trying to make her happy, as her final form of atonement.","Ji Fei caused a stir and then obediently stepped back, since she has no evidence, anything she says will not be acknowledged. She just hopes this situation will plant doubts in everyone's mind.","Otherwise, these people will be at the Qin family's residence, flirting when no one knows, which is just disgusting.","\"Hey, what did you just...\" Qin Yi quickly asks in a hushed tone from the side.","Ji Fei almost forgot about Qin Yi; she immediately activates her clever little mind to find an excuse. Then she hears her husband say: \"Didn't she just say it? She saw those two flirting, so she probably suspects something.\"","Ji Fei immediately hugs her husband happily, \"Yes, yes, that’s it.\"","\"Ah? There really was flirting?\" Qin Yi is dumbfounded. \"Could it be... true?\"","\"You can ask Fifth Aunt Qin later; does she know the mistress? If she doesn't know who she is, then isn't she the most suspicious?\" Ji Fei suggests.","Qin Yi is baffled and asks, \"Then why advise reconciliation? Does anyone willingly be a mistress?\"","\"Who knows what goes through a mistress's mind. Maybe she thinks she’s a saint and wants to accumulate merits? But those merits certainly won’t be enough, haha.\" Ji Fei says, unable to hold back her laughter, leaning against Qin Xian’s solid chest, her eyes sparkling with joy.","Qin Xian smiles gently, moving closer. \"What are you looking at?\"","\"Looking at how handsome my husband is.\" Ji Fei feels her heart flutter whenever Qin Xian does something.","Earlier, when he was scolding, she felt he was glowing, simply amazing.","Qin Xian can hardly resist his wife's gaze; he kisses her forehead without caring about the surroundings.","Qin Yi can't bear to watch, especially since they're still discussing the divorce.","With everything settled, they plan to arrange for a lawyer.","The lawyer needs to prepare materials and contact foreign law firms, so they'll have to wait a bit.","They’ll stay here for two more days.","Lu Yunqing, as the best friend, will naturally stay with Fifth Aunt Qin, while Zhao Chengle, still angry at the Qin family, stays as an external relative, so he cannot move out.","Logically, Zhao Jianghe should have no face to continue staying here.","Yet, he brazenly claimed to stay for one night, to handle things tomorrow, and pack his personal belongings, since he sometimes accompanied to visit the old master. If there’s anything with the lawyer, it’s easier to communicate immediately.","Fifth Aunt Qin didn’t expel him; although she has grievances, she isn’t ferociously enraged, so she arranged a guest room for him.","Before Lu Yunqing was scheduled to see a doctor, a guest room was prepared for her, which naturally will be where she stays.","This arrangement leaves the two of them alone in the guest-designated building.","Because Lu Yunqing stayed behind to have private conversations with Fifth Aunt Qin after the discussion, few took notice.","Even Ji Fei overlooked it, only seeing Lu Yunqing following Fifth Aunt Qin; then Zhao Jianghe carrying his luggage heading out.","Zhao Chengle, who had conflicts with them earlier, first went to the guest room with his father, then back to the building for the younger generation.","As he entered the hall where the group was talking, everyone turned to look at him, making him feel awkward but he had to greet them.","This time he was polite, even addressing Ji Fei as Second Sister-in-law, and apologized to Qin Yian and Ji Fei for the earlier conflict.","Although knowing he didn’t mean it and still felt Ji Fei was troubling Lu Yunqing, he was courteous.","Fifth Aunt Qin seems to have taught him well, though she failed unexpectedly.","Kids tend to resent those who strive for their future and appear more strict, even suspecting their motives. There might be some parents with impure intentions, but most worry about their children's ability to handle risks in the future.","Fifth Aunt Qin was strict with Zhao Chengle because the Zhao family wasn’t harmonious, while he had Qin backing, making him a target. He needed to be excellent to stand his ground, so she never allowed him to indulge at a young age.","However, Lu Yunqing always took advantage of Fifth Aunt Qin's strictness, showing pity and giving Zhao Chengle benefits, helping him evade, making him closer to her.","In this aspect, Fifth Aunt Qin is at fault ; Was Lu Yunqing really that good at pretending? Fifth Aunt Qin didn’t notice, considered her soft-hearted and needing guidance just like a child.","It seems Lu Yunqing completely understands this family of three; they are truly under her spell.","The most impulsive amongst them is naturally Qin Zhao. They meet annually at the old estate, so it's familiar; he takes the lead: “I’ve never seen you side with outsiders like this before, defending a mistress and your father, are you out of your mind?”","Zhao Chengle isn’t too reserved with him either. He replies: “Don’t look at me like that, you don't know the full story. But tell me, if you got married but then met a soulmate, and that soulmate is kind-hearted, refusing to destroy your family but is ready to give their life for you in times of need, can you guarantee you wouldn’t be moved?”","This hypothetical situation leaves many speechless. They listen carefully.","\"And I think my dad is quite responsible, once he realized he couldn’t separate from the other, he faced the result decisively. The Zhao family didn’t want him to divorce, neither did she ask for it. But he didn’t want to involve my mom, wanted to give the other person an explanation, and he’s done that well, hasn’t he? I won't deny my mom’s suffering, but I can also understand his situation. If it were you, could you do better?\""]},{"number":407,"title":"Chapter 407: Are You Good at Chatting, or Should You Just Stick to Drinking Your Wine","paragraphs":["Zhao Chengle spoke quite justifiably, and the others were momentarily swayed by his words.","Only the family of Qin Second showed disdain. If they hadn't heard Ji Fei's thoughts, they wouldn't have believed this guy could be so eloquent. Although he wasn't exactly inverting black and white, he did tarnish Fifth Aunt Qin's contributions while glorifying the deeds of the cheating man and his mistress.","\"I only know that if I marry someone, it’s because I love them. If I love them, I certainly won't be looking for some so-called soulmate. My eyes will always be on my wife. If you don't go looking around, how can you find a soulmate? That's ridiculous,\" Qin Zhao retorted directly.","Zhao Chengle's face stiffened, as if he was infuriated.","\"I think, if someone really had a kind heart, they wouldn't fall for another person's husband,\" Qin Rong couldn't help but chime in.","\"It's strange to go out of your way to meddle with someone else's husband, making it seem like she’s so capable. As elders say, does she have absolute certainty to save someone? If not, then isn't she just indulging herself?\" Qin Yan spoke with reservation.","Qin Xiaoyu bluntly added, \"She's just indulging in her own lust.\"","\"You guys... don't be so harsh, okay?!\" Zhao Chengle was getting flustered, feeling that these people hadn’t seen Lu Yunqing’s pitiful and agonized state, which is why they viewed her with malice.","\"Speaking logically, it wasn't your dad being responsible; it was your mom who caught him cheating, which led to the divorce. If she hadn’t found out, would your dad have divorced her?\"","Zhao Chengle was startled, his expression unable to hide his panic.","In fact, he was the first to arrive at the hospital back then. His father had promised to give Lu Yunqing a home, but Lu Yunqing adamantly refused, saying she couldn't hurt his mother or destroy the family. She didn’t want to be a bad woman; she just wanted to be by his father's side.","Ultimately, his father compromised and decided to keep it hidden for the time being. However, his mother eventually discovered the truth, which led to the uproar.","The logic of this sequence of events, when he had just spoken, he had unknowingly leaned towards their side.","Zhao Chengle was clear-headed for a moment but was still overwhelmed by his bias. \"Well... no one knows that, and I believe my dad would have left.\"","\"Heh,\" Ji Fei chuckled mockingly, making Zhao Chengle’s face turn red. Then Ji Fei suddenly changed the subject, \"Hey, do you have a girlfriend?\"","\"Yes... yes, I do,\" Zhao Chengle was caught off guard by the sudden question. He quickly recovered. \"Aren’t you asking what I would do if I encountered a soulmate? I would follow my heart and not drag anyone along.\"","Ji Fei rolled her eyes. \"Do you love her?\"","\"Of course!\"","\"Good then. If your girlfriend wants to break up with you because she found her soulmate, her one true love, would you smile and say congratulations?\"","Zhao Chengle was dumbfounded, but a flicker of anger crossed his face.","Ji Fei laughed outright. \"Looks like men really can only see things from a man's perspective, never considering how it would be if the roles were reversed. You just asked us if we could do better in such a situation, so first, ask yourself.\"","Zhao Chengle's eyes began to dart around, clearly confused.","Ji Fei wasn’t sure if this guy was redeemable. If he were her son, there would be no saving him—just discard him. That former sister-in-law could have another child, maybe Fifth Aunt Qin could even consider having a second child.","It’s clear the first attempt was a waste, might as well start anew with a fresh one.","Suddenly, Zhao Chengle picked up the red wine on the table and took a gulp, grumbling, \"Honestly... at first, I thought if Mom knew nothing, everything would be fine. I didn’t want my parents to divorce, but now that it’s come to this, what else can be done?\"","\"My goodness, your way of thinking is really harmful, and it’s hurting your own mother!\" Qin Zhao said.","\"As a woman, a strong woman, a Qin woman, we hope to know about such things first,\" Qin Wenqiang chimed in.","\"Why... why?\" Zhao Chengle asked. \"Many families just muddle through, and can changing one person really guarantee things will be better?\"","\"But Fifth Aunt is only in her forties, she can definitely start a new chapter in her life,\" Qin Jing joined the discussion.","Even Qin Jiaxi had some insight, softly adding, \"If you never know, you’ll spend your life working hard for a man who doesn’t love or respect you, managing his family’s business. And maybe, when he has an illegitimate child, he might even hand over the family business to them. If that happens...\" Qin Jiaxi pursed her lips. \"It’s as if you’ve lived in vain.\"","Zhao Chengle’s upbringing was different from theirs. Although he thought what everyone said made sense, shouldn’t life be about being pleasantly confused?","\"Bro, why don’t you say something,\" Qin Zhao asked, noticing Qin Yi hadn’t spoken up.","Qin Yi was startled, his expression odd, as he was still pondering whether Lu Yunqing was the hidden mistress. If she were, then the father and son bringing her here was truly disgusting.","After thinking about it, Qin Yi decided to ask Zhao Chengle, \"By the way, who’s the mistress? Have you seen her?\"","Zhao Chengle suddenly stiffened, his expression unnatural.","Those who didn’t know the truth were curious, asking what she looked like and what her background was.","\"I don’t want to discuss it,\" Zhao Chengle said awkwardly.","\"Did your mom see her? Know her?\" Qin Yi pressed on.","\"She... she hasn’t seen her, just heard about her. The woman is... weak, not aggressive. My dad was afraid my mom would...\"","\"Afraid Auntie would bully her? Who’s bullying whom now? That’s like the stereotypical innocent-looking jerk in TV dramas,\" Qin Xiaoyu exclaimed, surprised. \"No wonder you’re defending her; I think you’ve also been fooled, feeling sorry for her because she seems weak and innocent. She’s gone so far as to step all over your mom, and yet you haven’t stood up for her.\"","Zhao Chengle looked embarrassed.","Qin Zhao continued to mock, \"If it were me, I’d have already taken revenge for my mom, beating the crap out of the mistress, making her unrecognizable.\"","\"I’ve already said, she risked her life for my dad, she’s a sincere person, not some shameless mistress,\" Zhao Chengle impatiently retorted.","As if in Zhao Chengle’s eyes, that moment of life-risking devotion truly deserved the utmost respect.","Seeing Zhao Chengle so defensive, Qin Yi’s remark, \"Could it really be Lu Yunqing?\" got swallowed back. Given how fiercely he was defending her, he probably wouldn't admit it, using it to protect her no matter what.","If it really was Lu Yunqing, then this cousin was truly disappointing.","Qin Yi couldn’t help but say, \"Sincere person? Your dad only sees whoever is beside him, walking with him, while ignoring those far away, clearing obstacles for him. His smooth path isn't because someone is walking with him, but because someone beforehand has already cleared all the hurdles. Your dad doesn't see it, and neither do you beside him—it’s truly sad for Auntie.\"","Zhao Chengle felt he couldn’t argue with everyone, so in the end, he said nothing and simply changed the subject.","\"Enough about my family’s affairs, the outcome is already set, so what more can be said? Let’s talk about you guys. It’s been over a year since we last met, and this time... Second Brother and Second Sister-in-law are here, any fresh news? I wasn’t here when things got heated overseas, so I don’t know much about what’s happening here. Just now, Grandpa mentioned... something about not wanting a certain grandson anymore?\"","Everyone: ...","Ji Fei: \"You’re quite good at changing the subject, just stick to drinking your wine.\""]},{"number":408,"title":"Chapter 408: Oh my god, hurry up Catch the cheater","paragraphs":["Although they said that, other kind-hearted people still patiently informed him about the current situation here.","It is said that within less than a month, there have been divorces, breakups, hospitalizations, and imprisonments, making it a very lively scene.","Zhao Chengle's face turned green, probably suddenly feeling that their family's issues weren't such a big deal after all.","Ji Fei could tell from his expression. She couldn't help but silently complain.","【Your family's situation is not small either. It's highly possible that you'll end up like that grandson. After all, what you did is also extremely immoral. We must find a way to expose this. Lu Yunqing the white lotus is still shining brightly. We can't let Fifth Aunt Qin suffer double blows. Even if they divorce, she's determined to keep this secret from Zhao Jianghe. She doesn't even dare to dream of a wedding. She wants to keep it hidden until it's exposed. She doesn't mind being wronged, as long as, at that time, Fifth Aunt Qin can put aside all resentment and even bless them. I'm feeling sick just thinking about it.】","Qin Second's Family: Keep investigating that mistress's emotional journey. We're feeling sick too.","【There probably isn't much chance now. After all, in our territory, they must be very cautious. But about that matter you mentioned earlier, whisper some sweet nothings to my husband and get him to investigate. Then we can directly present the evidence to Fifth Aunt Qin.】","Qin Xian smirked, as he had already sent someone to investigate, knowing his wife's tricks, but he still wanted to hear how she would whisper in his ear.","【I don't think this is a double blow. For a woman, if her best friend betrays her and she's unaware, continuing to confide in her and maintain the friendship, only to find out later, that would be truly disgusting and may lead to depression!】","Qin Second's Family agreed wholeheartedly, strongly supporting a swift resolution.","After chatting for a while, the topic inevitably turned to Fifth Aunt Qin's situation, and Zhao Chengle repeatedly found himself clashing with everyone. He was afraid that if he drank too much, he might blurt out something he shouldn't, so he decided to step out for a walk to clear his head and rest. In truth, he was feeling troubled and embarrassed to stay any longer.","The rest continued chatting.","As it grew late, everyone was about to disperse when Fifth Aunt Qin suddenly arrived.","Everyone greeted her politely. This time, Fifth Aunt Qin brought gifts for everyone, especially for Qin Xian and Ji Fei, as she had been very pleasantly surprised and looking forward to their visit, despite the subsequent unpleasant events. She would have met everyone in a better mood today if not for those troubles.","Seeing that Fifth Aunt Qin seemed to be in a good state, everyone joked freely, saying things like \"new will replace the old\" and \"when Grandpa's birthday banquet comes, there will be many young talents for Auntie to choose from.\"","Fifth Aunt Qin laughed, then asked where Zhao Chengle's room was, as she wanted to talk to him.","\"He's not in his room. He stormed out for a walk after we irritated him,\" Qin Zhao cheekily said.","Fifth Aunt Qin sighed, \"Did you guys say something to him?\"","\"Wasn't he asking for it?\" Qin Xiaoyu pouted.","Fifth Aunt Qin sighed again, \"Maybe he resents me for being too calm back then.\"","\"Huh? Isn't calmness necessary to handle things properly?\" Qin Jing said in exasperation, \"Someone has to stay calm. He certainly didn't look like he could.\"","\"So, it's probably just a misunderstanding. When he matures a bit, he'll understand,\" Fifth Aunt Qin said.","It seemed that despite her son's hurtfulness, she still wanted to clarify things with him and hoped he would understand.","【What a pity... you don't know your son is hiding something even bigger from you. He... huh? Wait a minute...】","\"Auntie, why are you alone? Where's your best friend?\" Ji Fei asked curiously.","【Earlier, I thought Lu Yunqing would be pretending to be the perfect best friend, sticking closely to you.】","Fifth Aunt Qin didn't expect Ji Fei to be so interested in Lu Yunqing. Remembering Ji Fei's unfriendly remarks when she had misinterpreted the situation, she suddenly had a realization.","\"Oh, it's late, and she's tired. She went to the guest room to rest.\"","\"She's not sleeping with you?\" Ji Fei asked in surprise.","\"No, we're not little girls anymore. We don't have to sleep together just because we're having fun,\" Fifth Aunt Qin laughed.","Ji Fei suddenly found it hard to smile.","【So, the former brother-in-law is in the guest building, and the mistress is also in the guest building? Just the two of them? Alone? So, they're probably... Oh my god, let's catch them in the act!】","Qin Second's Family almost reflexively stood up, their spirits instantly on high alert.","Could it really be that explosive?","【Think of an excuse, think of an excuse...】","Just as Fifth Aunt Qin thought they had no more questions and turned to leave, Ji Fei instantly saw an opportunity. \"We'll accompany you. We just upset our cousin, so we should take the initiative to find him. After all, siblings quarrel, but we can't hold onto the anger till tomorrow.\"","Qin Second's Family gave a thumbs up. But then they thought, wait, how does this connect to catching them in the act? Zhao Chengle doesn't live there!","Qin Xian immediately hugged Ji Fei and stood up, \"Hmm, what my wife said makes sense.\"","Seeing Qin Xian's action, Qin Second's Family assumed there must be a complete plan and felt relieved.","The others were left completely confused, wondering if they needed to be so concerned about maintaining the relationship.","But seeing Qin Second's Family already on their feet, they also got up to not seem out of place.","Fifth Aunt Qin was bewildered but felt comforted, so she didn't stop them.","However, just as they stepped outside, Qin Second's Family panicked, fearing that if they directly encountered Zhao Chengle, it would all be over.","【Oh my god, I almost forgot. If we meet Zhao Chengle, it's all over. Luckily, there's no one outside for now. Let me check... Zhao Chengle is currently at Grandpa's little maze for Qin Xi and Qin Weiwei, still trying to find his way out. Now that we're all out, we need to figure out how to lead Fifth Aunt Qin there.】","Qin Second's Family: You're thinking about it now?","The group walked outward while feeling anxious.","Suddenly, Qin Xian said, \"I think I just saw Cousin going into the guest building. Is he perhaps visiting Zhao Jianghe?\"","【Oh my god, did Qin Xian just missee? He's not actually there. But that could work as an excuse!】Ji Fei's heart raced.","\"Ah? Really? Then I...\" Clearly, Fifth Aunt Qin didn't want to see her ex-husband again and was considering giving up on finding Zhao Chengle."]},{"number":409,"title":"Chapter 409: Is the soundproofing in the rooms here so poor","paragraphs":["【Ahhh, why is catching someone in the act so difficult? I just got carried away for a moment and now I'm in a frenzy!】","Qin Xian suggested, \"Why don't we go take a look? We've said a lot about Chengle earlier. If he gets provoked and clashes with Jianghe, it could get messy.\"","The hint of worry in Qin Xian's cold tone struck a chord with Fifth Aunt Qin, making her worry.","Others recalled their conversation earlier, where they had attempted to make Zhao Chengle see how unreasonable his father was and how hard his mother had it. If he took their words to heart, it was possible he might confront his father.","Of course, this was assuming the best outcome. Mostly, Fifth Aunt Qin found Qin Xian's suggestion very convincing.","Qin Yi seemed to have an idea and chimed in, \"Why don't we all go check it out?\"","Qin Zhao quickly agreed, \"Yes, let's go take a look. If nothing's happening, no harm done.\"","Fifth Aunt Qin initially didn't want to go, but before she knew it, she was swept along by the group.","【Ah, opportunity just presented itself! This is going too smoothly, almost unbelievable. My husband is my lucky star! Let the truth be unveiled on our turf; we'll make them pay! Catching someone in the act is just too exciting, hehe!】","Qin Second's family also found the situation exhilarating, their adrenaline pumping. Knowing the truth and seeing those people collude to deceive Aunt Qin had been infuriating. What made it worse was their pretense of acting in Aunt Qin's best interest, making them even more repulsive. So, the sooner this was exposed, the better.","【Oh, they're holding each other, yuck~ They're kissing! Damn! They're already undressing...】","Qin Second’s family, hearing this in their minds, turned green. How shameless! Doing this in their ex-wife's family home? Even animals wouldn't behave so disgracefully!","Let's catch them in the act!","The building was quiet, with only the servants resting in the first floor's maid room. The second floor was where guests stayed.","As they climbed upstairs, Qin Second’s family led the way, all of them holding their breath silently. The others, not daring to speak, wondered what they were doing so quietly.","Could they be eavesdropping on a father-son conversation to see if Zhao Chengle had reflected on his actions?","Everyone was puzzled.","Meanwhile, Ji Fei was thinking about how to open the door to catch them in the act. Asking Fifth Aunt Qin to do it would just give the two a chance to further deceive her.","Just as she thought this, they reached the door. Fifth Aunt Qin was about to knock when voices came from inside.","\"No, Brother Zhao, this is Yu's home; we can't do this...\"","\"Yun, you've been wronged today, and I feel for you!\"","Then came sounds like someone was struggling to breathe while kissing.","Fifth Aunt Qin froze.","The others, though not hearing everything clearly, could make out male and female voices.","【Damn, are the guest room’s soundproofing this bad? This is going to be too easy... Wait, does that mean when Qin Xian and I...】","Qin Xian quickly pulled Ji Fei closer to distract her, mindful of the others present.","Qin Second’s family: ...they have never eavesdropped on anyone.","Besides, the newer guest rooms were built with excellent soundproofing, unlike here.","Ji Fei was pulled out of her thoughts. She noticed Fifth Aunt Qin's eyes were reddening.","Apparently, she understood.","The conversation inside continued.","\"When I divorce Yu, we'll have our wedding back home. I must give you the best to make up for your love.\"","\"No, Brother Zhao, being able to love each other is enough for me. I don't need those material things. As long as you keep me by your side every day.\"","\"Why, Yun, don't you want to marry me?\"","\"But if we get married, Yu will find out. I don't want her to be hurt. You know, I never wanted to steal you from her. I just couldn't control my love for you. If I could, I'd want to maintain the balance of our three-way relationship. I can't bear to see my best friend hurt, but she found out. I just hope she learns the truth as late as possible.\"","\"But, Yun, you're being wronged.\"","\"I'm not wronged. I just want you two to be okay. Rest assured, I'll stay with you but also keep in touch with Yu, comforting her. Maybe after helping her through her troubles, she'll find someone new. When she learns the truth, she won't blame us. Unless she blesses us, we'll never get married!\"","\"Yun, you're...too kind. You're going out of your way for her, but it's not your fault.\"","\"It's my fault for falling in love with my best friend's husband. This is what I deserve. I just hope someday we can all be friends again...\"","Fifth Aunt Qin couldn't take it anymore. Tears streaming down her face, her eyes reddened, she burst into the room.","The others followed closely behind.","Despite not hearing everything clearly, everyone understood—they were here to catch someone in the act.","And it seemed there was only one person who fit that description—the so-called \"best friend\" who came along under the guise of friendship.","It was the cliche of the culprit being right under your nose.","No wonder Fifth Aunt Qin hadn't noticed.","Soon, screams filled the air.","The scene was unbearable to look at.","The two on the bed weren't fully exposed, but they were already disheveled, hugging and whispering intimately—enough to make it clear what was happening.","The screaming came from Lu Yunqing; Zhao Jianghe quickly pulled the blanket to cover Lu Yunqing, who was almost exposed. Himself, looking tense, stood up, but his body betrayed him, making the situation even more awkward.","Zhao Jianghe's face was grim as he tried to lash out at Fifth Aunt Qin, \"Where's your manners? How dare you barge into someone's room!\"","Fifth Aunt Qin seemed to be in shock, unable to respond.","But the Qin family behind her erupted in anger.","\"What right do you have to talk about manners, you adulterer sneaking with your mistress in your ex-wife's family home!\" Qin Xiaoyu raged.","\"Besides, this is our house! We can go wherever we please!\" Qin Jing added.","\"Damn!\" Qin Wenqiang, who hated mistresses the most, rushed forward to pull the blanket away.","Lu Yunqing screamed.","\"Don't touch her!\" Zhao Jianghe tried to intervene but was shoved to the ground by Qin Yi and Qin Zhao.","The blanket was pulled away, leaving Lu Yunqing exposed and in disarray on the bed. She looked up, tearful and pitiful, at Fifth Aunt Qin."]},{"number":410,"title":"Chapter 410: I Don't Have a Son Like You Who Betrays His Own Kind","paragraphs":["\"Yu~\" Even the tone was full of resentment.","Fifth Aunt Qin's pupils constricted, and she rushed forward, grabbing Lu Yunqing's hair from behind and slapping her face repeatedly. Lu Yunqing screamed in pain with each slap.","Zhao Jianghe was furious and tried to rush over to stop her. He had some brute strength and managed to break through Qin Yi and Qin Zhao, but Qin Xian turned and kicked him to the ground with a single move.","\"This is my aunt and her best friend's feud. You'd better stay out of it,\" Qin Xian said coldly, looking down at him. \"After all, anyone who does something wrong will always face retribution.\"","The room was filled with the sound of slapping and heartbreaking sobs.","There were also Fifth Aunt Qin's accusatory cries.","\"I've treated you so well, even considered you like a sister. How could you do something so despicable!\"","\"You feel wronged, you've suffered, then what about me? Where did I go wrong with you?\"","\"You even tried to conspire together to deceive me, wanted to make a fool of me? Watching me pour out my heart to you, did you feel happy, did you feel smug?\"","\"You thought I could forgive you two—this shameless couple? Let me tell you, that will never happen in this lifetime!\"","If her husband's affair had already left her heartbroken and angry, then discovering that the other woman was her best friend made her furious. Double betrayal is not a simple addition but a tenfold blow.","Fifth Aunt Qin was on the verge of a breakdown.","To Fifth Aunt Qin, Zhao Jianghe's affair was betrayal, regardless of who the other woman was. They had already fought, separated, and she had even forced him to leave with nothing. Fifth Aunt Qin had no interest in finding out who the other woman was.","But now, her best friend had betrayed her, attempted to deceive her, and had been acting innocent all along. This was beyond what Fifth Aunt Qin could endure.","\"Sobbing... I'm sorry, it's all my fault. I didn't mean to. Please, don't hit me anymore, don't hit me...\"","Even while being beaten, Lu Yunqing continued to speak in fragments.","It was clear that even at this moment, she was trying to play the innocent card. Her convictions were indeed strong.","Zhao Jianghe tried several times to get up and come to Lu Yunqing's rescue, but he was always knocked back down.","\"Enough, Qin Yu! Enough! Stop hitting her! If you want to hit someone, hit me! It's not her fault, I was the one who fell for her first!\" Zhao Jianghe shouted.","[Oh boy, what a devoted lover. It was clearly Lu Yunqing who started it, with her flirtatious glances and coy behavior, that's what got Zhao Jianghe hooked in the first place.]","Fifth Aunt Qin paused for a moment upon hearing this, only to seize a bedside lamp and hurl it accurately at Zhao Jianghe, leaving him with a head full of blood.","How laughable, did he really think Fifth Aunt Qin didn't want to beat him? She just didn't have the time.","Zhao Jianghe was stunned. After the initial outburst, Fifth Aunt Qin had only slapped him a few times, never going this far.","Clearly, seeing the truth unveiled, Fifth Aunt Qin had lost her sanity.","Just then, noise came from outside the door.","It was Zhao Chengle.","Zhao Chengle had finally returned and was about to rest when he heard commotion. Curious, he approached and saw the servants peeking upstairs, along with cries and shouts. Alarmed, he rushed up.","But he was stopped at the door.","Blocking him were Qin Yan and Qin Jiaxi, unable to push their way forward.","Qin Yan said, \"Do you know who to side with once you're in? If you're not clear, you'd better not go in.\"","Qin Jiaxi didn't speak but looked at their cousin with concern.","They feared he might act impulsively and further hurt his mother's feelings.","Zhao Chengle, now fully aware that his mother had discovered the truth, turned pale and pushed his way in.","Before he could even take in the scene, Ji Fei stepped forward and blocked Zhao Chengle.","This time, Ji Fei wasn't smiling; instead, she was completely serious. \"This is your last chance. If you make a mistake, there's no going back.\"","If it weren't for Fifth Aunt Qin, Ji Fei wouldn't have bothered with Zhao Chengle. She thought he was one of those people who couldn't understand others' pain unless it happened to them.","But since her grandfather was willing to give him a choice, she would give him one.","Yet, Zhao Chengle disappointed once again.","When he saw the scene inside, he completely forgot the warnings from his relatives, charging in and seizing his mother's arm as she was about to strike, preventing Fifth Aunt Qin from hitting Lu Yunqing. He quickly helped Lu Yunqing escape her grasp.","\"Mom, what are you doing!\" Zhao Chengle was shocked. His mother, who was always dignified, was now acting like a common street fighter. Lu Yunqing's face was swollen, some parts even broken, and she was crying inconsolably. How could his mother bring herself to do this?","\"Don't you see? Don't you know what's going on?\" Fifth Aunt Qin pointed at Lu Yunqing's clothes, the bed, and the ground where Zhao Jianghe lay.","Zhao Chengle wasn't an actor; his face betrayed confusion and hesitation.","He hadn't expected these two would be so reckless, so unable to resist temptation, even in the Qin Family home... He was struggling to face the reality.","In that moment of hesitation, Fifth Aunt Qin, who was barely holding on, seemed to freeze, staring at Zhao Chengle in disbelief.","[It's over. The biggest blow has come. Sigh, Zhao Chengle really disappoints. I hope Fifth Aunt Qin can survive this.]","Fifth Aunt Qin wobbled, her tears and crushed expression completely unnoticed by Zhao Chengle, who had only focused on his father and Lu Yunqing's beaten state. But now, Zhao Chengle's reaction spoke volumes.","\"You knew... you were complicit with them in deceiving me, you always knew!\"","Hearing his mother's voice, almost drenched in blood (figuratively), Zhao Chengle's heart was thrown into chaos. \"Mom, the situation... it's not like that.\"","He suddenly felt panicked, wanting to explain but not knowing where to begin. Finally, he blurted out, \"Mom, they... they also have a hard time.\"","The Qin Family members collectively felt a rush of blood to their heads. It was as if everything they had said before was just hot air. Not only had this kid not reflected on his actions, but he hadn't changed at all!","Those who didn't know the full story up until now finally understood, and immediately started shouting.","Qin Xiaoyu pointed at Zhao Chengle and said, \"You ungrateful wretch! You're not siding with your mom but helping your adulterous dad and the mistress! Do you even know who gave birth to you?\"","Qin Jing said, \"Have your values been eaten by a dog? It really is true that raising you is even worse than raising a dog!\"","\"I completely agree with what Grandpa said. You don't deserve to be part of the Qin Family!\" Qin Wenqiang sneered.","Zhao Chengle was red-faced, unable to retort, and could only look at his mother pleadingly.","But her gaze made him quiver.","Fifth Aunt Qin's expression turned hollow, staring straight at him before stepping forward and slapping him twice without a word.","\"I don't have a son like you who betrays his own family!\""]},{"number":411,"title":"Chapter 411: You Have Already Made Your Choice","paragraphs":["Zhao Chengle had grown up for the first time being hit by his mother.","Fifth Aunt Qin might have a strong personality, but she had never laid a hand on her son before, always settling matters with verbal education.","So these two slaps caught Zhao Chengle off guard. His eyes instantly reddened, and he stared blankly at his mother, saying, “Mom, you hit me.”","Fifth Aunt Qin was done looking at him. She wasn't naive; now that she knew her son had long been aware of the truth, everything he had done before suddenly had a completely different explanation.","Even though her heart felt like it was tearing apart, she was determined to cut out the rot. She would no longer let the people who hurt her succeed.","“You three, pack your things within ten minutes and get out of the Qin Family estate. If I see any of you here after ten minutes, don’t blame me for having the bodyguards throw you out.”","“Mom!” Zhao Chengle was truly frightened. Was his mother planning to kick him out too?","“Ten minutes,” Fifth Aunt Qin said coldly. “I never go back on my word.” She then turned to Zhao Jianghe and added, “I’ll notify you tomorrow to come sign the documents. Come alone! I don’t want to see anyone else.”","Zhao Jianghe had nothing to say in response.","Lu Yunqing, sobbing, tried to say something, but Fifth Aunt Qin raised her hand and snapped, “If you say one more word to disgust me, I’ll keep hitting. Don’t make your exit any more humiliating than it has to be.”","With that, Fifth Aunt Qin turned and walked away.","Seeing his mother about to leave, Zhao Chengle rushed over, trying to grab her hand, but she dodged.","“Even if I made you unhappy, I’m your son. I didn’t make a huge mistake.”","Zhao Chengle knew his actions might upset his mother, but he never expected it to amount to being treated the same as the other two, being scolded and then exiled. He hadn’t thought it would come to this.","“Because you’re my son, your betrayal is even harder for me to forgive,” Fifth Aunt Qin said with an icy expression. “I’ve said it before, I don’t have a son like you. Do you think I’m talking in anger?”","What happened next stunned not just Zhao Chengle, but everyone else, including the people from the Qin Family and Zhao Jianghe’s entourage. No one had expected Fifth Aunt Qin to be so ruthless with Zhao Chengle.","Even Ji Fei, who had known all along what was going on, found Fifth Aunt Qin’s actions somewhat surprising. Zhao Chengle’s only apparent crime was withholding information.","But perhaps that’s what the Old Master meant: anyone with the family’s bloodline should protect their own. If someone didn’t, why keep them around?","The younger generation of the Qin Family didn’t try to dissuade Fifth Aunt Qin. In fact, they even helped block Zhao Chengle as he tried to approach her as she left.","Zhao Chengle was red-eyed with desperation. “Don’t block me. Do you all really hate seeing me happy? I need to talk to my mom and make her understand. She can’t say something like this in the heat of anger!”","Qin Xian replied coldly, “You made your choice.”","“From the moment you chose to stand against your mother and help the other woman, you no longer deserved to be her son,” Ji Fei added.","With that, everyone dispersed.","Qin Wenqiang and Qin Yi called the steward to explain the situation and asked him to supervise the three as they packed and left.","Having been with the family for a long time, the butler was furious upon hearing the details but was shocked to learn that Zhao Chengle was also being exiled. He worried that Fifth Aunt Qin might forever damage her relationship with her son in her anger.","Despite carrying out the orders, the butler decided to seek advice from the Old Master.","In the main house, where the family was supposed to be resting, the commotion had woken everyone up. Coming out to see what was happening, they approached the younger family members for an explanation.","Faced with the situation, the men were furious and wanted to beat the culprits.","The Old Master eventually came out to ask Fifth Aunt Qin about her decision. With clarity, she explained her thoughts.","Hearing that she no longer considered Zhao Chengle her son, some elders couldn’t resist offering some words of advice, given that she had only one son and he was still young and ignorant.","But the Old Master ultimately decided to let Fifth Aunt Qin handle the matter herself. After all, she was already forty, and her life should not be dictated by others.","In the end, no matter how Zhao Chengle cried and pleaded to see his mother, he was denied. Instead, the butler and the bodyguards escorted him, along with the other two, into a car.","Zhao Chengle resisted, so they tied him up, and even his luggage was thrown in, implying that there was no turning back.","The others watched the drama unfold, content in their roles as onlookers.","As the car was about to leave, Lu Yunqing, her face swollen, turned to Ji Fei, the closest one there, and said, “Can you please tell Yu that I’m sorry? We truly didn’t mean to hurt her.” Her eyes were filled with tears as she spoke.","“Enough,” Zhao Jianghe defended his lover. “She already beat you like this; that’s more than enough.”","Zhao Chengle continued to struggle, his desperate actions conveying the fear of being abandoned. Deep down, he knew that one wrong move had cost him the most important person in his life.","Ji Fei found Lu Yunqing’s last words distasteful but refrained from responding until the latter brought up “Yu.” That’s when Ji Fei couldn’t hold back anymore.","Smiling, Ji Fei commented, “I’m curious. Why were you so willing to compromise instead of trying to break up their family? Why settle for being the other woman?”","Her words sparked a discussion among the onlookers.","Eager to take advantage of the attention, Lu Yunqing excitedly replied, “Because I didn’t want to destroy their family. I wanted everyone to be happy! But I loved Zhao Jianghe too, so...”","“So, you wanted Aunt Qin to continue being the proverbial ‘old face’ holding everything together while you and Zhao Jianghe enjoy life in the spotlight,” Ji Fei cut in. “From what I hear, you couldn’t get married because you can’t have children. So, as long as you had a kind stepson like Zhao Chengle, that was enough for you. You built a good relationship with him, secure that his strict mother would keep him in line. Doing all the hard work, Aunt Qin took the blame, while you took the credit, reaping all the benefits without any effort. Enjoying the love between husband and wife that even Aunt Qin couldn’t have, all thanks to the sacrifices she made.”","Her words were like a thunderbolt, finally revealing the twisted logic behind Lu Yunqing’s actions.","Lu Yunqing, exposed beyond any excuses, realized how sinister her own intentions looked when spoken out loud. She hadn’t acted with malicious intent. She had merely filled the gaps that Yu couldn’t, ensuring a stable home for her lover. As for Zhao Chengle, every child needs a balance between strictness and leniency. If Yu played the strict role, it was only natural for her to be the kind one. How could she be vilified for trying to make things work?","Observing Lu Yunqing’s stunned expression, Ji Fei understood. Here was someone truly stupid and cruel—completely oblivious to her own evilness.","Though Ji Fei’s words also shocked Zhao Jianghe and his son, Zhao Jianghe quickly snapped back to rationalizing things under Lu Yunqing’s soft sobs.","Zhao Chengle, on the other hand, was struck dumb, seemingly realizing the weight of his actions for the first time.","“Well, at least Aunt Qin can rest now,” Ji Fei concluded. “No one will benefit from her hard work ever again.”","Qin Xian signaled, and the driver and bodyguards finally escorted the three out of the mansion."]},{"number":412,"title":"Chapter 412: I really want to share this explosive and exciting news with everyone","paragraphs":["The next morning, Ji Fei heard that Zhao Chengle had come looking for her on his own initiative. However, Fifth Aunt Qin had made it clear that she didn't want to see him, so Zhao Chengle was still waiting at the main gate, just a five-minute drive away.","In the end, only Zhao Jianghe managed to meet with Fifth Aunt Qin, signing the divorce papers and finalizing the divorce.","This time, Zhao Jianghe didn't drag things out and opted to walk away with nothing.","As he watched Fifth Aunt Qin sign without hesitation, Zhao Jianghe sighed heavily, \"It's my fault for letting you down.\"","\"I don't want to hear your voice. It makes me sick,\" Fifth Aunt Qin said coldly.","Zhao Jianghe was momentarily speechless, letting out another deep sigh, as if he were the most helpless person in the world.","\"Let's not talk about me. What about our son? You really aren't going to see him?\"","\"I don't want him anymore. Why would I go see him?\"","\"Are you serious? You're giving up on Le Le?\" Zhao Jianghe exclaimed in surprise.","Fifth Aunt Qin let out a cold snort, \"Your son is so biased towards the two of you. What use do I have for him? Take him back and let him show filial piety to the both of you.\"","Zhao Jianghe immediately retorted, \"You're too cruel! He was just unsure of what to do at the time, wanting family harmony, so he kept it a secret.\"","\"And later? He supported the two of you getting together?\" Fifth Aunt Qin sneered.","Zhao Jianghe paused, \"You... you didn't want to be with me anyway, didn't you? What was wrong with him supporting that? Could it be that you still...\"","\"What I needed was his attitude, not his betrayal. Even if I didn't want to be with you, he shouldn't have supported a third wheel who destroyed his parents' relationship. A child with such morals, I can't bear to raise him,\" Fifth Aunt Qin retorted coldly. \"Let him call Lu Yunqing 'mom' instead.\"","Seeing how resolute Fifth Aunt Qin was, Zhao Jianghe was furious. Unable to contain himself, he said, \"With a personality so stubborn, you might end up regretting it later. If the boy doesn't come back, repairing your relationship will be too late.\"","\"Once I make a decision, I never regret it. The three of you can go to hell for all I care!\" Fifth Aunt Qin declared coldly.","She then proceeded to block and delete all contact information of the three of them right in front of Zhao Jianghe.","Zhao Jianghe was so angry his nose almost twisted. Feeling that Fifth Aunt Qin had gone too far, he said with a sneer, \"Do you think I'll live miserably just because I'm walking away with nothing? Even if you've taken over the company, you'll have to sell it at some point. I'll borrow money if I have to, and I'll buy it back. I'll run it even better than before.\"","\"Oh, that's fine by me. Although I despise you, I don't despise money. If you can gather the funds, I can sell it back to you quickly,\" Fifth Aunt Qin replied matter-of-factly. She had no desire to let emotions cloud business decisions. Since she wasn't planning to return, the company was just a burden, so getting rid of it as soon as possible was the best option.","Zhao Jianghe was nearly fuming by this point. Under the watchful eyes of the Qin family, he didn't dare escalate the conflict further and could only turn and leave.","In the end, Zhao Jianghe took Zhao Chengle with him.","After all, Lu Yunqing couldn't have children, and Zhao Chengle was Zhao Jianghe's only son.","Zhao Chengle probably realized that his mother had made up her mind and that further pleading would be useless. He decided to temporarily return with his father to handle the company's affairs.","With them gone, the Qin household returned to its lively atmosphere, preparing for an upcoming celebration.","However, the grapevine never stops growing, even while eating grapes.","Although Fifth Aunt Qin didn't want to hear any news about them, Ji Fei was still curious about their fate.","While hanging out in the living room with everyone, she couldn't help but occasionally check in on them.","[Wow, Zhao Jianghe really went all out to buy back the company. He even promised to continue running it but would share more profits with his brothers. It's almost like he's working for them! No wonder they were so willing to pitch in.]","[With Fifth Aunt Qin already knowing about their relationship, the two didn't bother hiding anymore. They got their marriage certificate the next day after returning and are planning a grand wedding in just a few days. Despite plenty of gossip and criticism within their circle, they seem completely immersed in their love and don't care. Let's hope they get pelted with pigeon droppings on their wedding day.]","Qin Second's family was also distracted by the gossip, wondering why there was no news about Zhao Chengle. Ji Fei didn't disappoint and quickly brought the latest update.","[Is Zhao Chengle just trying to numb himself? He's stopped going to school and is fully focused on helping his father with the company. It's practically like he's taking over Fifth Aunt Qin's former role behind the scenes, but he's not doing a great job. The company's old guard isn't too pleased. I wonder if he can still spout the line, 'The other woman had it tough too,' haha.]","Qin Second's family joined in the laughter.","Days passed, and Ji Fei rarely indulged in such remote gossip anymore.","Just as she was about to forget about it all, Fifth Aunt Qin received a call from across the ocean one day, which was directly connected to the old mansion. After the call, Fifth Aunt Qin's expression became somewhat enigmatic.","During dinner, someone asked her about it.","Fifth Aunt Qin simply said, \"It's no longer my concern.\"","Naturally, no one pressed further.","Ji Fei sensed there was a juicy story and immediately became attentive.","Meanwhile, Qin Second's family was on high alert, wondering what new drama would unfold.","[Holy crap, holy crap... holy crap!]","Hearing the increasingly loud exclamations, Qin Second's family's hearts were in their throats. So, what exactly happened?","[It seems like there really is a higher power, a cycle of karma that can't be escaped. Justice finally caught up with them!]","Qin Second's family: So, what exactly happened?","At that moment, Fifth Aunt Qin left the dining table early.","[Ahhh, I want to share this explosive and satisfying news so badly, but how do I even bring it up?]","Qin Second's family was still waiting for Ji Fei to spill the beans.","Suddenly, Qin Xian spoke up, \"Zhao Jianghe had an accident.\"","Everyone at the table turned their heads in surprise.","Ji Fei looked at Qin Xian in astonishment. [How does my husband know?]","Qin Second's family: Wait, Ji Fei hasn't revealed anything yet.","Qin Xian calmly continued, \"We can't let anyone who wronged Fifth Aunt live too well, so I've always been keeping an eye on their situation. If they were to prosper, I would have prepared to step in, but that's no longer necessary.\"","The whole family: ...","The whole family: !!!!!","The whole family: So that's why you're the head of the family. We feel so safe following you!","Ji Fei: [Ahhhh, my husband is so handsome. This is the kind of familial loyalty I love!]","Qin Xian smirked slightly and didn't keep everyone in suspense, revealing the whole story."]},{"number":413,"title":"Chapter 413: How many children do you want in the future","paragraphs":["After they bought back the company and it resumed normal operations, Zhao Jianghe was ready to resume his business in transportation and trade once again.","Unfortunately, they encountered the same situation as last time. Ambushed by local armed forces, they were caught in an incident and lost in the dense forest.","Lu Yunqing stayed behind to prepare for the wedding, otherwise she would have accompanied Zhao Jianghe on his trip.","But, as usual, Lu Yunqing rushed to the rescue for love, disregarding rescue regulations. Fueled by her passionate spirit, she ventured into the forest as a vulnerable woman.","Ji Fei admired her for this. Despite her seeming fragility, Lu Yunqing always managed to find the way. Sometimes, Ji Fei couldn’t help but marvel at the power of true love. But then again, with the area being a chaotic border zone, a single woman’s discreet passage was less likely to be noticed, unlike a rescue team which would require numerous formalities. So, it felt like fate at play.","However, this time there was no Fifth Aunt Qin to clean up the mess. Even if they were risking their lives for their intense love, no miracles happened.","The complexity of the rescue mission kept Zhao Chengle busy and overwhelmed. When he tried to contact Fifth Aunt Qin, he found her phone unreachable.","Determined but frustrated, Zhao Chengle chose to handle the rescue on his own. Yet, the overall efficiency was nothing compared to when Fifth Aunt Qin was in charge.","Just when everyone thought the two would likely die in the forest, the rescue team finally found them. When Zhao Jianghe and Lu Yunqing were found, both were unconscious, and Zhao Jianghe’s legs were broken.","Though they were saved, as soon as Zhao Jianghe woke up, he smashed Lu Yunqing’s head in a rage, yelling at her to leave.","Zhao Jianghe believed he wouldn’t have suffered such severe injuries if not for the troublesome woman who had come looking for him. She had brought nothing useful, forgotten the way back, and had to use his supplies. This was all a repeat of the previous life, as Zhao Jianghe struggled between life and death, still moved by the experience.","But things gradually took a turn for the worse. Without Fifth Aunt Qin’s timely arrangement of the rescue team and immediate medical care, their supplies ran out. Excessive physical exhaustion followed, and he had to take care of the woman who, beyond crying and spouting romantic nonsense, only dragged him down.","Their situation accelerated their deterioration. Eventually, an accident led to him breaking his legs due to Lu Yunqing’s recklessness.","It was an almost fatal moment, a true moment of despair. He finally broke down, regretting his decisions.","By then, even if love had clouded his judgement, he should have realized that a woman rushing for love couldn’t save his life. Only the woman who silently arranged everything behind the scenes could truly save him.","With Fifth Aunt Qin, every time he faced danger, he was always rescued in time, turning misfortune into fortune. Now, without her, only a burden remained by his side, and nothing was left.","When he woke up to find himself disabled, he struggled to accept reality.","Fifth Aunt Qin had saved him in four days, while Zhao Chengle’s rescue took a full fifteen days. By then, Zhao Jianghe was haggard, mentally and physically drained, appearing to have aged ten years overnight.","Seeing Lu Yunqing cry in front of him only fueled his anger. He knew that if not for this clueless woman, who offered nothing but trouble, he might have hung on with the remaining supplies until help arrived.","But with her acting in the name of love, he had suffered tremendously.","He realized he must have gone mad to have lost someone as remarkable as Fifth Aunt Qin for the sake of such a burden.","But it was all too late.","Even if he broke things off with Lu Yunqing, Fifth Aunt Qin wouldn’t come back. No amount of regret would change that.","Similarly filled with regret was Zhao Chengle. From the moment he took over his mother’s duties, he regretted it. When he heard about his father’s accident and Lu Yunqing’s involvement, he didn’t feel the same emotion as last time. Instead, he was overcome with anger and frustration. All he could think was, “What is she messing around with in such a chaotic time?”","In that moment, his heart felt pierced.","Unable to contact his mother, he blamed her for her decision to cut ties. Yet, as he attempted to handle the situation himself, he found himself increasingly overwhelmed by how difficult his mother’s job was. He couldn’t imagine how she remained composed during the intense days. He also began to wonder what his father was doing at the time: perhaps indulging in sweet nothings with his mistress? The thought made him feel nauseous.","Thinking about it made it even harder for him to reach out to his mother. As time dragged on, he grew increasingly anxious, fearing their rescue attempts might fail.","Finally, when he was on the verge of collapsing, his father was rescued.","Seeing his father in such a miserable state, Zhao Chengle wanted to ask if he regretted it. If their mother was still there, things wouldn’t have ended this way.","His father, upon waking up, unleashed endless resentment toward Lu Yunqing. Zhao Chengle realized then that his father’s regret ran even deeper; he had truly paid a heavy price.","Now that he was disabled, the debt to the Zhao family would likely take a lifetime to pay off.","In the end, Zhao Chengle called their ancestral home, hoping to tell their mother about their fate, expecting she might curse it as karma.","Fifth Aunt Qin received the call and simply said: “I told you not to contact me again. Your affairs are none of my business.”","...","After hearing this, everyone felt some sense of closure.","Karma always catches up.","The consequences are always yours to bear.","This matter had come to a complete end in their lives. Whether Fifth Aunt Qin would reconcile with her repentant son, Zhao Chengle, was a matter of time.","Ji Fei personally thought a remarriage and a second child would be a good idea.","At night, she even discussed it with Qin Xian.","Qin Xian was flexible. He believed it was fine either way. With their younger generation around, Fifth Aunt Qin wouldn’t have to worry about aging without care. Moreover, pregnancy at an advanced age could be risky. If Fifth Aunt Qin didn’t absolutely need a spiritual anchor, not having another child might be better.","“How many children do you want in the future?” Ji Fei casually asked out of curiosity.","The question made Qin Xian freeze, and Ji Fei blushed, realizing her own impulsive curiosity.","Qin Xian sneakily glanced at Ji Fei. “You decide, you know? It’s your body being affected. A lot of suffering is yours alone to endure. I can’t replace you. So, it’s up to you. How many do you like?”","Ji Fei hadn’t really thought about it before. She had always felt that love wasn’t in the stars for her, focusing more on a fulfilling life with wealth and leisure.","Now, with love, and an upcoming wedding, she had to think about the future... definitely, children would be part of it.","After all, their family had quite a legacy to pass on.","But for now, Ji Fei was still at that childlike stage of thinking, lacking a strong maternal instinct. Upon reflection, she decided not to overthink it and take things as they came.","Qin Xian held Ji Fei close and kissed her. He had his own thoughts on the matter, but he hadn’t dared to express them.","He didn’t want children. He was afraid Ji Fei would endure pain, and that once a child was in their lives, she would inevitably spend less time with him. She would shift a lot of her affection to the child, something he wasn’t comfortable with. He never had a generous spirit and absolutely didn’t want to share Ji Fei. The option of having children felt like an unwelcome intrusion into their family.","And... he worried about being a good father. He feared he wouldn’t be able to guide a child well.","After all, he wasn’t exactly “normal” himself.","...","News soon spread that Sixth Uncle Qin was about to return."]},{"number":414,"title":"Chapter 414: Is Miss Sweetie Coming Back","paragraphs":["Sixth Uncle's family is returning home, and their beloved daughter, Qin Tiantian, has finally finished her exams.","Everyone had originally planned to go to the airport to pick them up today, but Sixth Uncle mentioned that their clothes were not seasonally appropriate and decided to make a stop to buy some before heading back to the ancestral home. Thus, there was no need for the family to accompany them. They would see everyone at the ancestral home later. The family members all have rather carefree and relaxed personalities.","Since Qin Tiantian had finished her exams, the other young people in the family pulled her into their younger generation chat group.","As soon as she joined, Qin Tiantian started sending a flurry of emojis, fully expressing her joy at being set free, like a little bird.","It seems the exams had nearly driven this eighteen-year-old girl to the brink of a breakdown. She is the youngest child in her generation, even younger than Qin Jiaxi by a year.","Due to her studies, Qin Tiantian had been extremely busy since enrolling in a women's academy, which had been largely a closed environment. As a result, she and Qin Jiaxi didn't keep in touch much, meeting only once a year.","In the past, Qin Jiaxi's happiest moments were when Qin Tiantian returned home. Qin Tiantian is a cheerful, outgoing, and lively girl, a textbook extrovert who gets along well with everyone.","Ji Fei noticed Qin Tiantian tagging her and exclaiming excitedly, \"Second Sister-in-Law, I absolutely have to see you first thing when I get back!\"","Ji Fei was puzzled: \"Huh? Why?\"","Qin Zhao chimed in mischievously: \"Is it because you want to see firsthand the incredible woman who managed to snag your dreamy older brother?\"","Qin Tiantian: \"Hehe, I already knew! I've watched all your variety shows! I'm now a member of the Fei Faction!\"","Ji Fei was so embarrassed she didn't know what to reply, so she just sent a string of ellipses.","The group in the living room burst into laughter.","She had thought that everyone would at most take a passing interest, knowing the situation. Those who didn't watch variety shows or pay attention to entertainment, like the other siblings, would know about her and Qin Zhao's past appearance on a variety show and might have seen some performance clips, but they wouldn't delve into the trending memes and hot searches.","But it was clear that Qin Tiantian was different.","\"Do you know why she's so obsessed with you?\" Qin Zhao asked with a mysterious smile.","\"Why?\" Ji Fei asked, curious.","Qin Rong burst out laughing and explained to Ji Fei: \"It's because Tiantian met Second Brother when she was little and insisted every day that she would marry him when she grew up, claiming he was her male god (ultimate crush). But as she grew up, she realized that dream was never going to come true, so she was heartbroken. My Second Brother... he's even hard to resist for his own relatives.\"","Qin Rong got a light knock on the head from Qin Xian beside her.","\"Don't tease your sister-in-law like that.\"","Everyone else couldn't stop laughing.","It was evident that the others had often heard similar stories in the past. Qin Tiantian had been a huge fan of Qin Xian.","This was the first time Ji Fei had seen the whole family so delighted by someone’s return. Qin Tiantian was truly a ray of sunshine.","As they were all enjoying the moment, a voice excitedly asked, \"Is it that Miss Tiantian is coming back?\"","The Qin family is generally kind to their household staff, so when Aunt Mao suddenly interrupted, the family members didn't mind and just smiled, replying, \"Yes.\"","\"That's wonderful, I need to prepare her favorite desserts,\" she said and quickly rushed off to get busy.","Ji Fei looked at her eldest cousin, Qin Wenqiang, with a puzzled expression.","Qin Wenqiang explained, \"Aunt Mao has been with the Qin family for a long time. When she first started, she was in charge of taking care of Sixth Uncle's family. Tiantian was often under her care, so she's very fond of her.\"","With the topic shifted, everyone continued chatting.","In the afternoon, the sound of a car was heard outside.","Everyone hurried out and soon saw a car pulling in. One of the windows was open, and a head poked out, looking around. Seeing a group of people standing there, she immediately started excitedly waving.","Her exuberant energy was like that of a little sun, instantly endearing.","As soon as the car stopped, Qin Tiantian couldn't wait to get out, rushing over. Her parents, who had also gotten out of the car, watched her with a mix of helplessness and affection, reminding her, \"Slow down.\"","Qin Tiantian dashed toward the most beautiful woman standing in the middle, next to her crush, shouting, \"Fei Jie! Oh, no, Sister-in-Law! I finally see you! I want your autograph, a photo together, I want—\"","As Qin Tiantian rushed over, Ji Fei thought she was going to hug her, but the girl seemed to have some tact, unsure if the other person would appreciate the enthusiasm. At the last second, she changed the hug into a handshake.","She held Ji Fei's hand and kept shaking it, unknowingly indulging in a bit of playful teasing that made Ji Fei unable to resist.","In the family, only Qin Jiaxi and Qin Rong were younger than her, and both were quieter, making her first encounter with such vibrant enthusiasm a unique experience.","\"Alright, alright, I'll fulfill all your requests. Nice to meet you too, Tiantian,\" Ji Fei said with a smile.","The other siblings were also very happy to see her and reminded her not to focus solely on Ji Fei and to greet everyone properly.","Qin Tiantian then went through the motions of greeting everyone in order.","But when she saw Qin Xian, she sighed, \"Oh, Second Brother is even more handsome now. It's only going to get harder for me to find a boyfriend.\"","Qin Xian remained calm and composed, but everyone else burst into laughter, teasing Qin Tiantian for comparing her future boyfriend to Qin Xian, which was just setting herself up for heartbreak. They joked that she might end up never getting married.","Just then, Sixth Uncle Qin and Sixth Aunt arrived.","Qin Tiantian quipped, \"Well, I might as well just mooch off my parents for life, sticking to them and living as a pampered princess forever.\"","Sixth Uncle Qin tapped Qin Tiantian's head. \"Now that's ambition.\"","Sixth Aunt giggled, \"Fine, we'll take care of you forever.\"","The family members all greeted the elders, creating a harmonious atmosphere, and Ji Fei confirmed that the Sixth Uncle's family was in good spirits.","This only deepened the genuine smiles on the faces of the Second Brother's family.","There were voices coming from the main building, and everyone prepared to move over together.","Suddenly, Aunt Mao rushed over, exclaiming, \"Miss Tiantian, you're back! Oh, let me see you, you've changed so much in a year! You've grown taller, and even more beautiful!\"","Truthfully, the interruption felt a bit out of place at that moment.","However, everyone was in a good mood and didn't mind.","Qin Tiantian happily greeted Aunt Mao, and Sixth Uncle and Sixth Aunt also exchanged pleasantries, though it was clear Aunt Mao was quite perfunctory towards the couple. Her affection for Tiantian, on the other hand, seemed almost too intense, with tears in her eyes. It was a bit over-the-top.","Ji Fei couldn't help but joke, \"It feels like she's treating her as her own daughter.\"","\"Maybe because Tiantian is so lovable.\"","\"After all, she's watched her grow up.\"","Apparently accustomed to such situations, the Sixth Uncle's family didn't feel awkward, though others began to feel uncomfortable and reminded Aunt Mao that the elders were waiting.","Only then did Aunt Mao come to her senses and awkwardly mentioned that she had prepared Tiantian's favorite dessert and would come find her later.","Qin Tiantian smiled and replied, \"I've also brought gifts for you and Little Yi. Is Little Yi coming today? It's been so long since I've seen her.\"","Aunt Mao's expression momentarily turned unnatural, and she gave a perfunctory smile."]},{"number":415,"title":"Chapter 415: Just away for a little while, and there's such a tragic drama","paragraphs":["After Qin Tiantian finished speaking, she stepped forward and wrapped her arm around Ji Fei, heading towards the main building.","\"Who is Little Yi?\" Ji Fei asked with curiosity.","\"Little Yi is Aunt Mao's daughter, the same age as me. We went to the same elementary school and were really good friends,\" Qin Tiantian said cheerfully, skipping along.","Ji Fei didn't give it much thought, just asking out of passing interest.","With the arrival of Uncle Qin's family, the atmosphere in the house finally felt like a proper celebration for the upcoming birthday.","Qin Tiantian was genuinely charming and lovable, even her traditionally rigid grandfather couldn't help but smile from ear to ear. She truly lived up to her title as the family's little princess.","When they returned to the youth wing in the evening, only Qin Tiantian followed along. She seemed to have an endless stream of words and boundless energy.","As soon as she appeared, Aunt Mao showed up too, immediately bringing her favorite desserts. The treats for the other young masters and ladies were much less attentive, consisting of repetitive ordinary varieties.","Naturally, no one compared themselves to Qin Tiantian.","Qin Tiantian happily went to fetch her gifts and then chatted with Aunt Mao privately at the table.","\"Where's Little Yi? Isn't she coming?\" Qin Tiantian asked, puzzled.","Aunt Mao quickly replied, \"Oh, we're just servants. How could a servant bring their family to play at their employer's home? She's not worthy.\"","Qin Tiantian immediately frowned, \"But she's my friend! What's the harm in inviting a friend over? My family is very nice, no one will care.\"","Aunt Mao's expression stiffened slightly. \"She still has work to do. She really doesn't have time to come over.\"","Qin Tiantian was shocked. \"What? Work? But according to the school system here, isn't she supposed to be in her final year of high school?\"","\"Oh, she's not ambitious. She wasn't good at studying, so she dropped out after middle school and started working,\" Aunt Mao waved her hand dismissively.","Qin Tiantian was even more astonished. She clearly remembered that Duan Yi used to love studying. She had said that since her dad and brother didn't like her, she wanted to study hard and become someone useful, so that everyone would like her.","Back then, Duan Yi was even better at studying than she was. Although Qin Tiantian went abroad during middle school, they occasionally kept in touch over the phone, and every time they talked about studying. Even though their contact eventually fizzled out, Qin Tiantian always thought Duan Yi wouldn't give up on continuing her education.","Qin Tiantian was a kind-hearted girl, so she started imagining scenarios—perhaps it was because of the patriarchal mindset, and Duan Yi's dad and brother forced her to drop out and work to support her brother. But that didn't make sense either, since Aunt Mao worked for the Qin family and earned a good salary. Supporting two kids through university should have been no problem at all.","Qin Tiantian couldn't understand, but she had her own plans. She pestered Aunt Mao until she gave her the phone, and then secretly looked up Duan Yi's current contact information.","She quickly got in touch with Duan Yi. From Duan Yi's surprise and distant tone, Qin Tiantian sensed the long absence had created some awkwardness between them. She invited Duan Yi to come over, gave her a gift, and thought that if they met, she could help Duan Yi with any difficulties she might be facing.","She had often helped Duan Yi when they were young, so she didn't think much of it. She believed that if she had the means to help a friend, she shouldn't hesitate.","Afterwards, Qin Tiantian mentioned to others that she invited Little Yi to come over. Naturally, no one had any objections, since this was Qin Tiantian's home, and she could bring whomever she wanted.","However, Qin Tiantian then suggested that they all go to the amusement park together, the youth version, which was usually frequented by Qin Weiwei and Qin Xi while the adults politely declined.","In the end, Qin Jiaxi and Qin Rong, who couldn't resist the invitations, were included in the plan.","The next morning, Ji Fei came downstairs and found two people in the living room arguing.","\"Who let you come here?\"","\"What, did I come to embarrass you? It's Qin Tiantian who invited me.\"","\"You... she was just being polite.\"","\"Does a young lady like her need to be polite with a small fry like me? I know you adore Qin Tiantian. In your eyes, she is a hundred or a thousand times better than me. You like her more than your own daughter. But, Mother, do you have to treat me like a disease carrier and keep me away? Every time she comes back, you don't even tell me. I've been saying for years that I want to see her, but you go out of your way to keep me in the dark. Is meeting her really going to bring her any harm? She's of a higher class, I'm of a lower class, so I'm not even worthy of meeting her, right?\"","Ji Fei, who was eavesdropping at the corner of the stairs, was thoroughly entertained. She had always thought this aunt was a bit strange, and now she understood—she really didn't like her own daughter. Treating the employer's daughter like a princess while despising her own daughter. Well, in some ways, it was a manifestation of a snobbery.","Ji Fei couldn't help but peek over.","She saw a girl with a fairly charming appearance, but her clothing was... truly poor, standing there with a furious expression, questioning Aunt Mao.","This made Ji Fei curious. After all, the Qin family paid their staff well. It really shouldn't be so bad that the daughter of the house looked like she came from a slum.","Aunt Mao was sweating, looking anxious. Finally, she looked at Duan Yi with a mixture of grievance and helplessness, saying, \"She's a young lady who is adored to the utmost, born with a silver spoon. You... you just can’t compare. Our families are on different levels, so you two could never be friends. I’m doing this for your own good!\"","Duan Yi, seeing Aunt Mao's expression, softened a bit at heart. \"That's my business.\"","Seeing that her daughter was determined to stay, Aunt Mao had no choice but to persuade her patiently. \"Then, after you take the gift and exchange a few words, leave. You're off today, but the house still needs cleaning, your dad and brother still need to eat, and...\"","As Aunt Mao spoke, Duan Yi's expression grew darker, almost glowering at her.","Aunt Mao's face stiffened. \"The house still relies on you. Mom... mom has no choice. There's still work here, or else I would definitely help you.\"","Duan Yi's eyes reddened with grievance. Aunt Mao, however, could only look at her with an apologetic expression, as if she herself were so innocent, so powerless.","Ji Fei had accidentally witnessed a slice of Duan Yi's life.","She was also a pitiful girl.","So that's how it is. The parents remarried each other. Aunt Mao was unmarried and pregnant at the time, and then she married a man who had a son. However, the husband turned out to be good-for-nothing, lazy, and fond of gambling, with only a silver tongue that could sweet-talk. The family's main income depended entirely on Aunt Mao, while the son brought by the man was also lazy, spending all day playing games at home, and is still mingling around in vocational school.","Duan Yi, however, is ambitious. She's always been a good student, and was originally qualified to go to high school. But at that time, just when that son caused trouble and needed to pay compensation, the family didn't have any spare money due to these two father and son. Even borrowing from other members of the Qin family, they could only help the son solve the problem, while these two father and son firmly disagreed to continue supporting Duan Yi’s education. And this muddle-headed mother surprisingly agreed.","Incredible! She's her own daughter, yet with the money she earned, she destroyed her daughter's future for the sake of the man and his son. No wonder the relationship between this mother and daughter is so strange. Listening to their conversation earlier, it seems that things aren't just like this at home...","Qin Zhao and Qin Rong, who had just returned from the main building with a group of people, heard their sleeping sister-in-law's thoughts.","What? Just gone for a moment, and already such a tragic drama?"]},{"number":416,"title":"Chapter 416: Qin Tiantian is Just Lucky to Have Been Born into a Good Family","paragraphs":["【Oh my goodness, doing all the household chores, only to be met with abuse and scolding, it’s practically like growing up in an environment of mistreatment. And this Aunt Mao would just turn a blind eye, always siding with her husband and stepson, whether openly or secretly. Afterwards, she’d tell her daughter, “I’m sorry, it’s all because your mother is useless,” urging her to endure it. Not only was she weak and incompetent, but she also used emotional manipulation and moral guilt-tripping to make Duan Yi forgive her... Duan Yi was trapped in this toxic family dynamic. Sigh~ So, Aunt Mao didn’t want Duan Yi to interact with Qin Tiantian because she genuinely believed her own daughter wasn’t worthy of someone as heavenly as Qin Tiantian? After all, judging by the family dynamics, she looked down on herself and, by extension, her own daughter.】","Although Qin Zhao and Qin Rong wanted to hear more, they had already returned with the group.","While it wasn’t common for everyone to have breakfast together, when there were many people, they’d usually eat in the dining area. If there were only a few, like when it was just Ji Fei alone, someone would bring a tray over to save her the trouble of going to the dining room.","As soon as they entered, the conversation inside naturally stopped.","“Xiao Yi, is that you?” Qin Tiantian, upon seeing Duan Yi, immediately ran over and gave her an enthusiastic hug.","However, Duan Yi was visibly stiff in response to the hug.","Aunt Mao, standing nearby, looked even more uncomfortable, even showing signs of resistance, which made Qin Zhao and Qin Rong look down on her even more.","What kind of nonsense is this? How could she be so dismissive of her own daughter?","The gossip they had just overheard, combined with Duan Yi’s shabby appearance, painted a clear picture of the kind of life she was living.","Even the families of the servants in their own household lived much better lives.","It was clear that Aunt Mao hadn’t given her daughter a single extra penny.","It was truly... hard to even know where to begin with the disdain.","Such a bizarre situation would have seemed unheard of in the past, but now, having seen so many strange human behaviors, it didn’t seem all that surprising anymore.","They exchanged a glance, not wanting to say much. After all, they couldn’t just fire Aunt Mao on a whim just because they found her behavior unpleasant. She had been serving Sixth Uncle’s family for a long time and, from the Qin Family’s perspective, she had been dutiful in her role.","If they were to fire her, it might only make Duan Yi’s situation even worse.","Qin Zhao and Qin Rong exchanged another look, then greeted Ji Fei as she came downstairs. One asked her what she wanted to eat, while the other prepared to call a servant over to help, deliberately avoiding calling Aunt Mao.","Seeing Ji Fei come down, Aunt Mao seemed uneasy, sneaking a glance as if afraid Ji Fei had overheard something.","Ji Fei shared a similar sentiment with Qin Zhao and Qin Rong. There were too many people in the world suffering from unfortunate circumstances, and she wasn’t the type to interfere in others’ fates unless they were within her own circle. For everyone else, it was simply their own destiny.","However, Ji Fei thought that if Duan Yi were to confide in Qin Tiantian, Qin Tiantian would definitely help. She was the type of person who would go all out to help others without a second thought.","After chatting for a while, Aunt Mao, seeing that nothing was amiss, left to attend to her work, as she couldn’t stay and watch them indefinitely.","Qin Tiantian took Duan Yi back to her room, gave her some gifts, and they began to catch up.","Duan Yi responded with a smile throughout the conversation.","Suddenly, Qin Tiantian asked, “Xiao Yi, I heard you’re not studying anymore. Why is that?”","Duan Yi’s expression changed slightly, and she took the opportunity to complain about her situation.","As expected, Qin Tiantian’s face fell. “That won’t do! Is there still a chance for you to go back to school? Can you resume your studies? If you need help, I can assist you.”","In truth, Duan Yi had been waiting for this exact offer. Her mother wouldn’t give her money, but Qin Tiantian would. That was why she had been so eager to see Qin Tiantian.","After all, Qin Tiantian was that kind of overly generous person.","But at this moment, Duan Yi felt deeply uncomfortable, especially when she thought about the things her mother often said.","Her mother would often praise Qin Tiantian at home, smiling as she spoke, far more than she ever praised Duan Yi.","Her mother would also frequently compare her to Qin Tiantian, saying how she fell short in so many ways, and even brought up her own life as a point of comparison. Qin Tiantian was the “perfect child” from another family, someone Duan Yi could never measure up to.","Duan Yi believed that if she had been born into the Qin Family, she would have been even more outstanding than Qin Tiantian. Qin Tiantian was just lucky with her birth.","The childhood bond they once shared had long since faded, replaced by jealousy. She couldn’t help but wonder why her mother favored Qin Tiantian so much. Why did Qin Tiantian, who already had so much, still need to take away her mother’s attention and affection? Even though she knew these grievances had nothing to do with Qin Tiantian herself, she couldn’t help but feel resentful. She even wished Qin Tiantian would disappear forever and stop intruding into their lives. That was why she had cut off contact during middle school.","Yet, when she needed help, Qin Tiantian was the only person she could think of.","Now, however, it felt as though Qin Tiantian was a princess looking down from above, offering charity, while Duan Yi was nothing more than a beggar. She looked at Qin Tiantian’s smile and found it insincere, as if Qin Tiantian was only helping her to flaunt her own kindness and superiority.","“What are you spacing out for?” Qin Tiantian waved her hand in front of Duan Yi’s face.","Duan Yi forced a smile. “I’m just really grateful. I’ll repay you someday.”","“No need, it’s nothing,” Qin Tiantian replied casually.","Duan Yi’s expression stiffened again, but she quickly changed the subject, asking about Qin Tiantian’s recent life. She learned that Qin Tiantian had become infatuated with that beautiful woman they had seen earlier, who was both her sister-in-law and an idol, a somewhat mystical figure.","Duan Yi couldn’t help but think that Qin Tiantian, even now, was still as naive as ever. But at the same time, she understood that this was the result of being showered with love and care her entire life.","In truth, Duan Yi had never expected to be as fortunate as Qin Tiantian. All she wanted was for someone in her family to care for her.","But her only family member...","Just as she was lost in thought, Aunt Mao knocked and entered the room, clearly uneasy. She brought in Qin Tiantian’s favorite cake, which elicited a delighted laugh from Qin Tiantian. For Duan Yi, however, she only brought a simple, plain dessert, as if to say that this was all the care her daughter deserved. She didn’t even bother to pretend otherwise in front of others.","“Why didn’t you make the same for both of us?” Qin Tiantian asked, puzzled.","Aunt Mao replied, “Xiao Yi likes this one.”","Qin Tiantian let out a confused “Oh,” but ultimately decided to respect her choice.","Duan Yi clenched her teeth tightly. She didn’t like this dessert at all—of course, she preferred something better. But her mother believed this was all she deserved.","Downstairs, it wasn’t that Ji Fei enjoyed prying into others’ privacy, but when she saw Aunt Mao bringing different desserts upstairs, she couldn’t help but feel something was off. Her mind wandered, and she caught a glimpse of Duan Yi’s inner thoughts.","The more she saw, the more alarmed she became.","It seemed that Duan Yi, due to her own tragic circumstances, was beginning to resent Qin Tiantian.","However, Duan Yi was rational enough not to show it.","After all, thoughts alone couldn’t condemn someone—it all depended on their actions.","So, when they decided to go to the amusement park, Ji Fei changed her mind and decided to join them."]},{"number":417,"title":"Chapter 417: It Seems Duan Yi Can No Longer Stay by Qin Tiantian's Side","paragraphs":["So, a group of girls went to the children's playground in the backyard, which had a bubble ocean, slides, and trampolines. Fortunately, none of them were overweight, so they could all play.","Originally, as the oldest among them, Ji Fei wanted to act mature and not join in the fun, but seeing how happy everyone was, she got influenced and ran in to play too.","Qin Rong secretly took many videos of her and sent them to Qin Xian.","After seeing them, Qin Xian saved each one and immediately decided to build a similar playground at his own home.","After playing for a while, Duan Yi was the first to leave, as if she had already outgrown such childlike behavior.","Outside the playground, there was a resting area where tea and snacks were served. Duan Yi sat there, waiting for everyone. Soon, Aunt Mao came over, seemingly to urge Duan Yi to leave quickly.","Ji Fei watched from the trampoline, feeling that the more Aunt Mao treated her daughter this way, the more resentment Duan Yi would harbor toward Qin Tiantian.","Clearly, the two of them had another disagreement, and in the end, Aunt Mao had no choice but to leave temporarily, not daring to escalate the situation.","When everyone came out after getting tired, Duan Yi seemed to have recovered, at least her face showed no signs of anything being wrong.","But when they sat down to eat the pastries, Ji Fei suddenly noticed Duan Yi deliberately knocking a spoon off the table with her elbow.","And she specifically aimed it toward Qin Tiantian.","\"Ah, sorry,\" Duan Yi said, but she didn’t move to pick it up.","Qin Tiantian, seeing the spoon was close to her, bent down and picked it up casually.","Ji Fei kept sneaking glances at Duan Yi and saw her flash a smug smile when Qin Tiantian bent down to pick it up.","Ji Fei was utterly confused—was that something to be proud of?","However, after picking it up, Qin Tiantian said, \"It's dirty, don’t use it. Let’s ask for another one.\"","Duan Yi’s expression instantly turned subtle.","Ji Fei, who considered herself of humble origins, couldn’t understand Duan Yi’s thought process.","Did Qin Tiantian’s single remark make Duan Yi feel humiliated?","Was her dignity made of glass?","Ji Fei found it all baffling.","But since Duan Yi didn’t do anything else, Ji Fei decided to let it go.","When everyone went back to play, Qin Tiantian wanted to go on the slide, so she climbed up to the top platform. Since it was designed for children, the railings weren’t very high.","Walking normally wouldn’t be a problem.","Unless someone gave her a push from behind.","The ground below was covered with soft padding, but if someone actually fell, they could still get hurt.","So when Qin Tiantian called for Duan Yi to join her, Duan Yi suddenly had a wicked thought as she looked at Qin Tiantian’s sweet smile.","She wouldn’t dare to do anything outright malicious, but what if she and Qin Tiantian fell together? Better yet, what if it looked like she had tried to save her...","She knew she shouldn’t take such a risk, especially since Qin Tiantian had recently promised to secretly help her with her repeat studies and even offered to fund her without telling Aunt Mao, fearing that Aunt Mao might prevent her from continuing her education due to family issues.","If Qin Tiantian got hurt and suddenly became difficult, Duan Yi might lose her future again.","But... she couldn’t help it.","The things her mother had said earlier—how she wasn’t fit to play with the young lady, how this wasn’t her fate—felt like needles piercing her heart.","She was so upset; if she didn’t vent, she felt like she would explode.","Sometimes, a moment of impulse is the birth of a devil.","Duan Yi suddenly reached out, but before she could touch Qin Tiantian, she felt someone bump into her from behind, causing her to stumble.","\"Ah!\" Duan Yi instinctively cried out.","Qin Tiantian immediately turned around and saw Duan Yi and Ji Fei colliding.","\"Oops, sorry! I thought you were moving forward. I didn’t expect you to stop,\" Ji Fei said with a smile.","Qin Tiantian quickly laughed it off, \"It’s my fault for being too slow. I’ll slide down right away, sister-in-law, don’t rush.\"","Duan Yi, meanwhile, turned pale, not daring to look Ji Fei in the eye. She thought no one could possibly know what she had been planning. Even though she had reached out, it could be explained as anything.","Duan Yi convinced herself that she had just failed and scared herself, so she let it go. She didn’t notice the icy gaze from the person behind her.","While playing, Qin Rong overheard Ji Fei’s thoughts.","*It seems Duan Yi can’t stay around Qin Tiantian anymore. I need to warn someone. As for Qin Tiantian’s promise to help...*","Honestly, Ji Fei didn’t know how to handle it. Even though they were relatives, they weren’t particularly close.","*Oh, right! I witnessed this myself. I can just tell someone. I’ll discuss it with the others later and see what they think.*","Qin Rong: ???? What’s going on? Did Duan Yi do something bad?","The half-baked information made Qin Rong start observing Duan Yi more closely.","As she watched, Qin Rong found it absurd—she even thought Duan Yi and Qin Tiantian looked somewhat alike.","Later, Qin Tiantian invited Duan Yi to stay for lunch and then afternoon tea.","She even wanted to keep her for dinner, but Aunt Mao had to hand over her shift. As soon as her shift ended, Aunt Mao immediately pulled Duan Yi away.","Duan Yi wanted to stay a little longer, but Aunt Mao’s almost stern, even fierce, glare stopped her.","Duan Yi rarely saw her mother like this and was intimidated. Though she felt wronged, she had no choice but to obey her mother, who was her only support.","Just as Aunt Mao was taking Duan Yi away, Sixth Uncle Qin and Sixth Aunt Qin returned.","The two of them managed part of Qin Corporation’s affairs, so they had been at the company earlier and hadn’t met Duan Yi.","Duan Yi had seen them when she was very young, picking up Qin Tiantian.","The image of the three of them, so close and harmonious, was like a scene from her dreams.","The way the couple doted on Qin Tiantian wasn’t just enviable to her—even their classmates were jealous. It was like she was a precious gem.","She often thought that Qin Tiantian was just lucky. If she had parents like that, even if they weren’t wealthy, she would be happy too.","But instead, she not only lacked such parents but also had a mother who seemed to despise her to the core. At this moment, she should have stepped forward to greet them, but her mother was practically trying to hide her, as if she was an embarrassment.","Yes, her clothes were shabby, but wasn’t that because of her mother? Not only did her mother support that pair of men, but she also forced Duan Yi to support them. Otherwise, she could at least dress like a normal person.","This reminded her of the scene earlier when Qin Tiantian had tried to give her some clothes before she left.","Even without her mother stopping her, she would never accept them. Even if she could never afford nice clothes, she wouldn’t take Qin Tiantian’s cast-offs.","Perhaps Aunt Mao pushed too hard, because Duan Yi suddenly lost her temper and stepped out from behind her mother, standing conspicuously at the entrance.","Aunt Mao was horrified and rushed to pull Duan Yi back.","\"What are you doing? Don’t block the way of the hosts. Come here!\" Aunt Mao desperately tried to shield Duan Yi.","By now, not only Sixth Uncle Qin and Sixth Aunt Qin, but everyone else had turned their attention to them.","Ji Fei frowned slightly.","*This Aunt Mao... Didn’t she also lack tact last time, pushing herself forward? Why is she so against her daughter doing the same? Besides, it’s only polite to greet someone you meet at the entrance. After all, Duan Yi was invited by Qin Tiantian as a guest, and they seem to know each other.*"]},{"number":418,"title":"Chapter 418: This is so unfair, it's really too unfair","paragraphs":["\"Mom, Dad, this is Duan Yi,\" Qin Tiantian cheerfully introduced as she rushed to her parents.","However, Sixth Uncle Qin and his wife were utterly devoted to their daughter. As soon as they saw her, they first showered her with concern, asking how her day had been, before shifting their attention.","\"Duan Yi, right? I remember you—Tiantian's childhood friend. My, how you've grown! You've become even more beautiful,\" Sixth Aunt said gently with a warm smile.","\"Tiantian won’t be staying here for long, so cherish the time you have together. You’re always welcome to visit our home,\" Sixth Uncle Qin added, his demeanor kind and approachable, like a friendly uncle.","Duan Yi couldn’t help but feel a pang of envy at the scene. Qin Tiantian truly had wonderful parents, and they hadn’t changed a bit over the years.","She liked Qin Tiantian’s parents—she really did. But as her own mother had said, perhaps this was just fate.","Duan Yi politely greeted them.","Meanwhile, Aunt Mao stood to the side, her face pale and beads of sweat forming on her forehead. In fact, ever since Duan Yi arrived, Aunt Mao had seemed uneasy, though Ji Fei hadn’t thought much of it at the time.","Aunt Mao kept urging Duan Yi to leave.","Thinking Aunt Mao might have some urgent matter at home, Sixth Uncle Qin and his wife didn’t prolong the conversation and offered to arrange a car to take them home.","But Aunt Mao quickly waved her hands, insisting they didn’t need it—she would take Duan Yi on her electric scooter.","Then, she hurriedly pulled Duan Yi away, as if afraid the girl would stay even a second longer.","If one were to say she was just being overly cautious, it might make sense, but her behavior toward the Qin Family, who were so kind-hearted, seemed excessive.","That evening, the young people continued their usual fun and games, dispersing when it was time.","Qin Zhao wanted to leave, but Qin Rong kept hinting for him to stay, suggesting that Ji Fei had something to say.","However, Ji Fei and Qin Xian were cozily watching videos on the couch, and even after finishing, they showed no intention of speaking up.","[Alright, time to rest. Oh, and later, I’ll share some gossip with my husband.]","Qin Rong, who had been holding back her curiosity for hours, thought to herself: So, when sister-in-law said she wanted to discuss something with everyone, she really just meant with Second Brother?! How unfair!","Qin Zhao: What are we even doing here? I’m so sleepy!","Once back in their room, Ji Fei and Qin Xian began chatting while getting ready for bed. Ji Fei brought up the strange things she had noticed that day, and due to her lack of caution, she accidentally let slip information that only a system could have uncovered. If anyone else had been listening, they could have exposed Ji Fei on the spot.","But Qin Xian pretended not to notice anything unusual, patiently waiting for his wife to finish.","\"You don’t need to worry. Sixth Uncle and Sixth Aunt may seem easygoing, but when it comes to their daughter, they’re extremely protective. Today, Tiantian wasn’t hurt, but if something had happened, they would have gone to great lengths to ensure her safety. And if it’s a long-term friendship, they’d definitely dig deep into the other person’s background.\"","Ji Fei was taken aback. \"They’re that strict?\"","\"Well, she’s their treasure,\" Qin Xian replied with a smile.","\"Then Tiantian’s future partner is in for a tough time.\"","Qin Xian raised an eyebrow.","Suddenly, Ji Fei cupped Qin Xian’s face and said with a grin, \"But it’s not easy for Tiantian to find someone, especially since her standards are set by you. Our Qin Xian is a rare gem in the world—where could she possibly find someone like you?\"","Qin Xian’s face flushed, and he turned to kiss Ji Fei’s palm. \"I’m not that great. You’re the amazing one. I’m just lucky to have found the best Ji Fei in the world.\"","Ji Fei’s cheeks turned red, and she couldn’t resist leaning in for a kiss.","After a moment of intimacy, Ji Fei couldn’t help but bring up Duan Yi’s behavior again.","Qin Xian sighed but indulged his wife.","However, he did share his own suspicions.","\"Compared to Duan Yi’s reaction, I find Aunt Mao’s behavior even more puzzling. It seems like she’s hiding something,\" Qin Xian said.","\"Really?\" Ji Fei was about to investigate but suddenly realized she didn’t even know Aunt Mao’s full name. Embarrassed, she said, \"Uh, what’s Aunt Mao’s name again?\"","One of the things Ji Fei loved most about Qin Xian was that no matter how strange her requests were, he never questioned them and immediately acted on them.","So, late at night, the butler received a message asking for Aunt Mao’s full name.","Though the butler found it odd, he complied without hesitation, as the master had spoken.","As soon as Ji Fei saw the name, she connected with her system.","[Let me see... What on earth is this self-loathing lunatic thinking? The reason she treats her daughter this way is because... AHHHHHHHH!]","Ji Fei practically leapt out of Qin Xian’s arms, visibly shaken.","Qin Xian immediately sat up and held her. \"What’s wrong? Did you... think of something?\"","But Ji Fei’s inner voice was still screaming.","[Oh no, what do I do? Is this really true? That sweet Tiantian... and that selfish, narrow-minded Duan Yi... Why?! How could something so absurd happen? Is the Qin Family about to face a crisis? Are we dealing with some kind of switched-at-birth, true and fake heiress drama? Aunt Mao is truly despicable! How am I supposed to handle this?!]","Now Qin Xian was shocked too.","He had thought the situation with his eldest sister was already bizarre enough—swapping a child out of revenge after the mistress’s son died, raising the real child with the mistress for ten years while his sister believed she had no child, only to reunite later.","But this... an eighteen-year-long switch, with the child raised and cherished as their own.","If this came to light, it was hard to imagine the devastation it would cause.","Ji Fei’s mind was still in turmoil. She almost regretted discovering this secret. As an outsider, the weight of responsibility and the consequences were overwhelming.","To be honest, everyone has their biases, and Ji Fei, who had no blood relation to the Qin Family and had only recently gotten to know Tiantian as a little sister, found it hard to accept that Tiantian wasn’t a Qin, while Duan Yi was.","But reason told her that this was deeply unfair—Duan Yi’s behavior stemmed from the life that had been stolen from her."]},{"number":419,"title":"Chapter 419: Only Hope That Kind-Hearted People Are Not Hurt Too Deeply","paragraphs":["【If she had grown up like Qin Tiantian, perhaps she would have been an adorable girl too. All of this is the result of her environment; it's not her fault.】","【She deserves fair treatment and should reclaim her true identity.】","【But a girl like Qin Tiantian... who could bear to hurt her? And that family—if Qin Tiantian were sent there, she’d be bullied to death in no time. Yet Duan Yi has endured that kind of family for so many years. How much she must have suffered! Those hardships were never meant for her.】","【When I used to read novels, I always thought those who helped the fake heiress were scum. Now, I’m terrified I might become one of those scumbags myself.】","【Ahhh, I really want to stab that old witch Aunt Mao to death right now.】","【How could someone be so malicious? Just because she realized her husband wasn’t a good man and might negatively affect her daughter’s future, and because she looked somewhat like Sixth Aunt, and the two babies were born in the same month and looked alike, she took advantage of the family’s kindness and swapped the babies when they were staying at the same hospital. From then on, the fates of the two children diverged drastically.】","【How could someone be so selfish? No wonder her behavior was so strange today!】","【So that’s what happened! Thinking about it, it’s truly despicable! Ahhhh!】","Just as Ji Fei was about to be consumed by guilt, she was suddenly pulled into Qin Xian’s embrace. “What’s wrong? What are you overthinking now?”","Ji Fei stiffened, looked up, and took a deep breath. Even though her heart was tangled in knots, even though she adored Tiantian, some truths had to come to light. Maybe the outcome would be good. She shouldn’t scare herself.","Suddenly, Qin Xian interrupted Ji Fei’s attempt to muster courage. “Are you thinking about Aunt Mao? Don’t overthink it. I’ll investigate her thoroughly tomorrow. No matter what she’s hiding, there will be traces.”","Ji Fei was stunned, as if Qin Xian had made the toughest decision for her.","He understood why Ji Fei was so unsettled—the situation was truly complicated.","If it were true, Duan Yi would be pitiable. She was the true child of the Qin family. But as for Qin Tiantian, he believed Sixth Uncle and Sixth Aunt would make the right decision.","Qin Xian also had another thought.","He found it hard to believe. According to the information Ji Fei had seen, the mothers and babies were all at Qin Corporation’s hospital. How could such a mistake have happened?","Back when his eldest sister had her incident, it was because they weren’t on their own turf.","So, he needed to investigate what had happened back then.","Of course, the most basic step was a paternity test. They should get that done first to avoid any misunderstandings.","It wasn’t that he didn’t trust Ji Fei, but her “gossip system” had its flaws. The first time, with his eldest sister’s situation, they almost missed the truth. While the gossip about someone was usually based on real events, there was also a subjective element to it. Sometimes, even if everyone told the truth, it didn’t necessarily mean the whole truth was revealed. There were often gaps and errors.","Therefore, every time Ji Fei uncovered some gossip, Qin Xian would investigate as well. Only by combining the two could they arrive at the full truth.","Ji Fei hesitated, still wanting to remind Qin Xian.","Qin Xian smiled and said, “It’s too late. Time to sleep. Overthinking will just give you a headache. Don’t worry, I’ll handle everything.”","Ji Fei thought about it and agreed. After all, she was still somewhat removed from the situation—she was a daughter-in-law, not a blood relative. It was best for Qin Xian, as the head of the family and a close cousin, to uncover and handle this matter.","If Qin Xian didn’t figure it out, she could find a way to remind him later.","【I just hope the kind-hearted aren’t hurt too deeply, and that everything can be remedied quickly.】","What Ji Fei didn’t expect was that, just as she fell asleep, an incident occurred in a residential building in Y City.","Earlier, when Duan Yi had returned home, Aunt Mao had scolded her the entire way. When they got back, Duan Yi was in a bad mood, and since she hadn’t cooked, the two men in the house were left hungry. As soon as she stepped inside, an argument broke out, and Duan Yi was beaten.","Though she tried to fight back, as a girl, she was no match in strength. In the end, she could only endure the beating. She pleaded with her mother for help, but Aunt Mao just stood to the side, turning her head away with a look of regret but making no move to intervene.","After the father and son finished beating her, Aunt Mao finally stepped forward and said, “I told you to be obedient. Look what happens when you don’t accept your fate.”","Duan Yi’s resentment reached its peak. She pushed Aunt Mao away, ran to her room, and locked herself inside.","At eighteen, she had made up her mind. She didn’t want to go to school anymore. She would shamelessly beg Qin Tiantian to help her escape this family. Only by leaving this house and her mother could she find freedom.","Duan Yi locked herself in her room all night, not even turning on the light. She only heard the sound of the door opening when the father and son returned.","The son went to bed early, but the father continued drinking and watching TV until Aunt Mao reminded him a couple of times. The man snapped, “Shut up! I’m already in a bad mood from losing money today. Tell me... what are you planning to do with that daughter of yours?”","Duan Yi, who was already standing by the door, felt her heart skip a beat. She pressed her ear against the door to eavesdrop.","Aunt Mao, seemingly afraid of being overheard, quickly pulled the man into their room.","Duan Yi’s heart raced. Something felt off. She remembered that their room had an external air conditioning platform she could climb onto to listen in.","She had done it before to avoid beatings, so she wasn’t afraid. She climbed over and listened.","Just in time, she heard her stepfather say he wanted to marry her off to an old bachelor in exchange for a bride price.","Duan Yi’s eyes turned red. She thought, surely her mother wouldn’t agree to this, right?","Sure enough, Aunt Mao objected, “That old bachelor is no good. He’s too old. If we marry her off, what will people say about us? And it’s too cruel to Duan Yi. This... this really isn’t right.”","Though it wasn’t particularly protective, Duan Yi felt a flicker of warmth in her heart.","But the next moment, she was stunned.","Her stepfather sneered, “Too cruel? Are you kidding me, you bitch? After what you did to her, you’re talking about cruelty?”","Aunt Mao was visibly shaken. “Wh-what are you talking about?”","The man chuckled darkly. “Don’t think I don’t know. Back when you just had the baby, you pretended to be sick and begged the Qin family for help. They, being kind-hearted, took you and the baby to their big hospital to take care of you. But when you came back, I noticed your attitude toward her had changed. You weren’t loving anymore; you even neglected her. When she was first born, if I said one wrong thing, you’d go crazy like a tigress. So why did you suddenly stop caring?”","Aunt Mao’s face turned pale.","Outside, clinging to the wall, Duan Yi’s expression grew increasingly grave. This was the answer she had been searching for her whole life—why her own mother didn’t love her only child.","“Then, that night when the baby almost died because of your neglect, you stayed up crying, saying sorry and that you’d do more good deeds. I thought it was strange. If it was just negligence, why were you so terrified and guilty?”","Aunt Mao was trembling now, glaring at the man, who only laughed triumphantly.","“And then, seeing how scared you were of that brat getting close to the Qin family’s daughter, and how you always sneaked to the school to watch that girl even though you said you wouldn’t pick up your own daughter... Now it all makes sense! Haha, you, this seemingly meek woman, pulled off such a huge scheme behind everyone’s back!”"]},{"number":420,"title":"Chapter 420: You Stole My Life","paragraphs":["“Ah, shut up, shut up, shut up!” Aunt Mao suddenly lunged forward, trying to cover the man’s mouth.","The man kicked her away, “What’s gotten into you?”","“You’re lying, you’re lying! My daughter is Duan Yi, not... not...” Aunt Mao snarled.","The man was also startled, “So, you still care more about your own biological daughter. Are you afraid the truth will come out? Don’t worry, I’m not that foolish. I’m quite satisfied with my life now, so I don’t plan to say anything. But if you make me unsatisfied, don’t blame me for running my mouth at the Qin Family.”","Aunt Mao went completely mad, lashing out at him with such force that she nearly knocked the man down.","Outside the window, Duan Yi, who had been secretly watching all of this, trembled uncontrollably, nearly falling from the third floor.","Her blood felt like it was flowing backward, her breath caught in her throat, and her ears rang with a deafening buzz. The truth struck her like a tidal wave, leaving her mind blank. Then came an overwhelming surge of joy, followed by rage, the two emotions intertwining and tormenting every nerve in her body.","She didn’t know what to do. The world seemed to spin around her. Watching the woman inside—who had always been too afraid to stand up to the man—finally fight back, Duan Yi could only muster a bitter, mocking smile.","Of course, she thought. A child who isn’t your own isn’t worth loving. But your own flesh and blood? Not a single word can be said against them.","“If you keep hitting me, I’ll go straight to the Qin Family and spill everything. I mean it, don’t push me!” the man roared.","Aunt Mao instantly deflated, “Shh, shh, keep it down!”","The man smirked triumphantly, “Behave yourself. I’m your husband. How dare you hit your own man? Don’t you want to live peacefully?”","In her panic, Aunt Mao quickly came up with a counter, “You... you’re my husband, so... if you dare say anything, I’ll tell everyone it was all your idea, that you forced me into it. After all, everyone knows I’ve always obeyed you at home.”","The man’s eyes widened in shock, “You...”","“So it’s you who needs to behave. If this secret gets out and I’m arrested, you’ll be the mastermind! You’re a gambler, aren’t you? Planning to use this secret to blackmail the Qin Family Eldest Miss in the future? Does that sound reasonable?” Aunt Mao laughed coldly.","The man chuckled bitterly, “You really would do anything for your daughter, wouldn’t you?”","Aunt Mao calmed down and said, “As long as you behave, I’ll keep supporting you and our son with my salary. But don’t you dare touch my daughter! As for Duan Yi... you can marry her off if you want. I won’t interfere.”","Marrying her off might be for the best, she thought. That way, she wouldn’t keep going to the Qin Family, which was too risky. Besides, the man might slip up and reveal the truth. Once she was married, everything would be settled. And in the future, when Tiantian married into a good family thanks to her status, even if the truth came out, it wouldn’t matter anymore. She could go to prison with peace of mind.","The man sneered, “You really are heartless. After raising her for so many years, I thought I was shameless enough, but you... tsk tsk tsk... you’d really do anything for your own daughter.”","Aunt Mao suddenly exploded in anger, “And whose fault is that? It’s because of you! You tricked me into thinking you were a decent man worth trusting, so I married you while I was pregnant. But all you wanted was a son, not a daughter. Don’t think I didn’t know—you and that old fool were already planning to sell my daughter. Even if I managed to protect her, you would’ve made her life a living hell. I couldn’t let my precious daughter suffer like that.”","The man laughed mockingly, “Stop shifting the blame. I didn’t do anything. If you really loved your daughter, you could’ve taken her and left. You’re just making excuses to give her a better life.”","Hearing his taunts, Aunt Mao’s eyes turned red, but she didn’t argue back.","By then, the figure on the air conditioner outside had disappeared.","Duan Yi didn’t know how she made it back to her room. She had relied on sheer willpower to suppress her emotions, locking them away like a volcano waiting to erupt. She knew now wasn’t the time to explode. If she did, she might never reclaim her life.","She had to go there... to the Qin Family... to take back everything that was rightfully hers!","Yes, it was hers. All the beauty, all the privilege—it was hers. She shouldn’t have to envy anyone. She should be the one others envied!","Clenching her teeth and gripping herself tightly, she waited until the commotion next door had died down and everyone had gone to sleep. Then, in the early hours of the morning, she quietly got up, still in the disheveled state she’d been in after the beating, and slipped out of the house.","Using all the money she had, she took a taxi to the Qin Family estate.","The moment she stepped out of the car, she could no longer hold back her tears.","At two in the morning, the Qin Family butler was awakened by the gatekeeper, who reported that a girl was crying and demanding to see Miss Qin Tiantian.","After learning the girl’s identity, the butler frowned. It was too late to disturb the family, and he knew the girl was Aunt Mao’s daughter. He was about to bring her inside first when Qin Tiantian, holding her phone, emerged from the new building.","Seeing the butler, she said sleepily, “Xiao Yi asked me to come get her. She said something happened and needs my help.”","The butler had no choice but to accompany the young lady as the car brought Duan Yi inside.","When the car arrived and the door opened, Duan Yi practically leaped out, rushing straight toward Qin Tiantian.","Her aggressive stance made the butler instinctively step in front of Qin Tiantian to shield her.","Qin Tiantian, now wide awake, asked in alarm, “What’s wrong, Xiao Yi?”","Duan Yi stared at Qin Tiantian, her eyes wide. This was a girl who had been showered with love and wealth from head to toe, a stark contrast to Duan Yi’s own disheveled appearance.","Duan Yi forced a bitter smile, her expression twisting into something fierce and menacing.","“Qin Tiantian, I hate you!”","The butler’s face changed, and Qin Tiantian was completely stunned.","Duan Yi spat out each word like a knife, shouting, “Qin Tiantian, you stole my life! You and your shameless mother stole my life! I am the Qin Family Eldest Miss! I am the daughter of Sixth Master Qin and Madame! You’re just the daughter of a servant! You stole my life! You don’t belong to the Qin Family! You stole my life!”"]},{"number":421,"title":"Chapter 421: We Conduct Paternity Testing","paragraphs":["Duan Yi kept repeating, \"You stole my life,\" venting her bitterness, as if it were a desperate cry for salvation amidst despair.","Yes, that wretched life, those wretched family members—how could they be hers? Finally, she could leave without guilt, escaping that demon of a mother.","Her outburst not only stunned the person in front of her but also caused the quiet old mansion to light up one by one.","After all, in the dead of night, the slightest disturbance could wake anyone.","Sixth Uncle Qin and Sixth Aunt Qin were the first to rush out, having heard their precious daughter's name.","When they arrived, they saw their daughter, Qin Tiantian, pale with fright, and immediately hugged and comforted her.","Seeing this, Duan Yi couldn't hold back her tears. She wanted to step forward and push Qin Tiantian away but was stopped by the butler, who frowned in disbelief, thinking the young girl must be delusional, dreaming of becoming the young mistress.","\"Mom, Dad, look at me. I am your daughter. Mao Jie swapped the babies. Qin Tiantian is Mao Jie's daughter!\"","This time, she said it directly in front of Sixth Uncle Qin and Sixth Aunt Qin, leaving them both stunned.","\"What nonsense are you spouting?\" Sixth Uncle Qin barked sharply.","Sixth Aunt Qin, though silent, held Qin Tiantian tightly, glaring at Duan Yi with a protective ferocity.","Duan Yi cried even harder, as if she were the one intruding and breaking up this family.","\"No, you have to believe me. I overheard the truth tonight. Back when you were all in the hospital together, she swapped the babies so her daughter could live a privileged life. Think about it—hasn't Mao Jie always treated Qin Tiantian better than me? If I were her biological daughter, why would she do that?\"","Her words made the sharp-eyed Sixth Uncle Qin's eyes flicker, and his heart skipped a beat.","Yet, he instinctively resisted the intruder.","\"That doesn't prove anything...\"","\"A DNA test! Let's do a DNA test. I heard their scheme with my own ears. If it's all a lie, I'll accept my fate. But what if it's true? Are you really going to keep the daughter of a thief as your own and drive away your flesh and blood? Think about it—if this is true, then my life... my life has been completely ruined by her mother! Do you know what kind of life I've been living in that family?\"","Duan Yi pushed back her hair and rolled up her sleeves and pant legs.","By now, many people had gathered in the courtyard.","Including Ji Fei and Qin Xian.","Ji Fei stared in shock at the scene. She had only learned the secret a few hours ago, and now it was out in the open. She had thought that if Qin Xian investigated and found something, they could quietly confirm it with a DNA test before revealing anything. After all, she didn't dare take such a risk!","She knew everything Duan Yi said was true, but...","While it saved her and Qin Xian from further hesitation, the impact of this revelation...","Ji Fei looked at Qin Tiantian, who was now pale and visibly shaken, already beginning to doubt herself.","Sixth Uncle Qin and Sixth Aunt Qin's expressions were indescribable, with Sixth Aunt trembling uncontrollably.","As for Duan Yi, she was pitiful. The scars on her body were clearly recent, meaning she had suffered domestic abuse shortly after leaving the Qin family. Moreover, there were older scars, evidence of past abuse. The sight left Ji Fei breathless.","If this was truly a case of swapped lives, then Duan Yi's life had been a living nightmare.","\"For years, they abused me, treated me horribly, and even refused to let me go to school. In the end, I even had to ask Qin Tiantian for help. Now, looking back, it's all so ridiculous.\"","Qin Tiantian stiffened under Duan Yi's gaze, tears streaming down her face. She shook her head instinctively, unable to accept that her beloved parents might not be hers after all.","Duan Yi stared stubbornly at Sixth Uncle Qin and Sixth Aunt Qin. \"Mao Jie's husband even tried to sell me off to an old bachelor for a dowry. He knew about the baby swap, so she agreed to it. If I were Mao Jie's biological daughter, would she be so cruel, so heartless? It's precisely because I'm your daughter that she treated me so viciously. If it were Qin Tiantian, her own flesh and blood, she would never have been so ruthless!\"","Duan Yi cried out, \"I beg you, believe me. You're my real parents! How can you not believe me? A DNA test—take me for a DNA test right now, and you'll see I'm the real one. She's the fake, the daughter of a servant, the beneficiary of Mao Jie's scheme!\"","As Duan Yi spoke, she stepped closer, causing Qin Tiantian to shrink back in fear.","Sixth Uncle Qin immediately barked, \"Enough!\"","Duan Yi looked up sharply, and Sixth Uncle Qin's harsh tone faltered. If what she said was true, then the person before him might indeed be his biological daughter.","But how could their beloved Tiantian not be their own? The natural bond between parents and children—how could it be wrong?","\"Honey, it's not true, right? Tiantian is our daughter!\" The gentle Sixth Aunt was on the verge of tears.","\"Mom...\" Duan Yi called out angrily.","Sixth Aunt recoiled as if startled. \"Don't call me that!\" But seeing Duan Yi's pitiful, aggrieved expression, she couldn't bring herself to be harsh. \"It's not proven yet...\"","Duan Yi glared hatefully at Qin Tiantian, feeling that her parents' rejection was all Qin Tiantian's fault.","Qin Tiantian, meanwhile, remained speechless.","The relatives around them began to murmur, unable to accept the possibility that Qin Tiantian wasn't truly one of them. But Duan Yi's insistence on a DNA test suggested she had indeed overheard Mao Jie's confession.","At that moment, Qin Xian stepped forward. \"It's too late to continue this now. Sixth Uncle, arrange for Duan Yi to stay here tonight. Tomorrow, we'll do the DNA test. We'll discuss everything after the results come out.\"","Sixth Uncle Qin looked at Qin Xian, who added, \"Sixth Uncle, you know you have to do this.\"","Sixth Uncle Qin felt a pang of pain but didn't deny it. Torn between emotion and reason, the situation was truly agonizing.","Sixth Aunt clung tightly to Qin Tiantian, as if afraid her precious daughter would be taken away. \"Tiantian, sleep with Mom tonight!\"","Qin Tiantian was stunned. She looked at her parents, then at Duan Yi, whose eyes were filled with hatred that seemed almost tangible.","\"I... I want to be alone. Mom, Dad, I need some time by myself,\" Qin Tiantian forced a smile.","\"Then Mom will take you back,\" Sixth Aunt said immediately. She felt that Tiantian was her flesh and blood. She couldn't accept this, truly couldn't. All she wanted now was to escape from it all.","Sixth Aunt ignored Duan Yi, and though Sixth Uncle Qin felt a pang of guilt, he couldn't bring himself to suddenly show concern for a stranger. He instructed the butler to make arrangements.","As for Duan Yi, she stood alone, biting her lip and crying. Many couldn't help but feel heartbroken. If Duan Yi really was the Qin family's child, then this was truly a tragedy."]},{"number":422,"title":"Chapter 422: I Also Want to Know the Truth","paragraphs":["After returning, Ji Fei was in a low mood, and everyone else was quiet, not daring to speak.","However, as they looked at Qin Tiantian, who was at the front, they couldn't help but feel uneasy.","\"Tiantian, don't overthink it. It's not certain yet,\" Qin Wenqiang couldn't help but comfort Qin Tiantian.","Qin Tiantian forced a smile and said, \"I've read novels like this before. It's usually like this. I always thought Aunt Mao's attitude toward me was strange, but now... is this the reason?\"","As she spoke, Qin Tiantian burst into tears.","Everyone quickly stepped forward to comfort her. Qin Jiaxi even hugged Qin Tiantian tightly.","\"I can't bear it. I can't bear to leave my parents. I can't bear to leave everyone. I'm not a child of the Qin Family, am I?\"","\"It's not certain,\" Qin Yi also anxiously reassured her.","Qin Xiaoyu and Qin Jing also moved closer, but Qin Second's family didn't step forward, as they were too conflicted inside.","While others might wonder if Duan Yi was the problem or if it was just Aunt Mao's delusion, Qin Second's family wouldn't entertain such thoughts because they had already heard the truth from Ji Fei's thoughts. At least, what Duan Yi said was true, so they were less hopeful than the others.","If it were true, Qin Tiantian would be pitiable, but wouldn't Duan Yi be even more so?","Sigh, when such things happen to others, it's just gossip, but when it happens to oneself, it's pure torment.","Seeing Qin Tiantian cry so bitterly, Ji Fei tugged at Qin Xian's sleeve.","Qin Xian said, \"Actually, there's no need to be so upset.\"","The others immediately looked over, their expressions showing dissatisfaction. How could they not be upset when something like this had happened?","\"In the worst-case scenario, Tiantian isn't a child of the Qin Family, but she has been raised by the Qin Family for eighteen years. Would the Qin Family mind having one more daughter? Besides, Sixth Uncle and Sixth Aunt wouldn't let Tiantian return to such a family. If the child-swapping incident is indeed true, Aunt Mao will surely go to jail, and the other two have no blood relation. So, the most likely outcome is that both will be considered daughters of the Qin Family.\"","Hearing Qin Xian's analysis, everyone felt it made sense.","At the very least, Qin Tiantian could maintain her current life regardless of the circumstances.","But thinking this way... is it fair to Duan Yi?","No one spoke up, but Qin Tiantian herself was conflicted. \"Is this fair to Xiao Yi? If Aunt Mao really swapped our lives, then it's my fault that she lived those eighteen years. If we swap back, I'll still be here, and she'll suffer. I will too... wuwuwu.\"","Everyone sighed. What could they do?","Would it only be fair if Qin Tiantian returned to Aunt Mao's side and lived Duan Yi's life?","It must be said, that night, no one could sleep, as such a decision truly tested one's values, rationality, and morality. No one is perfect, and everyone could only follow their hearts.","Sixth Uncle and Sixth Aunt discussed it all night, and their decision aligned with Qin Xian's thoughts. If it were true, they couldn't abandon the daughter they had raised for eighteen years, and as for Duan Yi... they would do their best to fulfill their parental responsibilities.","The next morning, the Old Master asked during breakfast what had happened the previous night. Not wanting to trouble him, everyone said they would tell him once the matter was clarified.","However, the atmosphere in the family remained tense.","In the morning, the personnel and equipment responsible for the identification arrived at the Qin Family. Qin Xian had been thorough in his preparations, even arranging for people to track down the hospital staff from back then.","Of course, he also sent people to bring Aunt Mao and her husband over.","When the black-clad bodyguards appeared at the doorstep, Aunt Mao, who had noticed Duan Yi's disappearance, sensed something was wrong.","Upon seeing Duan Yi at the Qin Family, meeting her hateful gaze, and witnessing the sorrowful expressions of Sixth Uncle Qin and his family, Aunt Mao's mind went blank.","Aunt Mao quickly forced a smile. \"Xiao Yi, what are you doing here? I've been looking for you everywhere. Did you come to trouble the Qin Family? Come, let's go home with Mom!\"","\"Mom? How dare you say that! Are you really my mom? How could you be so vicious and shameless!\" Duan Yi lashed out.","Aunt Mao's face changed instantly. \"What are you doing here?\"","Aunt Mao immediately began shouting uncontrollably. \"Did you come here to spout nonsense? Don't listen to her! She's delusional, there's something wrong with her mind.\"","Duan Yi gritted her teeth in anger. \"I heard everything you said last night. I know now. I'm the Qin Family's daughter, and Qin Tiantian is your daughter. It's useless for you to say anything now. We'll soon have the paternity test. You swapped us, and the truth will come out. You wanted your daughter to live a good life, but you're dreaming!\"","Aunt Mao ignored Duan Yi and instead turned to Sixth Uncle Qin. \"Sixth Master, don't listen to her nonsense. She's always been a liar, with terrible character. She's always dreaming of being a princess. She's just jealous of Tiantian's good life. Don't pay attention to her. Let me take her away. Don't believe her lies. How could Miss Tiantian be my child?\"","Sixth Uncle Qin and Sixth Aunt's faces turned extremely grim. If Duan Yi were truly their swapped daughter, then Aunt Mao's words were utterly heartless. If she were their daughter, what kind of life had she been forced to endure?","They didn't dare to think too deeply and could only try to remain calm, wanting to settle the matter once and for all.","\"No need to say more. Everything has been arranged. Let's proceed with the test.\"","At this, Aunt Mao became frantic and started cursing. \"Are you all insane? You're going to doubt your own daughter's lineage based on the words of a crazy girl? You're not afraid of hurting the child's feelings?\"","Everyone was shocked and angered by her words. If she hadn't been so biased and gone too far, no one would have found her behavior strange or raised these questions. How could she now accuse them of being rash?","\"It's just a paternity test. Why are you so anxious? Or do you have something to hide?\" Duan Yi retorted fiercely.","\"Shut up! Who do you think you are? This is your fate. You have no right to steal someone else's life!\"","Tears instantly filled Duan Yi's eyes. After all, this was the person she had genuinely regarded as her mother for eighteen years. Being spoken to like this was deeply hurtful.","\"Is this my fate, or did you steal my fate? I understand now. You truly love your daughter, but unfortunately, I'm not her. So, I don't deserve even a bit of your love, right? Since you're so heartless to me, why should I let you have your way? I will reclaim our true identities and ensure your daughter can only be the child of a wretched person like you!\"","Aunt Mao was so furious she wanted to lunge at Duan Yi but was stopped by the bodyguards.","\"Sixth Master, Madam, you can't do this! You can't treat Miss Tiantian like this!\" Aunt Mao, seeing that her efforts were futile, began to cry.","Suddenly, Qin Tiantian spoke up. \"I also want to know the truth. I want to know if I've climbed over someone else to steal their life. If that's the case, I don't deserve what I have.\""]},{"number":423,"title":"Chapter 423: It's You Who Refuse to Acknowledge Me That's Why You're Acting and Providing False Testimony to Deceive Me","paragraphs":["Qin Tiantian thought about it all night and still felt that if it were true, she would truly be too ashamed to face Duan Yi. Her upbringing would never allow her to do something as deceitful as stealing someone else's place.","If... if her parents really did as her second brother suggested, she would move out and try to cut ties with them. Otherwise, she would feel forever indebted to Duan Yi.","Thinking this, Qin Tiantian resolutely said to Duan Yi, \"Let's go.\"","Duan Yi gave Qin Tiantian a deep look, then turned and followed her.","Sixth Uncle Qin and Sixth Aunt Qin's gazes remained fixed on Qin Tiantian.","Duan Yi naturally noticed this. She was jealous and couldn't hold back, snapping at Qin Tiantian, \"When the truth comes out, you must repay everything you owe me!\"","Qin Tiantian pursed her lips, trying to control her emotions and not let herself cry.","\"Miss Tiantian, no, don't cooperate with her, don't...\" Aunt Mao cried, her eyes filled with heartache as she watched the two walk away. She completely disregarded her nominal daughter.","Seeing the medical staff still coming for her, she struggled desperately, her actions only confirming something, making everyone's hearts race.","Finally, the medical staff forcibly took the necessary tissue samples for the DNA test.","Since Sixth Uncle Qin and Sixth Aunt Qin's samples were already stored, they didn't need to make another trip.","Watching the medical staff leave, Sixth Aunt Qin could no longer control herself. She lost her usual gentle demeanor and lunged at Aunt Mao like a madwoman, grabbing her collar and shouting, \"Tell me, did you really switch the children? Speak! Speak!\"","Aunt Mao was dazed for a moment, then suddenly pushed Sixth Aunt Qin away. \"Why did you bring Tiantian back? Such a good child, such a good child! Why are you chasing the truth? You raised her for eighteen years—don't you have any feelings for her? Why are you being so cruel!\"","Her words indirectly confirmed something.","\"So... so Tiantian really isn't...\" Sixth Aunt Qin staggered backward, and Sixth Uncle Qin quickly caught her. He glared at Aunt Mao and said, \"What did we ever do to wrong you that you would be so cruel? Where is your conscience? Did a dog eat it? So when you came to us for help back then, you were planning to deceive us? You used our kindness to switch the children. How could you...\"","Sixth Uncle Qin truly wished he could tear the old woman apart. Why did such a person exist? They had only ever been kind—what had they done to deserve this?","Aunt Mao wept and said, \"I had no choice. I just wanted my daughter to have a good life. I had no choice, it was all... all...\"","She habitually looked for someone to blame, but her husband was already terrified. \"It's not my fault! I only found out later. It was all this crazy woman's idea. She treated her daughter like her life, thinking her daughter deserved a good life, so she targeted you long ago. She served in households like yours every day—how could she keep a normal mind? She was just insane.\"","The two started arguing in front of the Qin family.","But the Qin family wasn't foolish and wouldn't be swayed by Aunt Mao's excuses.","Sixth Uncle Qin and Sixth Aunt Qin finally couldn't hold back and started beating Aunt Mao.","After all, today's tragedy was all her doing—her selfishness and greed had ruined the lives of two innocent girls and devastated the Qin family.","When Qin Tiantian and Duan Yi came out, they saw Aunt Mao being beaten. Both were stunned. Although the results weren't out yet, the fact that they were already beating her meant Aunt Mao might have confessed. Qin Tiantian's face went blank, while Duan Yi's face lit up with joy.","Noticing their presence, Sixth Uncle Qin and Sixth Aunt Qin stopped. Aunt Mao, bruised and battered, looked at Qin Tiantian and said, \"Tiantian, Mom is sorry, so sorry... I was useless. I couldn't protect your life. I was useless.\"","Qin Tiantian's face was pale, and Sixth Aunt Qin looked like she was about to lose her mind. That was her precious daughter, after all.","Duan Yi stared straight at Aunt Mao. She finally saw this woman's maternal side, but it wasn't directed at her. \"Mao Jie, shouldn't you be apologizing to me?\"","Duan Yi rushed forward and grabbed Aunt Mao's collar. \"Eighteen years! I was your daughter for eighteen years! If you had given me even a tenth of the love you gave Tiantian, we could have continued as mother and daughter! You stole my life but refused to give me even a shred of compensation. You let me be beaten and bullied by them, while your real daughter lived a good life. Do you really have no conscience? Won't you make up for the sins you committed?\"","Aunt Mao didn't want to face Duan Yi and tried desperately to avoid her, looking at Qin Tiantian instead. Seeing her like this, Duan Yi really wanted to laugh.","She didn't know if this counted as great maternal love—plotting so much for her child, willing to bear all the sins herself.","If only she had taken Duan Yi away and been a good mother to her, Duan Yi wouldn't hate everyone so much now that she knew the truth.","Duan Yi let go of Aunt Mao and turned to Sixth Uncle Qin and Sixth Aunt Qin. \"You know the truth now. You know I'm your daughter. Don't you have anything to say to me?\"","Sixth Uncle Qin and Sixth Aunt Qin were still in a daze, on the verge of collapse.","At this point, Qin's Father, the former head of the family, stepped forward. \"The Qin family's child must return. You can rest assured about that. As for you, do you have any demands?\"","Qin's Father could tell the girl had something to say.","Duan Yi looked at Sixth Uncle Qin and Sixth Aunt Qin with resentment, then turned to Qin's Father and said, \"I want Mao Jie to go to prison! I want her to pay for what she did!\"","Aunt Mao looked at Duan Yi in disbelief.","Ji Fei, who had been silently watching, almost laughed at Aunt Mao's expression. [Why is she surprised? Did she think Duan Yi wouldn't retaliate? How dare she be surprised!]","\"That's a given. Anyone who dares to do such a thing to the Qin family will face the consequences,\" Qin's Father said.","Duan Yi avoided Aunt Mao's gaze, her eyes filled with resentment and pain. Then she suddenly pointed at Qin Tiantian and said, \"The Qin family—either I stay, or she does!\"","\"No! That's impossible! Absolutely not!\" Sixth Aunt Qin was the first to object, breaking down in tears.","But the more she reacted like this, the more Duan Yi hated her. Why? Why... Just as her anger reached its peak, a staff member rushed out.","\"Based on the available data and DNA results, Mao Jie is confirmed as Duan Yi's biological mother!\"","The room fell silent, so quiet you could hear a pin drop.","Another staff member ran out.","\"Based on the available data and DNA results, Mao Jie is excluded as Qin Tiantian's biological mother!\"","The room remained eerily silent.","Finally, when two more staff members came out and confirmed that Qin Tiantian was indeed the child of Sixth Uncle Qin and Sixth Aunt Qin, and that Mao Jie was not, someone finally spoke.","\"No! This can't be! It's you... you don't want to acknowledge me! That's why you're putting on this act and faking the evidence!\" Duan Yi suddenly screamed."]},{"number":424,"title":"Chapter 424: The Truth Brought by the Old Nurse","paragraphs":["Not only Duan Yi, but everyone else was also unable to hold on.","After all, Aunt Mao had already admitted her guilt, so how could there be a mistake?","Sixth Uncle Qin and Sixth Aunt exchanged glances, both seemingly suspecting if the other had intervened.","Qin Tiantian and Aunt Mao were stunned, looking around in confusion.","[What’s going on? Is this a misunderstanding? Or did Sixth Uncle and Sixth Aunt really...] Ji Fei was completely bewildered, as her Gossip System had always shown her the truth.","At this moment, Qin Xian spoke up: \"The staff conducting the tests are all professionals, and the equipment is flawless. They supervise each other, and there’s surveillance. Every sample has been cross-checked, so there’s no room for error. If you don’t believe it, you can take the samples to any organization you trust for verification.\"","His words were like a conclusive verdict, a reassurance to everyone in the Qin family.","\"So, Tiantian is our child,\" Sixth Aunt said in shock, looking at Qin Xian.","Qin Xian nodded. \"I guarantee it on the Qin family’s reputation.\"","Sixth Aunt immediately rushed over and hugged Qin Tiantian, breaking down in tears. Sixth Uncle Qin’s eyes also turned red as he wiped away his tears.","\"No, no...\" Duan Yi still refused to believe it. \"You’re lying. You’ve all conspired against me because you don’t want me...\"","\"No, this can’t be!\" Surprisingly, it was Aunt Mao who shouted even louder than Duan Yi. \"I did the swap myself. I did it myself. How could there be a mistake?\"","Suddenly, something flashed through Ji Fei’s mind. [Just because it’s a fact doesn’t mean it’s the whole truth. So Aunt Mao did switch the babies, but something else must have happened afterward.]","Sixth Uncle and Sixth Aunt were now holding Qin Tiantian protectively, glaring at Aunt Mao.","Aunt Mao struggled desperately. \"No, this isn’t right. Qin Tiantian is my child. Duan Yi is yours. How could I have made a mistake?\"","Just then, a large vehicle arrived with a group of people.","They were the medical staff from back then, many of whom had already retired. But Qin Xian had arranged for them all to be brought back within a single morning.","Qin Xian looked at the hysterical Aunt Mao and the distrustful Duan Yi and said, \"Let’s ask them, then.\"","As they questioned each person one by one, the truth of what happened back then quickly came to light.","The Old Nurse, who had been in charge of the nursery at the time, recalled that the two babies had looked very similar. But having handled so many babies, she could easily tell the difference.","One day during her rounds, she confirmed the two babies: Qin Tiantian was Baby One, and Duan Yi was Baby Two. They were sleeping soundly in adjacent cribs, each covered with a different blanket.","But when she came back the next day for her rounds, she found Qin Tiantian in Baby Two’s crib and Duan Yi in Baby One’s, each covered with the other’s blanket. She assumed that a young nurse under her had carelessly swapped their positions, so she simply switched them back.","At the time, both new mothers were in poor health and only glanced at their babies briefly.","So when Aunt Mao saw the baby covered with the correct blanket, she didn’t look further, too guilty to pay close attention. She completely missed that her baby had been switched back.","Babies change so quickly that within a few days, it became impossible to tell them apart. In the end, Aunt Mao left with the baby she thought was the Qin family’s daughter.","Meanwhile, Sixth Uncle Qin and Sixth Aunt had been raising their own biological daughter all along.","The Old Nurse’s recollection, combined with the DNA test results, brought the whole truth to light.","Ji Fei also confirmed through her Gossip System that the Old Nurse’s memory was accurate. It turned out there really had been a twist that completely changed the truth. It was enough to give her a scare.","The Qin family collectively breathed a sigh of relief, feeling as though they had narrowly escaped a devastating tragedy. They had almost been torn apart by the pain of losing their own flesh and blood.","Sixth Uncle Qin and Sixth Aunt immediately took Qin Tiantian to bow and thank the Old Nurse. To them, her simple act of responsibility was akin to a second chance at life.","The Old Nurse waved her hands in embarrassment, just relieved that they weren’t blaming her. After hearing the full story, she was also deeply shaken.","\"So... I’m really my parents’ daughter?\" Qin Tiantian was still in a daze, but her parents hugged and kissed her cheeks.","\"Tiantian will always be our precious daughter.\"","\"Yes, always!\"","Qin Tiantian burst into tears. Though she had tried to act strong, she had been raised as a pampered little princess and couldn’t handle such a heavy blow.","This adorable little princess... If it hadn’t been for the Old Nurse’s experience, they might never have realized the truth. It was unbearable to imagine how their Tiantian might have suffered under Aunt Mao’s neglect. They only had to look at Duan Yi to understand the heartbreak.","Though Duan Yi was truly pitiable, she had nothing to do with their family, so they wouldn’t waste their sympathy on her.","Sixth Uncle Qin and Sixth Aunt turned their furious gazes toward Aunt Mao, who had nearly ruined their daughter’s life.","\"Evil deeds bring evil consequences!\"","\"Getting your own daughter as punishment—it serves you right!\"","Aunt Mao was completely stunned. Only when she heard these words did she snap out of it. Unable to face the truth, she lunged at the Old Nurse. \"You’re lying, aren’t you? You’re lying!\"","But she was stopped by the bodyguards.","The Old Nurse looked at her with disgust. \"I remember you. The Qin family was kind enough to give you the same level of care as Sixth Madam. But you, with your venomous heart, tried to steal someone else’s daughter’s life. Truly... Heaven has eyes!\"","Aunt Mao shook her head frantically. \"No, you’re all just trying to cover this up. You’ve fabricated this witness and evidence!\"","These were the same words Duan Yi had been saying, and now Aunt Mao was repeating them.","One couldn’t accept that her dream had shattered, revealing a cruel truth. The other refused to admit that her scheming had backfired, and the daughter she had cherished had been treated as nothing more than a servant.","They couldn’t face each other, and they couldn’t face themselves.","Qin Xian said, \"I told you, you can take the samples and have them tested wherever you want, even abroad if you wish.\"","His words made both women falter.","Finally, the Stepfather couldn’t hold back anymore. \"Look, they’ve made it clear that they’re not afraid of any investigation. This is the truth. So can you let me go now? Since there was no swap, there’s no crime. Even if you want revenge, don’t keep holding me here. I’m really innocent.\"","Aunt Mao suddenly turned to look at him, and in the next moment, she lunged at him, biting his neck with all her might. A bloodcurdling scream echoed through the air.","By the time Aunt Mao was pulled away, the Stepfather’s neck was covered in blood. If it hadn’t been for the medical staff present, the Qin family might have had a death on their hands, which would have been terribly unlucky.","\"It’s your fault! It’s all your fault! You’re the one who put the idea of swapping the babies in my head. You... you’re the one who abused and bullied my daughter, treating her like a slave! It’s you...\" Aunt Mao screamed, finally facing the truth and realizing that Duan Yi was her biological daughter.","But in the next moment, Duan Yi pounced on Aunt Mao, choking her neck with all her might, her expression filled with murderous rage."]},{"number":425,"title":"Chapter 425: Every Minute and Second of Aunt Mao's Future Will Be Torture","paragraphs":["Duan Yi felt that her entire life was utterly ridiculous, and all of it was thanks to her—this woman who believed she loved her biological daughter more than anything, this woman who thought she would sacrifice everything for her daughter’s happiness.","Duan Yi suddenly wanted to laugh. She admitted that all of this was retribution, the retribution for Aunt Mao’s wicked schemes. But why did it all have to fall on her?","Why did she have to have such a mother? Why was she so useless, yet so greedy and selfish?","She had once yearned for even a little bit of maternal love, but later stopped hoping, and she didn’t think it was her fault. After all, that wasn’t her real mother. Now, she was being told that the woman who had been too stingy to spare even a shred of love for her was actually her true mother, and that this mother loved her deeply—she had just mistaken someone else for her.","Hahaha!","Duan Yi just wanted to end this absurd life. She wanted this woman to die! She didn’t want to live anymore either.","Of course, she was once again stopped by the bodyguards.","“I’m sorry, cough, I’m sorry, Xiao Yi... I didn’t know, I really didn’t know it would turn out like this. I just wanted to give you the best life possible. I’m sorry, please forgive me. From now on, I’ll treat you well, always treat you well!” Aunt Mao coughed as she pleaded for forgiveness in a pitiful tone.","But Duan Yi just wanted to scream. “Listen to me, in this lifetime, don’t you dare think I’ll ever forgive you. Even in death, don’t expect my forgiveness. What kind of mother are you? You don’t deserve that title! You ruined my life, it was you, only you! I hate you, I hate you! I wish you were dead, dead!”","In truth, Duan Yi had never asked for much. All she had ever wanted was for her mother to care for her a little.","She never needed the life of a wealthy heiress. Never.","Duan Yi’s hatred was so intense it seemed to materialize and torment Aunt Mao, but the tragic scene only elicited sighs from those around them. No one offered much sympathy, as this was their personal feud.","“Enough! This is the Qin Family’s home. Take your drama back to your own house!” Sixth Uncle Qin was now completely unwilling to look at them. “Butler, fire Aunt Mao. From now on, none of them are allowed to set foot near the Qin Family’s property. Escort them out!”","Aunt Mao had once schemed so maliciously against Qin Tiantian, so the Qin Family naturally didn’t want to let her off easily. But for now, calming the household was the priority, and they didn’t want to see any more of this mess.","Soon, the three were sent away. The staff and medical personnel who had come were treated well, especially the head nurse. Sixth Uncle Qin and his wife gave her a large red envelope and promised her a favor, telling her to ask for help whenever she needed it in the future.","The head nurse felt she had only done her duty and didn’t dare take credit.","The Qin Family hadn’t rested well that night, and unlike Sixth Uncle Qin’s household, which was still buzzing with energy, most of them went back to catch up on sleep.","By evening, Qin Tiantian had returned. When Ji Fei came downstairs, she saw everyone gathered around Qin Tiantian, chatting and laughing.","Qin Tiantian’s eyes were still swollen, as if she had cried many times.","It was truly unfortunate. If Ji Fei and Qin Xian had acted sooner and gotten results, perhaps Sixth Uncle Qin’s family wouldn’t have had to go through this ordeal. Even if Duan Yi had appeared unexpectedly, they could have stopped her immediately. But the timing had been just right for this disaster to unfold.","From now on, Sixth Uncle Qin and his wife wouldn’t just spoil Qin Tiantian—they would practically worship her, given how close they had come to losing her.","“I wonder how Duan Yi is doing now?” Qin Tiantian suddenly sighed.","“Why are you still thinking about her?”","“Yeah, even though she’s pitiful, it’s not really your concern.”","Qin Tiantian said, “But I can’t help feeling that what happened to her had something to do with me. It’s like... she became my substitute and suffered the attack. No, that’s not quite it. I can’t explain it well, but I feel really bad about it.”","Everyone told her she was overthinking it and that she was too kind-hearted.","Ji Fei could understand, though. After all, they had once been good friends, so Qin Tiantian couldn’t help but worry.","Ji Fei couldn’t resist looking into what had happened to them.","[After Duan Yi was sent back, she immediately ran away. Aunt Mao chased after her but couldn’t find her. Meanwhile, her stepson, oblivious to what had happened, started yelling at Duan Yi and ordering Aunt Mao to cook. Then... yikes! Aunt Mao stabbed him several times.]","Qin Second’s family, listening to the gossip, was shocked.","Was this a belated attempt to avenge her biological daughter?","But hadn’t she been the one who had ignored her all along?","[He was taken to the hospital and didn’t die, but his injuries were severe. His life was effectively ruined. The stepfather, who had bitten his own throat in the chaos, now had difficulty swallowing and speaking. He also had to shoulder the burden of his son’s massive medical bills, leaving him utterly broken. As for Aunt Mao, after stabbing her stepson, she grabbed a knife and ran into the streets, frantically searching for her daughter. She was eventually taken to the police station and is now in custody, awaiting trial. She keeps begging the police to help find her daughter, saying her daughter is missing. The police, feeling sorry for her, went to her home to search, but...]","Qin Second’s family was now on the edge of their seats, curious to hear more.","Suddenly, Qin Tiantian’s phone buzzed. She picked it up and exclaimed, “It’s Duan Yi!”","Everyone immediately gathered around her.","It was a message from Duan Yi.","“I’m sorry, Qin Tiantian. Thank you for trying to help me back then, even though I was so terrible... I’m leaving now. I’ll always remember that you once considered me a friend.”","Qin Tiantian was terrified. “She’s not thinking of doing something drastic, is she?”","No one knew for sure. It sounded like it, but maybe not.","“She won’t,” Ji Fei suddenly spoke up. “She’s just found her answer. She’s let go of her obsession with maternal love and feels free now, free to leave that mother behind. She probably just wants to start over somewhere new, to live her own life.”","[Duan Yi secretly returned home, took all the money, gathered her identification documents, destroyed everything that belonged to her, and left the city under the cover of night. When the police arrived, they found nothing, even starting to doubt whether the girl had ever lived there. That was until they found a tattered photo—the only family photo of the four of them, and the only picture of Duan Yi and Aunt Mao together. But now, Duan Yi was no longer in it.]","Qin Second’s family was stunned. In just one day, Duan Yi had experienced things most people never go through in a lifetime. It was as if she had decided to cut ties completely, ending everything in one swift motion.","[The police gave the photo to Aunt Mao, who was now desperate to escape prison and find her daughter. Unfortunately, she wouldn’t be getting out anytime soon, and she would never have the chance to make amends with her daughter.]","Qin Second’s family felt that Sixth Uncle Qin didn’t need to lift a finger. Aunt Mao’s every moment from now on would be torture.","The woman who had wanted to pave the perfect future for her daughter had now lost her forever. Every day, she would be haunted by memories of what she had done to her own flesh and blood.","How many times had she ignored her daughter’s cries for help and pleas for a mother’s love? Those memories would now be like daggers, piercing her soul day after day."]},{"number":426,"title":"Chapter 426: Even If It Means Revealing My Secrets","paragraphs":["\"Is it true?\" Qin Tiantian asked uncertainly.","Qin Xian nodded. \"It's true. If she wanted to die, she wouldn’t have sent you a message.\"","As soon as Qin Xian said it, Qin Tiantian believed him. She even replied to Duan Yi with a message full of blessings.","And so, this little misunderstanding came to a complete end.","Ji Fei looked at Qin Xian speechlessly. Why was it that whatever Qin Xian said carried so much weight? She was the one who had the evidence, after all.","Qin Xian affectionately patted her head. \"Did you sleep well this afternoon?\"","Ji Fei nodded. Without any mental burden, she naturally slept well. \"Don’t you need to rest?\"","\"I’m fine,\" Qin Xian said, though he leaned his head against Ji Fei’s as if relying on her to relax.","Ji Fei felt a pang of heartache seeing him like this and decided not to linger any longer. She quickly pulled Qin Xian along to wash up and go to bed.","However, she couldn’t fall asleep herself. Lying beside Qin Xian, she played with her phone until she got tired. Then she’d glance at his handsome sleeping face to relax. Sometimes, feeling particularly happy, she’d lean over and plant a kiss or two on him. After all, Qin Xian was used to sleeping next to her and wouldn’t wake up easily, though occasionally he’d instinctively pull her closer or nuzzle into the crook of her neck.","It was as if only by being close to her could he feel safe, always trying to align their bodies as closely as possible.","Every time this happened, Ji Fei’s heart would melt. Who could have imagined that the man who usually seemed like an iceberg to others could sometimes sleep as peacefully and gently as a kitten?","Ji Fei continued scrolling through her phone, watching the occasional chatter in the group chat. They were talking about the upcoming birthday banquet, which was just a few days away. The only ones who hadn’t arrived yet were Lu Meihe’s family—the so-called seventh aunt and her household.","Ji Fei put her phone down and fell into deep thought.","Only Lu Meihe’s family remained unverified.","Through her time spent with the Qin family, Ji Fei had already gained a basic understanding of Lu Meihe’s family situation.","Compared to the eldest aunt and the tough-tempered fifth aunt, Lu Meihe, who wasn’t related by blood, had actually been the most doted-on child in the family when she was young. Because everyone loved Grandma Lv, they extended that affection to her, treating her like a real sister.","At home, she had always been the cheerful, lively, and sensible one. The only thing that could be considered out of line was her high school romance with a foreign college student—a relationship that was entirely online. The family didn’t even know the guy’s identity, and everyone just thought she was being a hopeless romantic, spending way too much time chatting with him online.","Though it might not have been related, her first love ended around the same time as Qin Xian’s issues surfaced.","Back then, she spent her holidays accompanying the young genius, Qin Xian. When they discovered he had mental health problems, she devoted herself to helping him, and everyone felt that Lu Meihe had matured, leaving her online romance behind.","Coincidentally, she ended up marrying Yu Hongxian, the foreign psychologist that the old master had hired to treat Qin Xian’s psychological issues. It was said that during the treatment period, the two spent so much time together that they developed feelings for each other.","Later, when Qin Xian was taken away by his parents, Lu Meihe married Yu Hongxian and moved abroad with him.","But whether it was due to the distance or the fact that Lu Meihe wasn’t involved in the Qin Corporation’s affairs, after getting married, she rarely kept in touch with anyone except Grandma Lv. Without the bond of blood, they gradually grew distant, only seeing each other at the old house once every few years.","Even their daughter, Yu Lu, hadn’t been seen for about six or seven years.","Yu Lu happened to be the same age as Qin Tiantian, both turning eighteen this year.","Because of the old master’s milestone birthday, Grandma Lv had repeatedly urged them to come, and the family finally confirmed they would attend.","It’s hard to say how relationships change over time, as everyone has their own lives.","Ji Fei didn’t want to dwell on it too much. Without verification, overthinking would only lead to empty speculation.","For now, she’d just enjoy a good night’s sleep with Qin Xian.","Two days later, they finally heard that Lu Meihe and her daughter would arrive first, while her husband, who had patients to attend to, would come on the day of the birthday banquet.","It was dinnertime when they finished eating, and everyone gathered to wait for Lu Meihe and her daughter.","Seeing Grandma Lv nervously rubbing her hands, it was clear how much she missed her daughter and granddaughter.","The other elders started gossiping.","\"I don’t know what’s going on with Meihe. She hardly ever comes home. I heard from Grandma Lv that the last time they met was two years ago, and they only video call occasionally.\"","\"Meihe used to be so lively. I don’t know why she’s become so distant.\"","\"When we do meet, she’s the same as before. It seems her husband doesn’t like her coming back.\"","\"Really? Is that normal? Is her husband some kind of control freak? A psychologist should know better.\"","\"Apparently, he’s just really attached to her. He takes her with him wherever he goes on business trips.\"","Hearing their conversation, Grandma Lv couldn’t help but chime in, \"He is very clingy. Meihe told me she had to sneak back with her daughter two days early this time. Otherwise, her husband would’ve insisted on bringing them back together on the last day.\"","Seeing Grandma Lv’s happy smile, the others didn’t say much. After all, it was a matter between husband and wife, and at least it seemed their stepsister was happy. They didn’t want to meddle.","Meanwhile, Qin’s Father and Qin’s Mother recalled that Lu Meihe’s husband was none other than Qin Xian’s first psychologist, Yu Hongxian. He had diagnosed Qin Xian with autism accompanied by memory confusion and gradual emotional detachment. Later, he admitted that he couldn’t cure him and suggested they find someone else.","Thinking about everything Ji Fei had done every time they met a new family member, they couldn’t help but glance at the young couple with concern. This was the last one.","Deep down, they hoped that none of this was related to Qin Xian’s past. They’d rather believe they were neglectful parents than accept that Qin Xian might have been harmed. The thought of that would break their hearts.","Qin Xian, meanwhile, was absentmindedly holding Ji Fei. When it came to his aunt Lu Meihe, he really didn’t have many memories. Due to the confusion of his childhood, even if he tried hard to recall, he only had vague impressions. Plus, they hadn’t had any contact since then, so he had no real recollection of her.","But for some reason, whenever he thought of her, his heart would grow heavier, as if... as if...","[Why is this taking so long?]","Qin Xian was startled by Ji Fei’s impatient voice in his arms and couldn’t help but smile. Over the past two days, he had clearly sensed Ji Fei’s growing anxiety. She didn’t even want to go out and have fun anymore.","[Sigh, I hope it’s not her. I really don’t want to suspect anyone, especially since Grandma Lv has been so kind to me. I can’t bear to see such a warm and caring person look sad. But if it really is related to her, I won’t let them off, even if it means revealing my secret.]"]},{"number":427,"title":"Chapter 427: What's going on, is there a problem with the system","paragraphs":["Ji Fei's inner thoughts suddenly left everyone in Qin Second's family stunned.","Revealing a secret? What did that mean? The secret of that gossip system?","Ji Fei couldn't help but calculate in her mind.","[Well, it must be like this. After all, back then, Mom, Dad, and Grandpa investigated so thoroughly. If there really was a culprit, it would mean there was no evidence. So unless the person involved admits it, or Qin Xian regains his memory, the only hope is my system.]","Ji Fei encouraged herself, thinking it was only natural: [Once I find out, I won’t hesitate to prove the existence of my system to everyone, just to expose the person who hurt Qin Xian.]","Qin Second's family was dumbfounded, their breathing becoming rapid.","Qin Xian also stared down blankly at Ji Fei, who was quietly psyching herself up in his arms.","Such a huge secret, and for something like this, she was willing to expose it? Wasn’t she afraid of being treated like a monster? Wasn’t she afraid of putting herself in uncontrollable danger?","Their family had always carefully hidden this secret, all out of concern for Ji Fei's safety.","And now, Ji Fei was willing to take risks for Qin Xian.","The entire family fell silent, deeply moved.","Qin Second's family couldn’t help but reflect and silently vowed that if they ever heard any secrets, they would do everything in their power to verify them and never let Ji Fei take such risks.","Qin Xian looked at Ji Fei, feeling a warm current flow through his heart, as if his soul was being wrapped in the warmest thing in the world.","Unconsciously, Ji Fei had already been willing to do so much for him.","But how could he bear to let Ji Fei take even the slightest risk? He really wanted to take her away right now. The truth wasn’t that important to him. He was already perfectly content with his current life. As long as Ji Fei was by his side, he didn’t need anything else.","Qin Xian was so overwhelmed by Ji Fei's actions that his thoughts were running wild, and he almost impulsively decided to leave with her. Just then, the sound of a car came from outside.","Lu Meihe had arrived with Yu Lu.","She was a beautiful, radiant woman, her hair pinned up with a hairpin, dressed in a very traditional Chinese style. The young girl accompanying her was lively, confident, and full of energy.","Some people stood up to greet them, while others smiled and said hello.","Only Qin Second's family remained tense, waiting for the verdict.","[Lu Meihe... search... no problem!]","Qin Second's family collectively let out a sigh of relief.","Ji Fei was also pleasantly surprised. [She really did like Qin Xian. She took care of him when they were young, often helped him with his studies, and actively sought solutions when he fell ill...]","Qin Second's family smiled.","Qin Xian, however, felt nothing due to his lack of memory. If anything... he even felt a bit disgusted.","But since he was holding Ji Fei, he quickly suppressed the feeling.","[She’s a good elder, so I’ll dig into some gossip. Her first love was... huh, her first online love was the psychologist Yu Hongxian?]","Qin Second's family was stunned.","What? They’d never heard of that!","Or... no one had ever mentioned it!","What was going on?","It felt a bit strange!","They couldn’t help but feel their hearts tighten again, despite having just relaxed.","At that moment, Lu Meihe and her daughter came over to greet Qin Second's family.","\"Second Brother, Second Sister-in-law,\" Lu Meihe's eyes lit up, her smile growing even warmer.","[Huh? What’s going on? Did the system glitch? Why did the information change? Her first love is now Qin's Father!]","Qin's Father, who was about to exchange pleasantries, froze, his expression turning complicated.","Qin's Mom also changed slightly but managed to hold it together, giving Qin's Father a knowing, half-amused look, as she had never heard him mention this before.","[Strange, why did the information change?] Ji Fei was baffled, wondering if she had misread the lines while checking internally.","But Ji Fei didn’t dwell on it. After all, the system’s voice function had gone offline at some point, and no matter how much she called, there was no response. Ji Fei assumed it was because her questions were too silly, and the system didn’t want to bother. Now, she had to figure things out on her own.","She muttered a couple of questions, but when there was no response, she let it go and continued reading.","[Is this too absurd? Oh my god, did I just stumble upon the elders’ youthful secrets? This is so awkward! Turns out, back then, apart from Qin's Father, the other three men in the Qin family had all liked her. But she only had feelings for Qin's Father. When Qin's Father and Qin's Mom started seeing each other, she panicked and confessed, but was rejected because Qin's Father already liked Qin's Mom. Plus, there was a significant age gap between him and Lu Meihe, and he always saw her as a little sister! So it was impossible. After being rejected, she was so embarrassed that she started an online relationship with someone, pretending she had already found a boyfriend, and convinced herself that her feelings for Qin's Father were just a misunderstanding...]","Qin's Father breathed a sigh of relief: Thank goodness for his wonderful daughter-in-law, who had cleared his name! Back then, when the little sister said it was just a misunderstanding, he didn’t take it seriously and didn’t even bother to remember it. Over time, he genuinely forgot about it. If Ji Fei hadn’t brought it up, he probably would never have remembered it in his lifetime.","After all, what adult would remember a little sister confessing her feelings? She was even younger than Yu Lu is now, definitely not an adult yet.","Qin's Father suddenly paused. Wait, does that mean there were several people in the family who liked underage girls? Creeps!","Qin's Mom also relaxed. At least Qin's Father hadn’t intentionally hidden it.","And judging by Lu Meihe's current state, she seemed to be doing well, so she wasn’t a rival.","The younger generation of Qin Second's family was also forced to digest this old gossip, and now they felt awkward around this elder.","Because of this distraction, everyone overlooked the sudden change in information.","When Lu Meihe saw Qin Xian, she paused. \"You’re Qin Xian? You look completely different from when you were a child. I hardly recognize you.\"","Qin Xian nodded faintly, and no one noticed that he didn’t make eye contact with Lu Meihe. \"Auntie.\"","Only Ji Fei felt the arm around her tighten slightly.","Just as Ji Fei was about to look at Qin Xian in confusion, Lu Meihe said, \"You must be Qin Xian’s wife, Ji Fei. Hello, you’re so beautiful.\"","\"Hello, Auntie,\" Ji Fei replied politely with a smile.","Lu Meihe didn’t linger but urged Yu Lu to greet them.","After a long pause with no response, Ji Fei looked up and saw the beautiful, radiant girl staring intently at Qin Xian, who was lost in thought with his eyes downcast. She didn’t move, but her cheeks gradually turned red.","She was completely mesmerized.","Ji Fei coughed lightly to remind her. Lu Meihe also awkwardly nudged her daughter, but Yu Lu still didn’t react.","It wasn’t until Qin Xian, who had been inexplicably tense, heard Ji Fei’s cough and looked over, completely ignoring everyone else, that he asked, \"What’s wrong? Does your throat feel dry? Do you need water?\"","Only when Qin Xian spoke did Yu Lu snap out of her daze. She then turned to Ji Fei, her gaze no longer friendly but serious and wary, as she scrutinized her from head to toe."]},{"number":428,"title":"Chapter 428: Double-check for safety.","paragraphs":["Ji Fei's radar went off.","【Oh? Didn’t find Qin Xian’s enemy, but found my love rival first? What are you looking at? Keep looking, but Qin Xian isn’t yours—he’s mine!】","Although her inner thoughts were already a mess, her expression remained friendly, and she even leaned affectionately on her husband's arm.","\"My throat feels a little itchy, but it’s nothing serious.\"","Qin Xian naturally heard her thoughts and saw Ji Fei’s smug, triumphant little expression. His heart was instantly filled with warmth, and he looked at her with a doting smile.","Qin Second’s family: He must only be yours!","Yu Lu’s face flashed with an unnatural expression.","Finally, Lu Meihe could only jokingly say, \"Do you think your brother and sister-in-law are so good-looking that you’re stunned?\"","Everyone around, whether they understood the situation or not, joined in the laughter.","Yu Lu reluctantly said, \"Qin Xian is good-looking.\"","Ji Fei: So?","At this point, even Lu Meihe felt awkward and could only give Ji Fei an apologetic smile before lightly tapping her daughter’s head. She then took Yu Lu to greet others.","Qin Xian wrapped his arm around Ji Fei and sat down. Ji Fei, dissatisfied, leaned close to Qin Xian’s ear and gently bit his earlobe. She only felt satisfied when she saw his earlobe turn completely red, but she still pretended to be angry and scolded, \"Such a heartthrob!\"","Qin Xian put on an innocent expression, then lowered his head and rubbed his nose. The affection between them was so overwhelming that the people around couldn’t bear to look, though they were quite used to it by now.","Meanwhile, Qin Second’s family was in a good mood. As long as the family was harmonious, Lu Meihe didn’t pose a problem.","Of course, they also knew that Ji Fei’s system wasn’t always accurate. The previous incident had proven its flaws. However, the events it highlighted were generally true, and whether there were unexpected circumstances afterward couldn’t be determined. At least, through the system, they knew that in Lu Meihe’s memory, she had never harmed Qin Xian.","Still, there was one thing everyone was concerned about, and Ji Fei was also pondering it in her heart.","To eliminate all doubts, Ji Fei had to investigate the situation she had seen earlier.","【The online love interest back then turned out to be the psychologist later. Is that just a coincidence? Why is this information so vague? Isn’t it important? System, are you even working properly?】 Ji Fei was getting a bit frustrated.","In the past, the system had always provided information that made the gossip clear and satisfying.","But this time, whether Ji Fei was overthinking it or not, she felt that the information about Lu Meihe was scattered—some parts were overly detailed, while others were too vague. It didn’t match the style of the gossip system at all.","So, after everyone separated, Ji Fei couldn’t help but ask Qin Xian, \"I heard that your uncle was the first person to give you psychological counseling back then. Do you still remember him?\"","Qin Xian answered honestly, \"I have some impression, but I don’t remember much.\"","Ji Fei could understand since Qin Xian had been in a state of memory confusion at the time.","\"He must have been young then, right? Did Grandpa bring him in?\" Ji Fei asked curiously.","\"Grandpa asked a contact from an authoritative institution to recommend someone. He was said to be an expert in child psychology,\" Qin Xian replied.","Ji Fei felt like she was overthinking things again.","Qin Xian was happy that Ji Fei cared so much about him, but seeing her so deep in thought also made him feel a bit sorry for her.","On the other side, Qin’s Father and Qin’s Mom, seeing their daughter-in-law working so hard, also decided to step up. When Lu Meihe sat down to chat with everyone, Qin’s Father was the first to ask, \"By the way, will your husband arrive on the day of the birthday celebration? Is work that busy?\"","Lu Meihe smiled and said, \"Yes, he has many patients, and they’re all people of status. It’s quite troublesome to manage, so it’s hard for him to get away.\"","Qin’s Mom then chimed in with a gossipy tone, \"While he’s not here, let’s gossip a bit. Didn’t you have a very loving online relationship back then?\"","Whether it was Qin’s Father and Qin’s Mom’s imagination or not, after they asked, Lu Meihe’s expression blanked for a moment, as if she was very confused. But then she firmly replied, \"Oh, it was him. What a coincidence, right? Back then, we had already broken up, and we didn’t know each other’s real appearances or names. I didn’t expect to find out later that it was still him.\"","Suddenly, the Old Master spoke up, \"Why didn’t you mention this before?\"","\"No one asked me before,\" Lu Meihe replied with a smile.","The Old Master looked away.","Qin’s Father and Qin’s Mom knew that the Old Master had started to suspect something because of this.","It wasn’t surprising for them to overthink it—it was just too much of a coincidence.","\"Really? That’s such a coincidence?\" Others chimed in, eager to gossip.","\"Then it must be a match made in heaven?\"","Lu Meihe smiled, \"It seems that because he knew I was in this city, he volunteered to come here after hearing about a patient here.\"","\"So, Qin Xian indirectly brought you two together.\"","Lu Meihe’s face showed a hint of discomfort, \"Yes, that’s right.\"","Qin’s Father and Qin’s Mom felt something was off, but they couldn’t pinpoint exactly what it was. They could only relay the information they had to the younger generation.","So, when everyone brought Yu Lu to the younger crowd, Qin Yan, Qin Zhao, and Qin Rong took the opportunity to gossip with Ji Fei and Qin Xian.","After hearing everything, Ji Fei reluctantly accepted the explanation.","Qin Zhao then jokingly said, \"But Mom and Dad said that Auntie Lu seemed a bit strange when she said that. She probably felt awkward being asked about it.\"","However, the information provided by Qin’s Father and Qin’s Mom mostly matched what the system had provided, so it should be fine, right?","【On the other hand, my husband’s family is even more gossipy than I am. They even have a small group chat where they secretly discuss other family members’ gossip. If they were told about the romantic entanglements between Auntie Lu and the Qin family men, they’d probably explode.】","The Qin siblings: ...It’s already pretty explosive. We almost had a parental crisis.","Ji Fei was distracted for a moment but soon returned to thinking about Lu Meihe and Yu Hongxian. She had a strong intuition that something felt off.","Qin Xian didn’t want Ji Fei to overthink things, especially since there wasn’t enough information. If there really was a problem...","Actually, Qin Xian was more suspicious of the psychologist, Yu Hongxian. So he followed Qin Zhao’s lead and subtly reminded Ji Fei, \"When Uncle Yu arrives, let’s not joke about them anymore.\"","Ji Fei immediately snapped out of it, 【Right, no need to rush. Once Yu Hongxian arrives, we can double-check and make sure everything’s safe.】","At the same time, Qin Xian had already sent a message to his assistant.","Although he didn’t know how he had become closed off before, during the last period, the person who had the most opportunity and ability to manipulate him was Yu Hongxian.","Based on Lu Meihe’s reaction and Ji Fei’s intuition about this family, Qin Xian felt it was necessary to have someone investigate Yu Hongxian’s past.","He looked at Ji Fei, his eyes filled with her. He couldn’t let his wife do all the hard work.","By now, everyone was in the main hall, sitting and chatting as per the tradition of welcoming newcomers.","Qin Jiaxi and Qin Tiantian were quite enthusiastic about Yu Lu, who was around their age, so they talked a lot. Qin Rong, who was close in age, stayed by Ji Fei’s side and didn’t say much.","As they sat down, Yu Lu suddenly said to Qin Tiantian and Qin Jiaxi, \"You two are both the young ladies of the Qin family, but why are you so different? One is like a real princess, while the other is like a servant. Qin Jiaxi, you’re actually a people-pleaser with a very low self-esteem, aren’t you? You’ll never get real love like this.\""]},{"number":429,"title":"Chapter 429: Is It That the Flower Qin Holds Is Too Fragrant","paragraphs":["The words instantly made the two younger girls stiffen.","The surroundings fell silent in an instant.","Seeing everyone's reaction, Yu Lu immediately felt uneasy and said, \"Oh dear, I'm sorry. I tend to be very straightforward when I speak. I didn't mean anything by it. You know, my dad is a very renowned psychologist, so I've picked up a lot from him. I guess it's a professional habit. Hahaha.\"","The others didn't feel like arguing with a young girl like her.","\"It's fine,\" Qin Jiaxi instinctively tried to smooth things over. Having grown up in a family where she was used to pleasing others, she had developed the habit, though she was gradually trying to change it.","\"So, what about you? Are you the low-EQ type?\" Ji Fei fired back without hesitation.","Yu Lu froze, her face turning ugly as she glared at Ji Fei.","The others secretly gave Ji Fei thumbs-up. Ji Fei was truly fearless.","\"You—\"","\"Oh dear, I'm sorry. I tend to be very straightforward when I speak. I didn't mean anything by it,\" Ji Fei said sarcastically, linking arms with Qin Xian as she stepped forward. \"I have low EQ too, because my husband said I don't need high EQ. Everyone will give in to me anyway.\"","Everyone nodded in agreement. \"Yes, yes, we'll give in to her. She's the lady of the house!\"","\"So I don't need to change, but you... you might want to be careful not to get punched when you go out!\" Ji Fei said with a seemingly kind reminder, causing several people to burst out laughing.","Yu Lu was so angry she almost stood up to leave, but Qin Wenqiang and Qin Xiaoyu managed to persuade her to stay seated.","\"Everyone's just joking. Don't take it to heart.\"","If Yu Lu really stormed off, it would only confirm that they were bullying the newcomers. However, Yu Lu really wasn't likable. If it weren't for Grandma Lv's sake, no one would have bothered with her.","She was as arrogant as a peacock, knowing her father was a big name in psychology. But so what? Everyone present had a status no less impressive than hers.","It wasn't that they were being exclusionary; it was just that Yu Lu was genuinely hard to get along with.","Thankfully, Ji Fei could put her in her place. They all wished they could be like Ji Fei, but they didn't quite dare.","Yu Lu shot Ji Fei a disdainful glare, clearly still unaware of who she shouldn't mess with.","Ji Fei didn't like her either. When you dislike someone, you should thoroughly enjoy their misfortune.","[Alright, no wonder I don't like her. She's not the low-EQ type; she's the annoying type. She formed cliques in school, isolating and bullying others. Thanks to her father's connections with patients, she had a circle of young masters and ladies from abroad. Plus, her father's family was a medical dynasty, so their little group was untouchable. She was the school's queen bee and bully, acting like she owned the place. No wonder she's still so haughty and condescending even in front of the Qin family's young masters and ladies. It's just a habit.]","Only the Qin family's second branch could hear these thoughts, so while the others chatted with Yu Lu, the second branch was busy enjoying the drama.","But to Yu Lu, it seemed like the entire family was following Ji Fei's lead to oppose her.","Then her gaze landed on Qin Xian.","It was the first time she had fallen in love at first sight. With her experience, she could tell at a glance that this man was the absolute best of the best, unmatched by anyone she had ever met.","She had never seen Qin Xian before, not even in photos of the Qin family. She only knew of his existence. Back then, her life was so vibrant and full; why would she be curious about a name?","Now, she regretted it. If she had known Qin Xian would turn out to be so perfect, with such an extraordinary aura, and that he would take over the Qin Corporation at such a young age, she would have immediately asked her mother to take her to visit Second Master Qin's family.","She should have grown up with Qin Xian. That way, she could have had the advantage of being close to him.","But... it wasn't too late, was it? Her only rule was not to become a stepmother. Otherwise, if she liked someone, she had to have them. Otherwise, what was the point of living?","She was young, she was beautiful, she understood men's psychology, and no man she set her sights on had ever escaped her grasp.","Yu Lu had been wearing a light jacket, but now she claimed it was too hot and took it off right then and there.","Instantly, the men in the room felt awkward. Yu Lu's outfit was more in line with Western fashion, which was still a bit too bold for the setting here.","It wasn't about disrespecting personal style, but when a girl's tank top revealed so much that it was almost indecent, and she kept subtly twisting her body to show off her curves to the people across from her, it was just too uncomfortable.","Especially when she suddenly stood up and leaned over to reach for a tissue on the large coffee table across from her, it was almost like she was offering herself up.","And across from her sat only two men: Qin Xian and Qin Zhao.","Qin Zhao felt like he was collateral damage! He was very clear about her intentions, as he often faced such advances at work. But he had sealed his heart and remained chaste.","Moreover, he found it hilarious because it felt like she was throwing flirtatious glances at someone who was utterly oblivious.","Hadn't she noticed that his brother, even while chatting, never took his eyes off his wife?","Once, he had curiously asked Qin Xian, \"Don't you ever get tired of looking at her?\"","Qin Xian said he didn't know. He just felt a sense of calm and comfort watching her, wanting to see every little change in her expression.","After a few days together, everyone around them had gotten used to it.","But Yu Lu was about to be embarrassed.","Sure enough, when she sat back down and looked up, she realized Qin Xian hadn't even noticed her.","Instead, Ji Fei was staring intently at her... chest.","[Damn! That's huge. How can an eighteen-year-old be like this? It's not scientific. This is absolutely not scientific.]","The Qin family trio: No, focus on the real issue!","[Wait, is she trying to seduce my husband?]","The Qin family trio: Thank goodness, she finally noticed.","[Am I really that unimpressive? Does she really want to compete with me? No, it's not my fault. I'm already great. It's just that Qin Xian is too attractive. Every kind of bee wants a taste of this flower.]","The Qin family trio: ...Yes, yes, it's all Qin Xian's fault!","Ji Fei suddenly turned her head and immediately met Qin Xian's gaze. It was strange. Every time Ji Fei wanted to look at Qin Xian, she always found him looking back at her.","And whenever their eyes met, for some reason, she just wanted to smile. All her frustration instantly melted away.","Ji Fei couldn't help but curl her lips, and Qin Xian followed with a soft smile.","The two of them were completely absorbed in each other, ignoring everyone else, which made Yu Lu's face turn green with anger.","Yu Lu stopped talking and angrily started typing on her phone. She was determined to find out how this Ji Fei had ended up with Qin Xian."]},{"number":430,"title":"Chapter 430: It's You","paragraphs":["Everyone was afraid that she would complain to the elders about them bullying her, but in reality, it was always her who started the trouble.","\"Ahem, Yu Lu, do you have a boyfriend?\" Qin Yi, sensing the awkwardness, changed the subject, subtly reminding Yu Lu. After all, it was obvious to everyone what Yu Lu was after, but the Qin Family couldn't condone such unethical behavior! What if things went too far? How would the elders handle it?","Yu Lu immediately put on a sweet, coquettish tone, \"Not yet, my standards are too high. I've never been in a relationship.\"","Ji Fei, who was about to take a sip of water, nearly choked upon hearing this. Qin Xian quickly patted her back as she coughed, holding her in his arms. Yu Lu's face twisted in anger, convinced that Ji Fei was deliberately flaunting her relationship with Qin Xian to assert her dominance.","But Ji Fei was genuinely shocked by Yu Lu's bold statement.","[Not to mention your current boyfriend was in touch with you not long ago, you've never been in a relationship? Seriously, you've been dating since middle school! And let's not even mention... some of those relationships were illegal before you turned eighteen! Love and freedom are one thing, but please don't lie to people, okay?]","The Qin Family members: ...They really had a troublesome guest on their hands.","Unfazed, Yu Lu continued, \"No one outside compares to the men in our family, especially someone like Qin Xian. I've never met anyone like him before. He must have a lot of admirers, right?\"","Qin Xian, however, didn't bother to hide his disinterest. He had no patience for people he didn't like.","As usual, the others stepped in to speak for him.","\"Xian has always had many admirers since he was young,\" Qin Yan said. \"But none of them ever caught his eye.\"","\"That's an understatement. Some people who liked me would switch their affections to my second brother the moment they saw him,\" Qin Zhao added. \"So, my brother never paid them any attention.\"","\"Anyone who met my brother through me would always ask me to introduce them,\" Qin Rong chimed in nostalgically. \"But my brother never showed interest in anyone.\"","\"Really?!\" Ji Fei suddenly perked up with excitement. \"Were there any particularly dramatic scenes?\"","The Qin Family members: ...Why are you so excited about stories meant for others?","Nevertheless, the three of them started reminiscing about various novel-like scenarios, which thrilled Ji Fei to no end.","\"Ji Fei, you're so excited. Do you wish you could've been with Qin Xian since childhood?\" Qin Yi teased.","\"She probably just wishes she could've started dating him from a young age,\" Qin Xiaoyu joked.","[Well... actually, I was thinking that if there were so many admirers, it would be like having an idol around. If I sold Qin Xian's photos, charged for delivering notes and gifts, I could've achieved financial freedom during my school years!]","After all, in her previous world, Ji Fei had dabbled in such small ventures, earning a little here and there.","Ji Fei: \"Yes, yes! I wish I could've been with Qin Xian since childhood, preferably as his desk mate!\"","Everyone laughed at the couple's sweetness.","The Qin Family members, meanwhile, were pinching each other to hold back their laughter, while Qin Xian's mood darkened noticeably.","Qin Xian suddenly grabbed Ji Fei's chin, turning her face to meet his gaze. His tone was hard to read as he said, \"Yeah, being desk mates would've been nice.\" But by the end of his sentence, his voice softened involuntarily.","Yes, being desk mates would've been nice. But they were several years apart, which was truly a pity.","If he hadn't waited so long for the right person, he might not have made mistakes along the way. It was strange—he couldn't even remember why he had agreed to date someone back then. It was as if he felt he was supposed to be in a relationship at that time.","But it made sense. Before falling in love with Ji Fei, his life had followed a predictable, ordinary path. He had people he disliked, family and friends he cared about, but no one who had deeply impacted him—until Ji Fei came along.","Qin Xian couldn't help but pull Ji Fei closer, tightening his arms around her as she squirmed in his embrace.","The room was filled with laughter, but one person was seething with anger.","She had been the one provoking everyone, yet somehow, the conversation had turned into a display of affection.","Swallowing her frustration, Yu Lu spoke up again, \"So, who was Qin Xian's first love?\"","She asked this because she refused to believe that Qin Xian's first love was his current wife. That would be rarer than winning the lottery. Were all other women fools? Had no one ever won Qin Xian's heart before?","Unbeknownst to her, Yu Lu had just stepped on a landmine.","The one dark chapter in Qin Xian's past.","The three members of Qin Lao Er's Family knew the story, and while others weren't entirely clear on the details, they had heard rumors about a relationship during his university years.","So, his first love was...","At this moment, Qin Xian cowered, lowering his head onto Ji Fei's shoulder, completely submissive, hoping his wife wouldn't get angry or bring up old grievances.","[Hahaha, you wanted to stir up trouble, but you ended up hitting Qin Xian's sore spot. How could he admit that a big CEO like him was once fooled in love? Hahaha!]","Qin Xian: ...","Qin Lao Er's Family: Well, our worries were for nothing.","\"What's the matter? Is it inconvenient to talk about, or does Sister-in-law not want to hear it?\" Yu Lu was clearly trying to stir the pot.","The others, thinking there might be some taboo, tried to change the subject.","Suddenly, Qin Yan seemed to remember something and said with a smile, \"If we're talking about first love, it would have to be the first woman Xian ever promised to marry.\"","Qin Zhao and Qin Rong immediately looked at their sister in shock. What was going on? Was she about to spill some major tea? Did Qin Xian really promise to marry his ex-girlfriend?","Qin Xian also looked at Qin Yan in confusion.","Ji Fei, on the other hand, was intrigued. She couldn't access Qin Xian's past secrets anymore, and there were many things she hadn't fully understood back then.","Seeing the change in everyone's expressions, Yu Lu smiled and said, \"Oh? What's the story? Let's hear it. Surely no one would get upset, right? Don't ruin the fun.\"","But no one paid her any attention. They were all nervous, curious, and worried, but since Qin Lao Er's Family was airing their own dirty laundry, the others could only sit back and enjoy the drama.","Qin Yan suddenly looked at Ji Fei and said with a smile, \"It's you.\"","Ji Fei was stunned. \"Me?\"","She thought Qin Yan was just referring to the time when Qin Xian had promised to marry her after they got together.","Qin Zhao and Qin Rong also remembered—Qin Xian had never promised to marry his ex-girlfriend, so Qin Yan had found a clever way out.","Even Qin Xian thought the same.","The others assumed Qin Yan was just being witty.","But then, in a nostalgic tone, Qin Yan continued, \"I remember when Xian was ten years old... He had started spending more time with us by then. We were playing house, and I wanted to be the bride, with Xian as the groom. But he very seriously said, 'I've already promised to marry someone else in the future, so I can't be your groom, not even pretend.'\""]},{"number":431,"title":"Chapter 431: Second Brother is Like an Iron Tree That Rarely Blooms, Only for One Person","paragraphs":["As Qin Yan spoke so earnestly, everyone quickly began to tease and laugh.","Qin Rong and Qin Zhao also asked in surprise, \"Is that true?\"","Qin Yan nodded, \"I only remembered it recently when I saw Xiao Xi and Wei Wei playing. It’s really funny when you think about it. Hahaha.\"","\"Wait, how can you be sure it was Second Sister-in-law?\" Qin Zhao asked curiously.","Qin Yan replied, \"Because afterward, I asked Mom if she remembered this funny incident, and she casually said, 'Of course I remember! It was the promise with Fei Fei. Didn’t they meet a year before that? Among the kids on vacation, there were only two. Fei Fei was too young to remember, but what about A Xian? Does he remember?'\"","Qin Xian’s expression froze as a memory suddenly flashed through his mind.","A little girl had woven two rings from flowers in the garden, placing one on his finger and one on hers. She giggled and said to him, \"I’ve already kissed Second Brother Qin, and now with this, we’re married. The most handsome Second Brother Qin is my husband! From now on, we’ll be together forever.\"","Back then, Qin Xian couldn’t speak yet and just stared at the ring.","Then the little girl ran off, laughing, but when she returned later, the ring on her finger was already gone, scattered somewhere.","Qin Xian was disappointed, and eventually, his own fragile ring broke too.","Coming back to the present, Qin Xian saw Ji Fei looking at him, her expression slightly uneasy.","[Awkward, that was from childhood... Sigh, could she really have been his first love?]","However, in the ears of the Qin family’s second branch, there was no censored part of the story.","After all, even if mind-reading existed, soul-swapping would naturally be censored.","But Qin Xian seemed to understand something from Ji Fei’s gaze.","He had a strong premonition that the little girl from his fragmented memories was indeed the Ji Fei standing before him.","And the woman who had schemed against him, the one he had instinctively avoided, was not the real Ji Fei.","If something as bizarre as a melon-eating system and mind-reading existed, then other strange things were possible too.","He remembered clearly that when he heard about Ji Fei’s family being in a car accident, he rushed to the hospital to see her. At that time, he couldn’t help but want to be close to her and protect her. But when Ji Fei woke up the second time, that feeling had disappeared.","If such magical things really existed in the world, he believed he could distinguish the differences between the two.","But it seemed Ji Fei didn’t remember the past? Or was there another issue? Qin Xian didn’t dwell on it too much, given his own fragmented memories.","However, he understood why Ji Fei was uneasy now—his wife was jealous, worried that he had been thinking about another Ji Fei from his childhood.","He leaned down, pressing his forehead against hers, and said tenderly, \"Only Fei Fei. The one I love is only Fei Fei.\"","Nothing more needed to be said; that sentiment was enough.","Qin Xian rarely made such straightforward declarations in front of others, and even the usually thick-skinned Ji Fei couldn’t handle it, her face instantly turning red.","The room erupted in cheers.","Only Yu Lu stood out, almost losing her temper. Why did every attempt to stir trouble end up with them flaunting their love?","Yu Lu wasn’t ready to give up. Amid the laughter, she stepped on another landmine. \"So you two have known each other for so long! That’s strange. Even though you’re married, why haven’t you had a wedding yet? Otherwise, we could’ve met earlier.\"","Although Yu Lu didn’t interact much with the younger generation of the Qin family, if any of them were getting married, they would at least send an invitation. Whether they attended or not, they would prepare gifts. So Yu Lu was certain these two hadn’t had a wedding, but since they were already married, they must have registered. This made the situation quite delicate.","Everyone immediately stopped laughing, thinking how Yu Lu always knew how to bring up the most uncomfortable topics.","Not just the second branch of the Qin family, but everyone could sense Qin Xian’s displeasure at that moment.","They didn’t mention the messy reasons from before.","This time, there was a legitimate excuse.","\"I heard Grandfather asked them to postpone it,\" Qin Wenqiang said.","\"Why? Did Grandfather have some issue with Second Sister-in-law?\" Yu Lu immediately asked with a smile, her gloating expression all too obvious.","\"It’s because he’s too satisfied, so he didn’t want them to hold it now,\" Qin Yi quickly interjected. \"In recent years, the Qin family’s romantic luck hasn’t been great. You’ll hear about it soon—several couples have broken up or divorced recently. Grandfather was worried it would clash, so he asked them to delay it.\"","The others nodded in agreement, acknowledging the bad luck.","In truth, the second branch of the Qin family knew it wasn’t about luck but rather the accumulation of long-standing issues. It was only because of Ji Fei, the anomaly, that everything had come to light so quickly. Without Ji Fei, these problems might have remained hidden for years.","But Qin Xian and Ji Fei knew each other inside out, so there was no need to worry.","Suddenly, Qin Xian spoke up, \"Since everyone’s here, I’ll take this opportunity to announce that after Grandfather’s birthday celebration, you’ll all need to set aside some time to attend Fei Fei’s and my wedding. We’ll pick a good date and let you know.\"","The room was in an uproar.","\"Really? You’re going to hold it right after?\"","\"But didn’t Grandfather say...\"","\"It’s fine. I’ll talk to Grandfather. I don’t want to wait any longer,\" Qin Xian said, turning to Ji Fei. \"We don’t believe in those things.\"","Seeing Qin Xian’s seriousness, Ji Fei nodded as well. \"Yes, we don’t believe in them. We only believe in each other.\"","When the right person is there, even the worst luck can’t stand in the way.","There was nothing left to say but to offer congratulations.","Qin Zhao even boldly declared, \"Perfect timing. Grandfather’s birthday will bring you good fortune.\"","Everyone burst into laughter again.","The atmosphere became even more harmonious, making Yu Lu feel even more like an outsider.","Yu Lu couldn’t take it anymore. If this continued, she might explode in anger. She excused herself, saying she was tired and needed to rest, and asked a servant to show her to her room.","As a quasi-daughter of the family, she still stayed with them.","After she left, everyone exchanged glances and chuckled quietly.","\"She’s so annoying,\" Qin Tiantian couldn’t help but say. It was rare to hear Tiantian express dislike for someone.","\"What? Weren’t you very enthusiastic at first?\" Qin Xiaoyu teased.","\"But she was so rude to Jiaxi, and she’s been so hostile to Second Sister-in-law. What’s she thinking? Does she want to ruin Second Brother and Second Sister-in-law’s relationship?\" Qin Tiantian pouted.","\"Do you think their relationship can be ruined?\" Qin Jing pointed across the room.","Ji Fei was already sitting cross-legged on the sofa, completely enveloped in Qin Xian’s embrace, as if she were a precious treasure. He was even feeding her fruit, completely oblivious to the world around them. With such an intense bond, there was no room for anyone else to interfere.","Their Second Brother was like an iron tree that rarely bloomed, but when it did, it was only for one person.","Qin Tiantian found it unbearably sweet and wanted to take a photo to send to Second Brother, who always rewarded her with red packets.","\"I didn’t know much about Auntie’s daughter before, but now it seems she’s not the type to give up easily. I wonder if she’ll stop after tonight.\""]},{"number":432,"title":"Chapter 432: Get Out of Our Sight","paragraphs":["At this moment, Yu Lu returned to her room after throwing a tantrum. She finally picked up her phone and, after some urging, received the general information she had been waiting for.","After reading it, her eyes immediately lit up.","So, this was how their marital relationship came about? The Ji Family was already in name only, so there was no threat of a political marriage. Ji Fei was just a comedian, with nothing but a good figure and beauty to her name. She had almost nothing else.","So, was it just a case of love blossoming over time?","Looking at Qin Xian's restrained demeanor, having been emotionally deceived by his ex-girlfriend and then tricked into marriage by Ji Fei, it seemed he had never experienced a truly exceptional woman. Now, he was simply caught up in the heat of romance. It was much simpler than she had imagined. A playful smile curled on Yu Lu's lips.","She immediately added Qin Xian's contact information directly.","At this moment, Ji Fei was playing with Qin Xian's phone when she saw the friend request. She couldn't help but feel exasperated. This girl really didn’t give up, did she?","Ji Fei showed it to Qin Xian, who glanced at it and rejected the request without hesitation.","Not long after, another request came through.","\"Brother Qin Xian, it's me, Yu Lu. My mom told me to add you.\"","Ji Fei chuckled. She was quite good at finding excuses. After all, there was still a nominal family connection between them.","Ji Fei couldn’t help but think to herself, amused by her own thoughts. *This girl is different—she has no blood relation to Qin Xian. If I weren’t here, given the family ties, it’s entirely possible that she might have ended up with Qin Xian, this so-called cousin of his.*","As she was lost in thought, Qin Xian pinched her nose.","Ji Fei glared at him, feigning grievance. Qin Xian took the phone and rejected the request again, not bothering to explain. No matter how many times she tried, the answer would always be no.","Sure enough, after a while, Yu Lu stopped trying.","*Oh, I thought she had given up. Turns out she thought I was the one rejecting her on Qin Xian's behalf. She must be planning to try again when she sees Qin Xian holding his phone. This girl really knows how to console herself.*","The second branch of the Qin family was chatting when they unexpectedly got wind of this drama. They were utterly speechless.","Qin Xian was equally exasperated. He had no fondness for Lu Meihe, and he certainly wouldn’t indulge Yu Lu in the slightest.","So, that night, when someone knocked on his door wearing a seductive nightgown, Qin Xian’s face instantly darkened. His icy gaze sent a shiver down Yu Lu’s spine.","But she boldly displayed her curves, the kind that could make any man’s blood boil, and said in a coquettish voice, \"Brother Qin Xian, there’s something on top of my closet that’s too high for me to reach. Could you help me get it? Please?\"","As she spoke, she tried to tug at Qin Xian’s sleeve, acting cute.","Qin Xian stepped aside. \"You can ask the servants for help.\"","Yu Lu, failing to grab his sleeve, took a step forward, attempting to brush her knee against him. \"I don’t know how to call them. It’s so quiet here...\"","Qin Xian pulled out his phone, ready to call someone.","Yu Lu quickly added, \"But they’re not tall enough. They’d need a ladder, and it’s too noisy at this hour. Brother Qin Xian, you’re the tallest. You can definitely help me.\"","By now, Yu Lu was practically breathing seductively, her eyes filled with allure.","Any man with even a hint of interest would have been unable to resist at this point, either following her or engaging in some flirtatious banter.","\"What exactly do you need to get in the middle of the night? Dust from the top of the closet?\" Ji Fei’s voice suddenly came from behind, clearly displeased.","*I’m really speechless. Is Yu Lu really this bold? If it weren’t for my gossip system, I wouldn’t have believed she actually threw her underwear on top of the closet, planning for Qin Xian to help her get it. The moment he reached for it, she thought he’d realize she wasn’t wearing anything underneath, and then she’d pretend to fall into his arms. Even if nothing happened immediately, she’d still manage to captivate him. Ugh, does she even know what personal hygiene is? She’s trying to dirty my husband’s hands! How infuriating!*","Qin Xian: ...Just hearing the plan made his ears feel dirty.","Yu Lu, however, remained oblivious to the fact that her scheme had been completely exposed. Hearing Ji Fei’s sharp tone, she was even more pleased. She had come prepared for Ji Fei to find out. In fact, she hoped Ji Fei would get jealous and lose her temper. Men often liked to play the mediator in such situations, which would only make Ji Fei angrier.","\"Sister-in-law, are you upset? I’m sorry. It’s my first day here, and I don’t know how things work. Since you two live close by, I thought I’d ask Brother Qin Xian for help. It’s just a small favor. Surely, it’s not worth making you this unhappy, is it?\" Yu Lu finished with a pitiful look at Qin Xian. \"Brother Qin Xian...\"","*Hahaha, she’s really putting on a classic performance! What a textbook example of green tea tactics. Hilarious! But, I have to admit, with that devilish figure, that innocent yet seductive makeup, the green tea vibe, and that nightgown... Wow, is she really not wearing anything underneath? I can’t even bring myself to look closely... She’s downright mesmerizing. If I were a man, I’d probably be tempted too.*","Just as Ji Fei finished her internal rant, Qin Xian suddenly shifted his body, blocking half of Ji Fei’s view. Ji Fei had to tilt her head to see around him.","Qin Xian immediately said impatiently, \"Then don’t get it. Don’t disturb our rest.\"","With that, he moved to close the door.","Yu Lu was stunned. She quickly pushed against the door, trying to read Qin Xian’s expression for any signs of guilt or hesitation, perhaps fearing his wife’s reaction.","But there was nothing. Qin Xian’s face was as impassive as ever, now even colder, as if encased in ice.","Yu Lu bit her lip, forcing an awkward smile. \"Brother Qin Xian, let me add your contact information. My mom said you’re the head of the family, and I should reach out to you if I need anything. Please accept my request.\"","She immediately sent a friend request, and Qin Xian’s phone lit up with the notification.","Yu Lu watched as Qin Xian leisurely opened his phone. Just as she was about to smile, she saw the notification: *Request declined.*","Her face stiffened. \"What’s going on? Is Sister-in-law not letting you add me? I’m just your cousin. There’s no need for this, is there?\"","Ji Fei looked at her innocently.","Yu Lu looked up and met Qin Xian’s icy gaze, which was now filled with bone-chilling coldness.","\"Know your place.\"","Yu Lu froze but still tried to defend herself.","Then she heard Qin Xian speak bluntly, without any attempt to soften his words. \"Do you like me? I will only ever love my wife. I will never like you. So, stop being a nuisance in front of us! If you try this again, even Grandma Lv won’t be able to save you from the consequences.\""]},{"number":433,"title":"Chapter 433: Everything is According to Sister-in-law's Preferences, Right","paragraphs":["It was probably out of respect for Grandma Lv that Qin Xian acted so decisively. After all, Yu Lu's advances were so aggressive that if he let her continue like this, things might spiral out of control.","Better to make things clear once and for all, to avoid any further complications and to completely shut down all of Yu Lu's excuses.","Sure enough, after Qin Xian finished speaking, Yu Lu froze in place. His tone was serious, and she wasn’t foolish—she could tell.","Shouldn’t men enjoy scenes of women fighting over them? Even if they weren’t intentionally two-timing, shouldn’t they feel a sense of pride in such situations? Even the most outstanding men couldn’t escape this—they usually pretended not to understand and secretly reveled in it! What was wrong with Qin Xian?","Staring at the closed door in front of her, Yu Lu returned to her room in a daze and collapsed onto the bed.","She had never felt so humiliated or defeated in her life. In an instant, a wave of bitterness overwhelmed her, and tears began to fall.","She had never cried over a man before.","If Qin Xian had initially been her prey, he had now truly pierced her heart.","She had always been spoiled and confident in her understanding of human psychology, so nothing had ever slipped out of her control. This was her first real defeat.","She refused to give up. If seduction didn’t work, she would resort to drugging him. After all, wasn’t that how his wife had come into the picture?","Unfortunately for her, Ji Fei saw right through her plan.","Ji Fei’s lips twitched as she clung to Qin Xian, nibbling his chin. “You’re such a magnet for trouble!”","Hearing Ji Fei’s thoughts, Qin Xian’s expression darkened. It seemed some people just couldn’t take a hint.","Qin Xian couldn’t be bothered to deal with it and instead took the initiative to send a message in the family’s gossip group behind Ji Fei’s back. He had more important matters to attend to.","In no time, the group chat exploded.","After replying to a few messages, Qin Xian wrapped his arms around his beloved and went to sleep.","The next morning, Qin Xian went alone to see Grandpa Qin.","Upon hearing his request, Grandpa Qin glared at him in exasperation, but then a sense of pride washed over him. It was rare for his grandson to make such a bold request, and he was more than willing to grant it. This was an honor none of his other grandchildren had received, as Grandpa Qin had always carried a sense of guilt toward Qin Xian.","“Back then, I didn’t take good care of you. I’m glad you’ve now... settled down and built a family. The fact that you’ve found someone you want to spend your life with makes me truly happy.” As he spoke, Grandpa Qin’s eyes grew misty.","“Grandpa, I’m fine now,” Qin Xian said calmly. Since he barely remembered the past, it no longer mattered to him.","Grandpa Qin blinked and waved his hand. “Alright, have your people make the arrangements.”","After leaving the study, Qin Xian went to see Grandma Lv. Originally, she had been handling the preparations for the birthday banquet, but now Qin Xian took over everything.","Grandma Lv was still worried, fearing that Qin Xian might be overburdened, but he assured her it was no trouble.","As they were talking, Lu Meihe arrived. It was natural for her to visit her mother, and when she saw Qin Xian, she greeted him with a smile.","Qin Xian immediately felt uncomfortable, especially when Grandma Lv got up to fetch something and Lu Meihe sat down close to him. In that instant, his body stiffened, and his expression turned grim.","“It seems Yu Lu hasn’t gotten up yet. Last night, she went back with you all to rest. I hope she didn’t cause any trouble. That girl has been spoiled by her father and me. If she’s being stubborn, feel free to scold her as her elder brother. It’s fine.”","If Grandma Lv hadn’t returned just then, Qin Xian might not have been able to respond at all. He quickly stood up, excused himself, and left without another word.","“Did I say something wrong?” Lu Meihe asked, puzzled.","Grandma Lv sighed. “Ah, it’s our fault for not taking better care of him when he was young. His personality still hasn’t fully recovered. Maybe when your husband arrives, we should have him take another look.”","Lu Meihe suddenly froze, her mind going blank.","When Grandma Lv called her name twice more, Lu Meihe abruptly changed the subject, and Grandma Lv, not noticing, went along with it.","From that day on, the entire old estate began to be decorated. Various construction teams came and went.","First, the main residence was adorned, followed by the backyard, the square...","As Ji Fei passed by, she couldn’t help but laugh. “Grandpa may be old, but his heart isn’t. Does he really like these pink and blue colors? And all these hearts, balloons, and flowers? Is this really the style for a birthday banquet?”","The other family members were equally puzzled and asked the elders, but no one knew for sure. All they knew was that everything had been arranged by Qin Xian.","“Could it be... that it’s all tailored to Sister-in-law’s preferences?” Qin Tiantian asked with a smile.","Ji Fei glanced around. “Your brother has no sense of aesthetics, but you’re right—this is exactly my style.”","The members of Qin Xian’s family didn’t dare say more. Apart from busily coordinating with the workers, they were careful to prevent others from noticing anything unusual.","Meanwhile, Yu Lu, who refused to give up until she hit a wall, finally got her hands on the drug but couldn’t find an opportunity to use it. Qin Xian was simply too busy. Even Ji Fei only saw him at night. To avoid any mishaps, Ji Fei reminded him to stay far away from Yu Lu and not to eat or drink anything suspicious.","Qin Xian didn’t need Ji Fei’s reminder, but as he looked at her, the love in his eyes became even harder to conceal.","One day before the banquet, a team of makeup artists arrived to do trial looks for the women of the household.","Ji Fei usually preferred light makeup and wanted to skip the hassle, but Qin Yan and Qin Rong insisted, forcing her to sit through the full process in her room.","“You’re the lady of the house. You have to make a dazzling entrance. You can’t just slack off,” Qin Yan said.","“Exactly! All sorts of business partners will be there. If another Yu Lu shows up, it’ll be a nightmare. So, Sister-in-law, you have to outshine everyone!” Qin Rong exclaimed excitedly.","“Alright, alright. But do you really need to watch me like this? Shouldn’t you find your own rooms to get ready?” Ji Fei asked, noticing that the team assigned to her was the largest—over a dozen women, each with their own tasks.","With all their tools, the room felt a bit cramped.","“We’ll watch you first, then go do ours,” the two said, their enthusiasm making Ji Fei suspicious.","[Are they just using me as a dress-up doll?]","Qin Yan and Qin Rong: Nervous.JPG.","[They don’t really need this elaborate trial. They’re just playing a dressing game with me!]","Qin Yan and Qin Rong: ...","Suddenly, there was a loud bang outside. Ji Fei immediately wanted to see what was happening, but the curtains in the room had been drawn without her noticing.","“What’s going on?” Ji Fei asked.","Qin Yan quickly held her down. “Don’t move. The makeup artist is about to start.”","Qin Rong ran to the window and pretended to look out. “Oh, something that was being moved earlier fell over. It’s nothing.”","Meanwhile, in the newly constructed building, all the girls who had gone in for their trial looks were being quietly ushered out.","When they stepped outside, they were stunned."]},{"number":434,"title":"Chapter 434: Total Mobilization","paragraphs":["The square before them, previously cluttered with decorative materials, had now been meticulously arranged into various enchanting displays. A dreamy kingdom of balloons, a wonderland of flowers, sacred pillars inspired by mythology, candles, lights, projections, and various text signs all conveyed messages of love.","This was no birthday banquet—it was clearly a proposal scene.","Except for Yu Lu, everyone else rushed toward the young man standing in the center.","\"What's going on? What's going on?\" Qin Tiantian exclaimed excitedly.","Qin Yi said, \"We just saw it when we came out, but it's obvious someone is planning to propose formally.\"","They saw huge posters, some featuring Ji Fei alone, and others showing candid photos of Ji Fei and Qin Xian together.","\"That one was taken by me,\" Qin Tiantian cried out in delight.","\"So, Second Brother hasn't proposed to Second Sister-in-law yet?\" Qin Jiaxi asked in surprise.","Qin Wenqiang laughed, \"They talked about holding a wedding before, but I didn’t expect him to propose now. He really keeps his word.\"","\"Look at all these details. It doesn’t seem like a spur-of-the-moment decision. He must have been planning this for a long time,\" Qin Jing analyzed.","\"Of course! Look at those flowers. I only heard Second Sister-in-law mention once that she likes blue hydrangeas. Did Second Brother really buy all the hydrangeas in the city?\" Qin Xiaoyu said with an excited laugh.","\"Hey, they're here. Let's help,\" Qin Zhao called out as he walked over. \"Cousin, the band—go keep an eye on them.\"","\"Why didn't you tell us earlier?\" Qin Yi immediately became frantic.","\"It had to be kept secret! I got the band you're most familiar with. The songs were chosen by my brother, and everything is ready. Just follow the plan!\" Before Qin Zhao could finish, Qin Yi had already rushed toward the orchestra that had just arrived.","When Qin Zhao turned around, he saw the rest of his siblings staring at him eagerly, as if waiting for him to assign them tasks.","After receiving their roles, they scattered excitedly to help with the preparations.","When they arrived, they realized that each station was already being monitored by people familiar with Qin Xian's plans and requirements. However, since these individuals weren’t familiar with the Qin family or the mansion, collaboration was essential.","Upon meeting, introductions were naturally exchanged.","Qin Wenqiang, who was assigned to oversee the placement of the posters, noticed a woman working efficiently with a walkie-talkie, giving out instructions. Curious, she went over to greet her.","The woman turned around with a professional smile. \"Are you from the Qin family? Hello, I’m Pei Mingxuan, a partner at Ji Fei's studio and her career manager. Mr. Qin Xian asked me to come and help.\"","\"Oh, hello. I'm their eldest cousin,\" Qin Wenqiang replied.","Over at the band, Jing Yan stood up to greet Qin Yi, and they quickly became acquainted.","\"When did you arrive?\" Qin Yi asked.","Jing Yan rubbed his temples. \"Late last night.\"","\"That's really hard work.\"","\"Well, it’s a once-in-a-lifetime proposal for a brother. Of course, we had to help. Actually, this was originally planned to happen at our place, but as soon as the engagement ring was ready... I guess he couldn’t wait any longer, huh?\" Jing Yan laughed.","By now, each group had made new friends and was enthusiastically discussing the surprise proposal.","In a daze, Yu Lu finally realized what was about to happen. Although she knew the two were already married, seeing Qin Xian prepare such an elaborate proposal scene made her feel as if she had been metaphorically slapped in the face.","It wasn’t just the extravagance and grandeur of the scene but also the timing.","Grandpa Qin's milestone birthday banquet was set to shake the business world, and many influential people would attend, making it a grand event.","By choosing to propose the day before, Qin Xian ensured that the banquet would be filled with discussions about the proposal. All eyes would be on Ji Fei, and no one would dare gossip about their lack of a wedding or question their relationship. Instead, everyone would see how much Qin Xian adored Ji Fei and how much Grandpa Qin valued his granddaughter-in-law.","Any attempt by Yu Lu to interfere would make her look like a clown.","Or rather, this couple, about to receive the world's blessings, would make anyone trying to come between them a target of public scorn.","Having failed to seduce Qin Xian, Yu Lu now had to face this situation. Overwhelmed, she turned around and tried to rush back inside.","However, as soon as she reached the entrance of the new building, two black-clad bodyguards suddenly appeared and blocked her way.","Luo Fei stepped forward with a smile. \"Young lady, no matter who you are, Mr. Qin Xian has instructed that no one disturb his wife. Please wait outside for the ceremony.\"","\"I forgot something inside,\" Yu Lu said through gritted teeth, determined to ruin the surprise.","But then a stranger, a woman with a similar style but much taller, walked out of the building. She looked Yu Lu up and down.","\"It's fine, Luo Fei. We'll follow her. If she causes any trouble, just knock her out,\" Guo Yalan said with a smile.","\"You... What are you doing? I’m part of the Qin family! I’m...\" Yu Lu's eyes burned with anger.","\"If you weren’t assigned a task, it means Mr. Qin Xian doesn’t consider you one of his own. So, either you leave, or we’ll make you leave—and it won’t be pretty,\" Guo Yalan said, unyielding.","Yu Lu clearly knew she was outmatched and could only storm off toward the Qin Family Mansion to complain.","Luo Fei turned back. \"Did the dress get delivered?\"","\"Yes, it’s the one I designed myself. I’m a great fashion designer, after all,\" Guo Yalan replied.","\"Are you sure? Will Mr. Qin Xian let Ji Fei wear something you designed?\"","\"Hey, hey, hey! I have conservative designs too, you know. With Qin Xian being such a jealous person, anything too revealing wouldn’t make it out the door. But trust me, it’ll look amazing.\" As she spoke, someone else came out.","\"Sis, it seems Sister Ji Fei has changed into the dress. By the time estimate, we have about an hour left,\" Han Ziyu said.","Guo Yalan pinched her sister's cheek and then picked up the walkie-talkie to relay the message.","Outside, the preparations became even more frantic.","Han Ziyu smiled. \"I just saw Yu Rouyin and Sun Man. They rushed over from the film set.\"","Meanwhile, at the Qin Family Mansion, the elders had already received the news. Qin's Father and Qin's Mom had even changed their clothes and were nervously waiting for further instructions.","Just then, Yu Lu stormed in with red eyes.","Qin's Father and Qin's Mom exchanged a glance and then signaled Fifth Aunt Qin.","Fifth Aunt Qin immediately stepped forward, pulling Yu Lu toward Lu Meihe to prevent her from ruining the atmosphere."]},{"number":435,"title":"Chapter 435: Proposal Ceremony","paragraphs":["“Mom, they...” Yu Lu was about to complain.","“Today is an important day for the head of our family. With so many people around, conflicts are inevitable. If you feel wronged, please try to bear with it for now. We’ll stand up for you after everything is over. Don’t spoil the mood, or your second brother will be upset,” Fifth Aunt Qin said with a smile.","It was clear that everyone had noticed Yu Lu’s recent antics.","Lu Meihe also felt helpless and pulled Yu Lu aside, saying, “Don’t cause any trouble. Just behave and stay close to me.”","Yu Lu felt wronged but was silenced by her mother’s stern look. With so many elders present, the atmosphere didn’t allow her to act out.","Frustrated, Yu Lu ran back to her mother’s room and called her father to vent.","Yu Hongxian was shocked to hear that they had already returned. “Why didn’t you tell me?”","Yu Lu was startled by her father’s tone and grew even more furious. “Why are you being so harsh? What’s the big deal? I’m telling you about how Qin Xian is mistreating me!”","“Qin Xian... Has your mother seen Qin Xian?” Yu Hongxian suddenly asked.","“What? Of course, we’ve been back for a while now. Dad, what are you even talking about?”","“Has anything unusual happened in the past two days?” Yu Hongxian pressed.","“Huh? Even if you’re attached to Mom, you don’t need to act like this. Mom’s been fine, just spending time with Grandma. I’m talking about me, Dad! Help me figure this out. I’ve never wanted someone so badly. Today, he’s planning this grand proposal for that woman. What does he mean by that? Dad, don’t you know hypnosis? Can you hypnotize him to make him fall for me?”","“Enough!”","Suddenly, Yu Hongxian shouted over the phone, startling Yu Lu into silence. “Dad!”","“Lulu, listen to me. You can date anyone you want in this lifetime, but Qin Xian is off-limits. Don’t get close to him, and don’t let your mother get close to him either...”","“But Dad!”","“Listen to me! Qin Xian is a no! I’ll be there soon... Damn it, there’s a storm... Listen, Lulu, keep an eye on your mom during this time. I’ll come as soon as possible. If your mom acts strangely, contact me immediately! Don’t tell anyone, understand? This is very important! It’s crucial for our entire family!”","Yu Hongxian emphasized repeatedly, and Yu Lu, hearing her father’s tone for the first time, instinctively agreed. By the time she processed what had happened, her father had already hung up. Furious, Yu Lu buried herself in her blankets and cried.","Meanwhile, Lu Meihe also received a call from her husband. After a few casual exchanges, she was relieved that he wasn’t angry about her sneaking away.","Not long after, Qin Xian appeared at the door in a tailored suit, different from his usual attire. The suit was stylish with subtle patterns, exuding low-key luxury. His white shirt and black suit made him look impeccably refined, almost unreal.","Qin’s Father and Qin’s Mom were moved to tears, unable to imagine how grand his actual wedding would be.","Qin Xian invited the elders outside and stood at the designated spot, where a path of flower petals led to the entrance of the new building.","Holding a bouquet, Qin Xian gazed intently in one direction.","Meanwhile, Ji Fei stood in front of a mirror, confused.","“Wait, is this the right outfit for a birthday banquet?”","She was wearing a pristine white gown, intricately designed with a fishtail silhouette adorned with pearls. The front of the dress was shorter, resembling ocean waves that shimmered with every movement, thanks to the embedded diamonds. The dress accentuated her long, slender legs and cinched waist, though Ji Fei felt no discomfort. To others, she looked breathtakingly delicate.","Paired with a set of ruby jewelry, she looked more radiant than the flowers themselves.","When she stepped out, the women in the room gasped in awe.","“Ahhh, so beautiful, sister-in-law!” Qin Rong excitedly snapped photos.","Qin Yan nearly teared up. “Stunning, absolutely stunning. Our Feifei is truly the most beautiful.”","“Wait, isn’t this a bit too much for Grandpa’s birthday banquet? Shouldn’t we keep it low-key and luxurious? This... this outfit could pass as a wedding dress!”","Ji Fei was baffled. Was this how the wealthy celebrated? Shouldn’t it be more understated?","Qin Yan and Qin Rong exchanged guilty glances.","Suddenly, Qin Rong grabbed her phone and said, “Oh no, something’s happened to Second Brother! Sister-in-law, hurry downstairs!”","Seeing their urgency, Ji Fei didn’t have time to think. Had Yu Lu succeeded in causing trouble?","As she ran downstairs in her heels, her flowing dress created a beautiful arc in the air.","When Ji Fei reached the entrance, she froze.","The scene outside was entirely different from what she had seen four hours ago. It felt like she had stepped into another world.","The moment she appeared, the crowd erupted in cheers and applause.","At the end of the flower-petal path stood a man bathed in sunlight, as if naturally filtered, captivating and mesmerizing.","He smiled at her, extending his hand in an inviting gesture.","In that moment, Ji Fei understood, but an overwhelming nervousness took hold of her.","This was... Qin Xian’s proposal?","For some reason, Ji Fei felt like crying.","As she was about to step out, two flower bouquets appeared before her.","Qin Yan and Qin Rong each handed her a bouquet and placed a simple crown and veil on her head.","“Go on, Feifei.”","“Go on, become my sister-in-law.”","Ji Fei took the flowers and stepped outside. Along the petal path stood many familiar faces, each holding a bouquet, ready to offer their blessings.","The first was Luo Fei.","“Take care of each other.”","Next were Guo Yalan and Han Ziyu.","“The dress I designed—beautiful, right?”","“Sister Fei, you’re absolutely stunning!”","Then came Yu Yue and Bai Xiaoxi.","Bai Xiaoxi was in tears. “I don’t know why, but this is so touching!”","“You beat us to it. Congratulations!”","Cen Ting and Jing Yan stood on either side, offering their flowers.","“The ruby jewelry I designed is worth a fortune and will hold its value.”","“Don’t bully my friend.”","Next were several uniquely beautiful women.","Pei Mingxuan sighed. “I was hoping to make money off you, but I guess Mr. Qin won’t let you keep your marriage a secret anymore.”","Yu Rouyin and Sun Man said, “Boss, may you be happy. Don’t forget about our studio. Keep that career drive alive!”","“Look here.” Ji Fei turned and heard the click of a camera. Behind it was a familiar figure, Ruan Jia.","Ruan Jia held the camera confidently. “Good deeds bring good rewards. You’ll be happy for life.”","Ji Fei was genuinely surprised. Qin Xian had invited all the friends she had made since coming into this world.","Further ahead, she saw someone even more unexpected—Chu Xinyue.","Chu Xinyue handed her a bouquet. “Sister Fei, be happy. Second Brother Qin will surely make you happy.”","A few steps later, she encountered Qin Zhao.","Ji Fei raised an eyebrow.","Qin Zhao handed her a flower. “Stay focused. Second Brother is waiting for you.” He remained composed, clearly supporting his brother and sister-in-law.","Ji Fei smiled and continued walking.","Next came Qin’s siblings, with Qin Jiaxi and Qin Tiantian nearly crying as they hugged Ji Fei, only to be pulled away by the others.","Finally, Ji Fei saw Qin’s Father and Qin’s Mom.","Both had tears in their eyes.","“Feifei, don’t worry. Ah Xian will take good care of you.”","“Yes, if Ah Xian ever upsets you, tell Dad, and I’ll scold him for you!”","Ji Fei couldn’t help but laugh, though tears streamed down her face. Despite the dreamy, romantic setting, an overwhelming sense of emotion welled up inside her.","She looked up and met the gaze of the man who had always looked at her with such tenderness, ever since that one fateful day."]},{"number":436,"title":"Chapter 436: Marry Me","paragraphs":["From the moment Ji Fei appeared at the door, Qin Xian couldn’t take his eyes off her. His heartbeat quickened with every step she took closer to him.","He felt so nervous that he was almost suffocating, and his hand, clutching the ring box, trembled uncontrollably.","She was the girl who made life feel interesting, the girl who made him dream of building a future with someone, the girl he wished to hide in the depths of his heart, never letting anyone else steal her attention. He just wanted to keep her by his side forever, watching her every moment.","No matter how he tried to prove that she was his, it never felt enough.","So, he decided to leave behind every piece of evidence in the world that would show they belonged to each other.","She... had finally come to him.","Ji Fei had originally come here carefree, just wanting to live a relaxed life and enjoy the perks. To her, Qin Xian was just a handsome guy to admire.","But gradually, the warmth and protectiveness of this family made her unconsciously integrate into their lives.","Later, Qin Xian’s changes, his feelings, and his confession.","By the time Ji Fei realized it, Qin Xian was always by her side, indulging her in even the most trivial matters. He would always stand behind her, giving her confidence, always watching over her. For Ji Fei, who had always felt adrift and unattached, this gave her the feeling of being cherished deeply.","She couldn’t find a reason not to like him, not to love him.","Perhaps this proposal was a surprise, an unexpected twist.","Qin Xian probably didn’t understand what this meant to Ji Fei.","This was a formal promise to give her a home.","Not to her past self, but to the real her.","The previous marriage certificate meant nothing—this was the real commitment between her and Qin Xian to spend their lives together.","Ji Fei suddenly felt as if she were walking on clouds, lightheaded and unsure of herself.","But when she stood in front of Qin Xian, met by his unwavering gaze, her heart settled. She knew she could trust him.","From looking up to looking down, Qin Xian knelt on one knee before Ji Fei and took her hand.","The room fell silent, the music fading into the background.","Professional equipment ensured that Qin Xian and Ji Fei’s words would be amplified clearly for everyone to hear.","Qin Xian’s dark eyes burned with intensity as he looked at Ji Fei.","“Ji Fei, meeting you is the greatest fortune of my life. Our story began with a misunderstanding, but I’m glad I didn’t let you go in a moment of impulse. It gave me the chance to truly know you. I love you, not for the past, but for the present and the future. Will you marry me?”","Everyone had their own interpretation of Qin Xian’s proposal, but Ji Fei’s heart skipped a beat. She looked at him uncertainly.","“Not for the past”—what did that mean?","Was it what she thought it meant?","Their story had started with the misunderstanding about her stealing confidential information, and Qin Xian had suddenly decided not to divorce her, and then...","Ji Fei wasn’t sure and wondered if she was overthinking it. She couldn’t help but ask, “Is it me?”","“It’s you! Only you,” Qin Xian answered firmly, his eyes reflecting Ji Fei’s tearful face.","“So, will you marry me?”","“I will!” Ji Fei nodded frantically, unable to hold back any longer.","The room erupted in cheers, with confetti, balloons, and flower petals filling the air, accompanied by thunderous applause.","In this atmosphere, Qin Xian slipped the ring onto Ji Fei’s finger—a ring made of the most expensive and valuable materials, as the rumors had said.","Ji Fei also placed a ring on Qin Xian’s finger. Before she could even admire it, Qin Xian stood up and pulled her into a deep, passionate kiss.","The day was filled with photos, blessings, and cake-cutting. Gifts and red envelopes kept coming, and Ji Fei’s smile never faded. The night ended with a bonfire party in the backyard. Meanwhile, the front square was being redecorated for the old master’s birthday celebration, which couldn’t be forgotten.","The young people gathered to sing, dance, and drink. To Ji Fei’s surprise, Yu Lu, who could have ruined the mood, was nowhere to be seen.","Qin Xian seemed exceptionally happy, drinking every toast offered to him. By the end, he was so drunk that he clung to Ji Fei like an octopus, refusing to let go.","Today, Qin Xian looked unbearably handsome, and Ji Fei couldn’t help but feel a little greedy.","A group of women pulled Ji Fei aside to dance, but really, they just wanted to gossip. They asked her when she was going to “conquer” Qin Xian.","Ji Fei talked a big game, saying she wanted to, but Qin Xian was too traditional, insisting on waiting for their wedding night. She blamed it all on him, not mentioning that she was just as nervous.","The more experienced women shook their heads in frustration, offering advice on the spot. The less experienced ones blushed, and they all encouraged Ji Fei to drink a little more—enough to boost her courage but not enough to get her drunk.","So, when the two finally returned to their room and got intimate, Ji Fei was eager to take the lead.","Qin Xian almost gave in, but at the last moment, he held Ji Fei’s hand and said, “Fei Fei, we’ve only just gotten engaged...”","Ji Fei’s face turned red, and she mustered her courage, flipping over to sit on top of Qin Xian. “I can’t wait anymore. I have no patience. I want you tonight. If I can’t have you, I’ll... I’ll...”","Ji Fei’s threat was incoherent, but Qin Xian, his eyes dark with desire, pulled her down.","“You’re testing me when my willpower is at its weakest. Then... I won’t hold back anymore.”","Ji Fei’s eyes lit up, and she bit Qin Xian’s Adam’s apple. “I won’t hold back either!”","Qin Xian groaned, his Adam’s apple bobbing, his gaze turning completely dark, like a predator in the night.","The decorated room truly felt like a bridal suite, with even the bedsheets and pillowcases in festive red. The most beautiful symphony began to play in the room, and the long night had only just started."]},{"number":437,"title":"Chapter 437: Hypnosis","paragraphs":["\"Wuwuwu...\"","Lu Meihe tugged at her daughter under the blanket. \"They are already married. Today is just a romantic ceremony. Why are you... Do you really have to have Qin Xian? By name, we are still relatives. How could you...\"","Yu Lu suddenly threw off the blanket, crying, \"You’ve always given me whatever I wanted before. Aren’t I your most beloved daughter? Besides, among the wealthy families abroad, hardly any marriages are first marriages. I’m no worse than Ji Fei. Why can’t I take him away? You saw it today—it was so grand, so romantic. Qin Xian is so outstanding, no one can compare to him.\"","Lu Meihe hesitated, \"If he weren’t married, I could have swallowed my pride and asked for an introduction for you. But now...\"","\"You won’t help me, and Dad won’t either. If only Dad would hypnotize him, he would definitely fall in love with me!\" Yu Lu shouted.","\"Your father is a professional psychologist. How could he just hypnotize someone like that?\" Lu Meihe said helplessly. \"Besides, hypnosis isn’t as magical as you think!\"","Yu Lu was about to argue that it wasn’t a big deal, especially since her father had once hypnotized her mother to help her reorganize her memories after a traumatic event. But her father had warned her never to mention this to her mother. Even though Yu Lu was willful, she didn’t dare reveal this now and swallowed her words, feeling even more wronged.","\"So what he said was true... Do I really have no chance at all? He’s so cruel. Why won’t he even look at me?\" Yu Lu couldn’t help but confide in her mother about the memory that had left her humiliated and furious.","\"Mom, do you know? A couple of nights ago, I dressed up beautifully and went to ask him for help, but he...\"","\"You went to see him in the middle of the night?\" Lu Meihe was shocked and tapped her daughter’s head. \"That’s so improper.\"","Yu Lu knew her mother wouldn’t scold her too harshly. Unlike her father, her mother was a contradictory person—strict and conservative herself but indulgent toward her daughter. Yu Lu had always felt that her mother was subconsciously compensating for something through her, which was why no matter how boldly Yu Lu pursued men, her mother never seriously reprimanded her, at most offering a few words of caution.","So Yu Lu continued to complain, \"Most men wouldn’t be able to resist! But do you know what he did? Not only did he refuse to add my contact information, but he also bluntly told me, ‘You like me? I will only ever love my wife. I will never like you. So, don’t get in our way. If you do this again, even if you bring up Grandma Lv, I won’t spare you any courtesy!’\"","\"He actually said that to me... Ugh? Mom? What’s wrong?\" Yu Lu stopped mid-sentence, noticing that Lu Meihe had gone pale and was staring blankly.","\"What did he say?\" Lu Meihe murmured.","Yu Lu repeated the words.","Lu Meihe echoed softly, \"You like me? I will only ever love my wife. I will never like you.\"","\"Yes, isn’t that so cruel?\"","But Lu Meihe repeated the words again, which struck Yu Lu as odd.","\"Mom, are you okay? Are you feeling unwell? Should I call Dad?\" Yu Lu suddenly remembered her father’s warnings and felt uneasy.","Lu Meihe, breathing heavily, waved her hand. \"No, I’m just a bit tired. I need to rest.\"","Yu Lu wanted to continue venting her frustrations, but seeing her mother’s pale face and pained expression, she grew worried. She thought about calling a doctor, but her mother stopped her.","\"I’m really tired, Lulu. Stay with me tonight. Don’t go looking for trouble.\"","With that, Lu Meihe seemed to collapse into sleep.","Yu Lu, still uneasy, sent a message to her father but received no reply. She wondered if he was already on a plane.","Meanwhile, Lu Meihe’s mind kept replaying those words.","Suddenly, a young boy’s voice echoed in her mind.","\"You like my dad? My dad will only ever love my mom. He will never like you.\"","\"You like my dad? My dad will only ever love my mom. He will never like you.\"","\"You like my dad? My dad will only ever love my mom. He will never like you.\"","...","\"Ah!!!\"","Lu Meihe suddenly sat up, startling Yu Lu awake. \"Mom?\"","Lu Meihe turned to look at her daughter, her eyes completely unlike the gentle gaze of a loving mother.","\"Mom?\" Yu Lu felt a wave of unease. Her mother’s eyes now resembled those of some of the patients who came to see her father—filled with obsession and madness.","Suddenly, Lu Meihe reached out and patted Yu Lu’s head, smiling. \"You like Qin Xian?\"","Yu Lu was taken aback but nodded nervously.","\"Then I’ll make sure Qin Xian marries you, okay?\"","Yu Lu’s heart leapt with joy, but then she frowned. \"Mom, what’s going on? Can you really do that?\"","\"He... will listen to me,\" Lu Meihe said with a cruel smile. \"I need to go to the attic to find something. If anyone asks for me, tell them I’m still sleeping, understand?\"","Yu Lu wanted to stop her mother, but Lu Meihe was already out of reach.","Yu Lu grew even more anxious. Soon, her phone rang.","\"Dad, are you almost here?\"","\"Not yet, I’m transferring flights. How’s your mom...\"","\"Dad, Mom’s acting really strange! Last night, she was fine, then suddenly she had a headache and wanted to sleep. This morning, she told me...\"","Yu Lu recounted everything, but all she heard on the other end was her father’s heavy breathing.","\"Listen, Lulu, you’re the only one who can help me now. Your mom went to the attic, right? Go up there now, lock her inside, and don’t let anyone near her until I arrive. Do you understand?\"","\"What? Dad, are you crazy?\"","\"You have to do it. Your mom... she’s sick. If anyone finds out, do you want to be known as the daughter of a madwoman? Go, now!\"","Yu Hongxian made it sound dire. Though Yu Lu didn’t fully understand what was happening, her mother’s current state frightened her more. She followed her father’s instructions and ran to the attic of the old house.","There was a staircase leading to the very top, and between the fifth floor and the roof was a small attic filled with old, unused items.","Yu Lu went up but didn’t dare enter. She listened for any sounds inside—it sounded like electronic music, which was odd. Convinced someone was inside, she decided to quietly close and lock the door.","But before she could fully shut it, the door was yanked open from the inside. Yu Lu’s heart pounded like a drum.","Before she could react, Yu Lu heard her mother's almost sinister voice, \"What a disobedient child. This is why... your parents have grown to despise you.\" As soon as Lu Meihe finished speaking, she flipped open an old-fashioned flip phone in her hand. A strange electronic melody began to play, its eerie sound echoing in the empty, silent space.","Yu Lu was stunned. What was her mother saying? \"Mom? Despise? What are you talking about? I'm your precious daughter!\"","Lu Meihe was smiling, but her eyes were chillingly cold. \"What? Did you really think your parents could love a strange child like you? Every word you say, every thing you do—it's all so annoying. They only treat you decently out of consideration for others. Don’t fool yourself into thinking anyone actually likes you! After all, you’re so... peculiar. So, shut up, be quiet, and don’t—say—a—word!\" The ringtone started again.","Yu Lu didn’t know what was happening, but suddenly her throat tightened. She felt so crushed by her mother’s belittlement and scolding that she couldn’t bring herself to speak. All she wanted to do was cry.","But the next second, a sharp pain shot through her neck, and Yu Lu was knocked unconscious."]},{"number":438,"title":"Chapter 438: Celebrating a Birthday","paragraphs":["Ji Fei was in a daze when she heard the impatient knocking at the door.","The warmth enveloping her disappeared, followed by the sound of the door opening.","\"Please, it's already eleven! Today is the birthday banquet! The feast is about to start. Even though we understand the sweetness of your recent engagement and your siblings are willing to handle all the guests for you, you can't just skip the luncheon! Everyone is here first for the banquet, and second, for you. You have to show up! Wait... don't tell me you haven't slept yet!\"","Ji Fei only felt the noise was overwhelming. Soon, the sound of the door closing came, and a low, husky voice whispered in her ear.","\"Fei Fei, it's time to go out. I'll bring you back later.\"","Ji Fei was truly afraid of the sound of breathing near her ear and Qin Xian's low, husky voice. It meant that someone hadn't had enough and wanted more. She really didn't want to continue; she felt like she was going to die!","Annoyed, she waved her hand, trying to push him away, but he kissed her palm instead.","\"I love you, Fei Fei.\"","Shortly after, the room fell silent again. Qin Xian had gone into the bathroom.","Ji Fei felt like she had only slept for a short while.","In her daze, she felt uneasy all over. When she finally realized what had happened, her face gradually turned red, and she couldn't help but cover her face with her hands, letting out a silent scream.","She had no idea how the night had passed, but she remembered that even at dawn, Qin Xian's low, teasing voice was still in her ear.","He usually doted on her and almost always gave in to her requests, but this time, no matter how much she pleaded for him to stop, it was useless.","He was... he was... completely unrestrained! It was really too much!","Now her back and waist were sore~ Huh? Wait, it didn't hurt as much as she thought. Oh, right, she remembered—Qin Xian had just helped her massage earlier.","When Qin Xian came out, he saw his wife with a bright red face, her fair shoulders marked with his kisses. His eyes darkened as he walked over, hugged her, and kissed her ear.","\"Fei Fei, it's time to freshen up. I'll carry you.\"","Seeing Qin Xian's grinning face, Ji Fei really wanted to throw a tantrum, but she felt too embarrassed, especially since she had been the one to start things last night.","\"No, I can do it myself. You get dressed first!\"","But as soon as she finished speaking, Ji Fei's legs gave out halfway, and she sat back down. Although her waist was fine, her legs clearly weren't up to the task yet!","A pleasant laugh sounded in her ear. Ji Fei glared at him unhappily, only to be scooped up in his strong arms.","He carried her straight to the bathroom sink, then half-held, half-carried her as he personally helped her brush her teeth and wash her face.","Ji Fei felt like a baby, but the man in the mirror looked quite amused and seemed to be enjoying himself. She hoped this wouldn't turn into some strange habit.","Looking back at the mirror, she confirmed it—she could only wear pants and long sleeves today to cover the marks. She was too embarrassed to face anyone.","In the end, Qin Xian even helped her put on her shoes before supporting her as she stood up.","\"Just hold on for a little while. After we pay our respects at the birthday celebration, I'll bring you back so you can rest. You can eat after you wake up.\"","Ji Fei leaned against Qin Xian's embrace as they walked, trying to get used to her newly \"installed\" legs.","\"I'll probably have to stay for the entire luncheon. After it's over, I'll find time to come back and keep you company. You only need to come out for the evening banquet.\"","\"Do I not have to socialize?\"","Qin Xian smiled. \"I promised you before—as my wife, you can do whatever you want. You don't have to engage in social obligations or take on responsibilities. You just need to be yourself and stay by my side.\"","Ji Fei couldn't help but smile. It was the confidence that came from being indulged. But she wondered if Qin Xian's lack of principles would spoil her.","\"But what about the elders...\" Ji Fei struggled to find a reason to insist.","\"At least for today, Grandpa, Dad, and Mom will understand. After all, it's my fault...\" Qin Xian said, gently nibbling her ear.","Ji Fei almost lost her balance again. \"Stop messing around! Are you even Qin Xian anymore? Where's your usual demeanor?\"","\"What demeanor?\"","\"You know, being a bit more aloof.\"","\"Why should I be aloof with my own wife?\"","Even as they walked, Qin Xian clung to Ji Fei from behind. \"Wife, I'm so happy. Really, if only we didn't have to deal with those people outside... I just want to stay with you and never leave the house.\"","\"No, no, no, it's better if you go out,\" Ji Fei immediately protested, alarmed.","Qin Xian gave her a dissatisfied look. \"So Fei Fei didn't like how I was last night? Then I'll...\"","Ji Fei thought he would say he'd be more restrained, but instead, she heard Qin Xian say, word by word, \"Then I'll practice more until my wife likes it.\"","[No need for that! I want to live a few more years!]","Qin Xian burst out laughing.","\"Let's go. Time to collect Grandpa's red envelope.\"","At the mention of this, Ji Fei's eyes lit up.","The youngest head of the Qin family made his first public appearance, leaving the guests who had arrived early waiting for quite some time.","It wasn't until the younger generation began paying their respects that the couple finally made their entrance.","Arm in arm, they stepped into the spotlight, drawing everyone's attention.","Qin Xian was as calm as ever, while Ji Fei, thoroughly exhausted from the night's events, also appeared relaxed.","Despite their youth, neither showed any sign of nervousness.","Whispers began to spread among the crowd, recalling the proposal ceremony from the previous day. It was clear that even though Ji Fei no longer had a family to rely on, her status was still extraordinary, at least within the Qin family.","Qin Xian led Ji Fei to stand in line with his siblings.","The others exchanged teasing glances, their smiles filled with hidden meanings. Even Ji Fei couldn't help but lower her head under their gaze.","Among the elders, Qin's Father and Qin's Mom were beaming, clearly delighted and not at all concerned about the couple's late arrival.","At that moment, Grandma Lv couldn't help but inform everyone, \"Little Mei and Lu Lu went to pick up their father, but they're stuck in traffic and won't make it back in time. Let's proceed with the birthday wishes without delay. They can pay their respects to Grandpa later.\"","No one seemed to mind, as they were stepchildren and had grown more distant after marriage. The guests didn't pay much attention either.","Once the auspicious time arrived, everyone stepped forward in order to kneel and offer their blessings."]},{"number":439,"title":"Chapter 439: Lü Meihe, Yu Hongxian, You Deserve to Die","paragraphs":["When Ji Fei and Qin Xian knelt down to speak, Grandpa laughed the most joyfully. Ji Fei couldn't help but wonder if it was because they were the only couple among the grandchildren.","After Ji Fei received her big red envelope, Qin Xian handed his own envelope to her. Before the guests could swarm around them, he quickly whisked Ji Fei away, grabbing some food and drinks on the way.","As they walked, Ji Fei noticed they hadn’t run into any familiar faces. Curious, she asked, “Where are the others?”","“Your friends from the studio, along with Ruan Jia and Chu Xinyue, still have work to do, so they couldn’t attend the birthday banquet. They left this morning, and Qin Zhao saw them off. The rest are still here, but they’ll manage on their own. No need to worry.”","After escorting Ji Fei back to her room, Qin Xian planted a gentle kiss on her forehead and gazed at her tenderly. “Get some rest. I’ll come back to you soon.”","“Aren’t you tired?” Ji Fei was already feeling a bit dizzy.","“I can go a full day and night without sleep.”","Ji Fei thought to herself, *I know Qin Xian is in great shape and has more stamina than most, but why does that sound so dangerous?*","Indeed, Qin Xian still looked radiant and full of energy—perhaps even happier than ever. Meanwhile, Ji Fei felt like she was about to collapse from exhaustion.","Her face flushed, and she secretly cursed, *Greedy jerk! Always bullying me!*","She quickly waved him off, but Qin Xian still heard her. He pulled her close and kissed her passionately before reluctantly leaving her side. “I *am* greedy,” he said with a smirk.","Ji Fei was utterly exhausted. She usually needed more sleep than most people, and the sight of the bed was too tempting. She didn’t even bother changing her clothes or eating the snacks Qin Xian had left for her. She simply flopped onto the bed and fell into a deep sleep.","After leaving, Qin Xian headed to the banquet hall to host the birthday celebration. He moved through the crowd with ease, exuding confidence and charm.","Qin's Father and Qin's Mom couldn’t help but notice that Qin Xian seemed to have changed a bit since proposing.","However, as time passed, Qin Xian began to feel uneasy. He sensed a malicious gaze fixed on him, sending a chill down his spine.","The longer he stayed, the more uncomfortable he became. All he wanted was to return to Ji Fei, to be where she was.","After excusing himself from some lingering guests, Qin Xian hurried through the corridor, eager to leave.","“Second Brother? Leaving already?”","“Yes.”","Qin Zhao watched Qin Xian with amusement. *Is he really in such a hurry?*","But as Qin Xian passed the staircase, a faint, old-fashioned phone ringtone echoed from above. The sound seemed to drain all the strength from his body.","As if in a trance, Qin Xian stepped onto the stairs.","Ji Fei didn’t know how long she had been asleep, but she felt like she was trapped in a nightmare. Suddenly, her heart skipped a beat, as if jolted by an electric shock. She woke up in a panic, though she couldn’t remember what had frightened her.","Checking the time, she was shocked to see it was already 4 PM.","Ji Fei quickly freshened up and tried to contact Qin Xian, but he didn’t respond. She then reached out to the family group chat.","Qin's Father: “Awake?”","Qin's Mom: “Hungry?”","Eldest Sister: “Don’t worry, everything’s fine.”","Third Brother: “Where’s Brother? Didn’t he come find you?”","Fourth Sister: “Sis-in-law, you can sleep a bit more.”","This family was so reassuring!","“No, I’m up. I’ll come over.”","Since she was awake, she couldn’t keep lazing around. Otherwise, she’d feel guilty about not fulfilling her role as the lady of the house.","Most importantly... she missed Qin Xian terribly. She had an inexplicable urge to see him right away.","After tidying up, she stepped outside. Many guests were still relaxing in the square, and they greeted her warmly as she passed. Ji Fei responded with polite smiles.","As she approached the residence, she heard the sound of a car pulling up behind her. It seemed another guest had just arrived.","“Huh? Strange, where’s my brother? Why are you alone?” Qin Zhao approached, looking puzzled.","Ji Fei was taken aback. “He hasn’t come back. Wasn’t he busy entertaining the guests?”","Qin Zhao frowned. “No, he was heading back to you an hour ago. Did someone stop him along the way?”","“What?” Ji Fei’s heart sank.","Qin Zhao tried calling Qin Xian, but there was no answer. “Never mind. You go find Rongrong. I’ll look for Second Brother so you don’t have to run around.”","With that, Qin Zhao left.","Ji Fei knew she wasn’t as quick on her feet as Qin Zhao, so she didn’t argue. As she looked around, her mind began to wander, and she thought of Yu Lu. After all, that woman had once declared she would win Qin Xian’s heart. Could she be behind this?","Just as Ji Fei was about to look into Yu Lu, someone rushed in and bumped into her. The person apologized quickly before darting inside.","Ji Fei looked up and saw a middle-aged man, looking travel-worn, approach Grandma Lv and ask her something.","Ji Fei instinctively guessed the man’s identity. *Could he be Yu Hongxian?*","She quickly searched for information and was overwhelmed by a flood of details that nearly made her head explode.","As Yu Hongxian hurried away, Ji Fei’s pupils contracted. She followed him without thinking, unable to let his figure disappear from her sight.","Her inner voice exploded, echoing in the minds of everyone who could hear her thoughts.","[*It’s him. It’s them! They’re the ones who hurt Qin Xian!*]","The revelation struck like a thunderclap, instantly darkening the faces of Qin’s family. They stopped their cheerful conversations, rose from their seats, and quickly gathered together, disregarding the guests around them.","Qin Zhao was the last to join. “I was just talking to Second Sister-in-law, but I went to look for Second Brother. I don’t know where she went now.”","Qin's Father said firmly, “Don’t panic. Listen!”","[*It was hypnosis. Lu Meihe was hypnotized, her memories altered and hidden. That’s why I couldn’t find anything!*]","The Qin family’s faces turned ashen.","So it was...","[*Lu Meihe, Yu Hongxian, you deserve to die!*]","The Qin family’s expressions shifted dramatically, especially Qin's Father and Qin's Mom. They had always blamed themselves for not protecting Qin Xian well enough, never imagining that someone had deliberately harmed him.","But in the next moment, Qin's Father nearly broke down.","Through Ji Fei’s inner voice, everyone finally learned the truth of what had happened all those years ago."]},{"number":440,"title":"Chapter 440: The Truth of That Year","paragraphs":["Lu Meihe became a quasi-young mistress because her mother married into the family she had long served. However, her upbringing in such an environment made her insecure and sensitive, always feeling like an outsider. Her mother constantly reminded her to be content, grateful, and to know her place.","Being too young to fully grasp the concept of boundaries, Lu Meihe often felt anxious and out of place in the Qin Family. One rainy night, she got lost in the woods near the old estate. Too afraid to call for help, she tried to find her way out on her own, not wanting to trouble the Qin Family. Eventually, overwhelmed by panic, she broke down in tears.","At her most vulnerable moment, Qin's Father found her with a flashlight and an umbrella, carrying her back home.","For the young girl, that moment was both salvation and the beginning of her infatuation. It also became her breakthrough into the Qin Family, and gradually, she became the most beloved \"youngest daughter\" of the household. Yet, her eyes and heart always followed Qin's Father.","As she grew older and entered adolescence, the other brothers in the family began to develop feelings for her. Grandma Lv noticed this and repeatedly, albeit hesitantly, reminded Lu Meihe to maintain boundaries. Though her words were subtle, Lu Meihe understood. Grandma Lv, still carrying a sense of servility, believed her daughter was unworthy of the young masters, thinking they would eventually marry women of equal social standing. She warned Lu Meihe not to overstep, lest she be seen as ungrateful.","In that moment, Lu Meihe's unrequited love had nowhere to go. She realized that Qin's Father, whom she had secretly admired, was even more unattainable.","But who can control matters of the heart? Just as she was mustering the courage to confess, Qin's Father met Qin's Mom. Desperate, Lu Meihe impulsively confessed her feelings, only to see shock and disbelief in Qin's Father's eyes. To him, the age gap and their familial roles made such feelings unthinkable.","The shame from that look shattered her composure, and all the insecurities she had suppressed came rushing back. She began to question herself, wondering if there was something wrong with her.","Unable to face Qin's Father, who now awkwardly avoided her, or Qin's Mom, who visited the house with her beauty and grace, Lu Meihe felt like a clown. To distract herself, she turned to the internet, researching whether her attraction to someone so much older, and technically a brother figure, was a sign of illness. She noticed that the brothers who once seemed interested in her now treated her purely as a sister. They had moved on, but she hadn't. She convinced herself that she must be the one with the problem.","During her research, she met Yu Hongxian. Lu Meihe immediately saw an opportunity to ease her embarrassment by pretending to have an online romance, explaining to Qin's Father that her feelings were merely a \"brother complex.\" This allowed her to revert to her role as a sister in his eyes.","Yu Hongxian, thinking she was just a young girl interested in psychology, enjoyed discussing the subject with her. He recommended books and introduced her to more advanced topics, such as psychological suggestion, mental manipulation, and hypnosis.","Unbeknownst to him, his discussions planted dangerous seeds. The knowledge she gained seemed to offer a solution: she began using self-hypnosis to suppress her feelings for Qin's Father, believing this would allow her to live a normal life.","Later, when Qin's Father married and had children, Lu Meihe could smile and offer her blessings. No one noticed her secret.","However, the delicate balance began to crumble with the birth of Qin Xian, Qin's Father's second son and a child prodigy.","At first, Lu Meihe genuinely cared for Qin Xian, loving him as an extension of her affection for Qin's Father. The Qin Family often spoke of how Qin Xian's genius would be Qin's Father's greatest pride. Though Qin's Father treated all his children equally, outsiders believed that Qin Xian's success would bring immense benefits to the family. Lu Meihe often helped care for and tutor him, further solidifying her role in the family.","But everything changed with one sentence.","\"You like my dad? My dad will only ever love my mom. He will never love you.\"","These words, spoken by a child too young to fully understand social nuances but perceptive enough to see through her, shattered the fragile lock on her suppressed emotions.","In that moment, Lu Meihe began to hate Qin Xian with an intensity she had never known. She had been willing to live a lie, even forgetting her own heartbreak, but Qin Xian had exposed her deepest, most painful secret.","Why did he have to see it? Why did he have to say it? Was it fun to tear open old wounds? Just because he was a genius?","He was right, though. Qin's Father would never love her. The thought filled her with unbearable frustration. If she couldn't have him, then she would destroy what he cherished most. She decided to ruin Qin Xian, the child Qin's Father was most proud of.","Under the guise of a caring aunt, Lu Meihe subjected Qin Xian to three years of psychological abuse. She constantly belittled, mocked, and undermined his achievements. She slowly killed each of his pets. The final month wasn't spent at a foreign summer camp, as the family believed, but in complete isolation. Qin Xian was confined to a dark room, alone, with no sound, no human contact, and only food and water. For thirty days, the young boy did nothing but eat, sleep, and relieve himself.","The entire Qin Family was oblivious, believing Lu Meihe was doing her best for Qin Xian.","It wasn't until Yu Hongxian grew suspicious of Lu Meihe's frequent inquiries—which sounded too much like real-life cases—that the truth began to unravel. After discovering Grandpa Qin's plea for help, Yu Hongxian visited the Qin Family and met Lu Meihe and the severely autistic Qin Xian. Piecing together the truth, he realized Lu Meihe also suffered from severe mental illness.","Despite this, Yu Hongxian couldn't bring himself to abandon her. He loved her and chose to help her cover up her crimes. After treatment, Qin Xian forgot the abuse he had endured, his memories fragmented. The autism caused by the trauma was beyond Yu Hongxian's ability to treat, so he shifted the blame to Qin Xian's parents, claiming their neglect and his genius were the reasons for his condition.","Yu Hongxian believed no other psychologist would uncover the truth. After all, only he and his mentor possessed the skill to use hypnosis at such a level. No one would ever know Qin Xian had been hypnotized to forget.","Using this as leverage, Yu Hongxian forced Lu Meihe to marry him and took her away for hypnotic treatment, hoping to give her a chance at a normal life.","[How dare they! How dare such monsters deserve a normal life when even Qin Xian hasn't recovered... I'll kill these two!]","Ji Fei's inner voice was almost choked with tears.","Meanwhile, the Qin Family was in chaos. Qin Yan and Qin Rong were sobbing uncontrollably, while Qin Zhao cursed incessantly. Qin's Father, overwhelmed with grief, collapsed to his knees, weeping openly, even with guests present.","\"Qin's Father, stay strong, it's not your fault, it's not!\" Qin's Mom quickly said, \"It's their fault, they harmed Qin Xian! We can't let Ji Fei face this alone. We must go! Forget everything else, we must avenge our son!\"","\"By the way, Second Brother, Second Brother is missing. Could something have happened to him?\" Qin Zhao immediately shouted, \"Has anyone seen my Second Brother and his wife?\"","Those who had come upon hearing the news could only see that the entire Qin Family was in disarray.","Someone tried to approach and ask questions, but Qin Zhao lashed out in anger.","Finally, one by one, people began to share what they had witnessed.","They only saw them going upstairs, but no one knew exactly where they had gone."]},{"number":441,"title":"Chapter 441: Finale Part 01","paragraphs":["After learning what Qin Xian had endured in his childhood, Ji Fei felt as though her heart was bleeding with pain, and anger robbed her of all reason.","[How dare these people show their faces before Qin Xian again? How could their daughter have the audacity to fall for him...]","Lost in her fury, Ji Fei chased after them to the top floor when suddenly, she saw Yu Hongxian stop ahead—and at his feet lay Yu Lu, unconscious.","\"Lulu!\" Yu Hongxian screamed in terror.","Ji Fei froze in her tracks as an old-fashioned phone ringtone abruptly pierced the air. Turning her head, she spotted a half-open attic door—the sound was coming from inside.","Her heart clenched as if seized by an invisible hand.","The space within was dim and lifeless...","[This was where Qin Xian had been imprisoned as a child...]","That final month, everyone had thought Qin Xian was sent to summer camp, but in reality, Lu Meihe had intercepted him midway, stuffed him into a suitcase, and smuggled him back to the old house, locking him in the attic. Though it was the closest place to home, he had been trapped there for an entire month, isolated and tormented. By the time Lu Meihe took him out again, Qin Xian had completely shut himself off, unable to communicate normally with anyone. A rising star had been ruthlessly dragged into darkness.","Ji Fei pushed open the door—and her pupils shrank in horror.","There, leaning against the far wall near an old wooden window, sat Qin Xian. His empty eyes stared blankly outside while his arms wrapped around his knees. Though a tall, grown man, he now looked like a helpless child on the verge of vanishing.","\"Qin Xian...\" Ji Fei’s voice trembled as she rushed toward him.","Qin Xian flinched. It was as though he were submerged in a pitch-black, freezing lake—so cold, so heavy, as if everything in the world had drifted far away from him. But this feeling... was all too familiar.","Whispers echoed endlessly in his ears:","*\"Aren’t you supposed to be a genius? You can’t even do this?\"*","*\"If you keep this up, your parents will be so disappointed.\"*","*\"No wonder your parents abandoned you.\"*","*\"You won’t tattle, right? After all, I’m only telling the truth.\"*","*\"I’m doing this for your own good. You’re just... that pathetic.\"*","*\"You... are a freak that everyone despises.\"*","*\"Don’t speak. Everyone hates you. They wish you’d just disappear.\"*","The ringing continued...","If he stayed silent, avoided communication, and sealed his heart away—maybe then, he wouldn’t be hated.","People around him were always crying, their eyes filled with sorrow and frustration. It was all his fault. He shouldn’t exist at all.","......","*\"Big brother is so handsome! Qin Xian?\"*","*\"Qin Xian... Qin Xian... Qin Xian... I only like Qin Xian... I want to be with Qin Xian forever...\"*","......","\"Qin Xian! Qin Xian! It’s me—wake up!\"","Qin Xian’s lashes fluttered, and a flicker of light returned to his pupils, reflecting Ji Fei’s face.","[Why is Qin Xian like this? It must be Lu Meihe’s doing. Where is she now?]","Ji Fei thought—if Lu Meihe was responsible, then the hypnosis must have been lifted. Maybe she could check her condition.","But the next second, all Ji Fei saw was a blank void. Even the previously altered information had disappeared.","Had she gone completely insane?","Ji Fei’s instincts screamed in alarm, and she whipped her head around—","Just in time to see Lu Meihe swinging a large bucket toward her.","\"If you die, Qin Xian will belong to my daughter! If I couldn’t fulfill my wish, then my daughter will!\"","[You crazy bitch!]","Ji Fei cursed and tried to lunge at her, convinced she could overpower this madwoman.","But before she could move, Lu Meihe twisted her wrist—flipping the bucket upside down.","A pungent, unmistakable stench filled the air as liquid splashed onto Ji Fei.","[Gasoline!]","Drenched from head to toe, Ji Fei stared in disbelief at Lu Meihe.","[Is she trying to kill me?!]","Sure enough, Lu Meihe pulled out a lighter—*click*—and a flame burst to life.","Ji Fei’s blood ran cold. Not only was she soaked, but gasoline had also splattered across the floor like a fuse. In this narrow attic, escape was nearly impossible.","Then—a shadow darted in front of her.","Tears welled in Ji Fei’s eyes.","Qin Xian. He had snapped out of it.","\"So you *did* recover? I thought I had completely shattered your psyche back then. How tenacious of you—to break free from my hypnosis so easily.\" Lu Meihe sneered.","\"Because I found my savior.\" Qin Xian’s voice shook, but his heart bled with regret. If only he had truly healed, Lu Meihe wouldn’t have exploited his weakness to hypnotize and control him again—nor would Ji Fei be in danger now.","\"Feifei, I’m sorry. I dragged you into this.\"","Ji Fei longed to throw herself into his arms, but the gasoline covering her made her hesitate.","\"If you hate me, take it out on me. Don’t hurt anyone else.\" Qin Xian’s eyes locked onto the flame in Lu Meihe’s hand. He knew this woman was a lunatic, capable of anything.","Though Qin Xian was strong enough to overpower her, the slightest misstep—even if Lu Meihe merely flicked the lighter—could ignite the gasoline on Ji Fei in an instant. He wouldn’t risk it.","He would rather beg on his knees, trade his own life—anything to keep Ji Fei safe.","The fire danced mockingly in Lu Meihe’s grip, taunting them.","\"All these years I’ve been in the shadows, and yet you thrived—successful career, happy family, even your mind healed. *Why?* I was supposed to ruin you! How dare you live so well?!\"","Lu Meihe couldn’t comprehend it. Some things defied logic.","With the hypnosis broken, Qin Xian remembered everything. Three years of relentless psychological torture—yet Ji Fei had cracked his shell in just three days with her warmth. Without her, he might have ended his own life long ago.","While others tiptoed around him, treating him like fragile glass, Ji Fei—bright, bold, and unafraid—had barged into his world like sunlight, showering him with affection and praise. She had flung open the doors he’d locked shut.","A twist of fate. A stroke of luck.","Now, hearing Lu Meihe’s deranged words, Ji Fei’s blood boiled. Even in this perilous state, she couldn’t hold back. \"You—! All of this because Qin Xian exposed your sick obsession? You’re a goddamn psychopath!\"","She didn’t care if she revealed too much—she glared furiously at Lu Meihe. \"You’re a twisted, sick monster!\"","Maybe provoking her was unwise. But knowing what Qin Xian had suffered over something so trivial, Ji Fei couldn’t stay silent. She needed to scream, to curse—anything to expel the rage choking her chest.","Qin Xian tensed instantly, his arms moving reflexively behind him as if to shield someone, only to realize there was no one there to protect.","In that moment, he understood—Ji Fei was afraid of dragging him down...","“Hahaha, that’s right! I *am* a deranged psychopath! Obsessed with my own brother to the point of madness. But I hid it so well! I could’ve been a good aunt—*he* ruined it! He mocked me, tore off my mask, forced me back into being the monster I am! It’s *his* fault he destroyed me, so I’ll destroy him. Fair, isn’t it?” Lu Meihe snarled, her face twisted with rage.","“What I said back then... it wasn’t what you thought,” Qin Xian said, forcing his voice into something calm and placating. “I was too young to understand. I just saw you... suffering. I only wanted to tell you not to torture yourself over my father. To let go of what could never be and find happiness.”","Even as a child, when Aunt Lu had cared for him, Qin Xian couldn’t have harbored malice toward her. His intentions had been pure—but a heart steeped in darkness twists even light into shadows. She’d been searching for an excuse, a reason to shatter the chains of morality, and his words had handed it to her.","Lu Meihe was the kind to double down on her path of destruction. What began as petty cruelty spiraled until she unleashed her bitterness and resentment on a helpless Qin Xian, finding perverse solace in his suffering.","So even now, as Qin Xian spoke the truth, Lu Meihe shook her head, sneering.","“You think I’d believe that? No. You ruined me, and now you’ll pay. My daughter wants you—so you *will* be with her. As for this one you love...” Her lips curled into a chilling smile. “You know how this goes. Every living thing you’ve ever cherished—the goldfish, the parrot, the rabbits, the cat—I made sure they died. And now, I’ll take *this one* too.”","“If you hate me, then kill *me*,” Qin Xian demanded urgently.","“Killing you? Where’s the fun in that? I want you to suffer like I did. That’s the *real* punishment.”","A sudden creak of wood made Lu Meihe snap to attention. She flicked open her lighter, pressing her back against a support beam to keep both flanks in view. One wrong move, and she’d hurl the flame without hesitation.","“Wife... please. There’s no coming back from this,” Yu Hongxian pleaded, his voice trembling with tears. He’d covered for her crimes before, but murder? That was a line even he couldn’t erase.","“*You*—!” Lu Meihe whirled on him, eyes blazing. “You *hypnotized* me! You *raped* me! I never loved you, never *could*! You’re nothing but a predator!”","Yu Hongxian paled. “All these years... none of it meant anything to you? If you’d just let yourself *feel*, you might have—”","Lu Meihe’s derisive laugh cut him off, her gaze so icy it nearly knocked him to his knees.","Done with delays, she raised the lighter. “Qin Xian, step back. I’d hate to scar you—Auntie still cares, you know.”","“STOP!” A hoarse shout rang out.","Lu Meihe froze.","“Meihe, *please*—don’t hurt them. I’m begging you, as your brother!”","Qin Xian and Ji Fei turned to see Qin’s Father on his knees in the doorway, tears streaking his weathered face.","Lu Meihe shuddered—but her grip on the lighter didn’t waver. “*No one moves!*” she barked. “One step, and the girl dies *now*!”","The crowd at the door stiffened; even Qin’s Father stayed rooted in place.","“Meihe, if you need vengeance, take it from *me*,” he whispered. “I’m their father. Let me bear this.”","“It was never your fault. I don’t love you anymore, but... there’s no turning back.” Her voice was eerily calm, but her eyes burned with desperation. If today ended in blood, she’d make sure *someone* paid.","Madness had long since eroded her logic. If Qin’s Father hadn’t chosen Qin’s Mother, she’d have had her chance. Now, if Ji Fei was gone, her daughter could claim Qin Xian. Never mind that she’d tormented him, or that she’d doom her own child by becoming a murderer.","Reality didn’t matter—only her warped resolve.","Qin Xian knew words were useless. They needed a plan, but one misstep would set everything ablaze.","*[What do we do? We have to save ourselves... At the very least, I can’t let others get hurt. I need to make Qin Xian leave.]*","Qin Xian’s eyes flickered. “I’m *not* leaving you,” he murmured. “Not ever.”","Ji Fei startled.","“We’ll figure this out *together*,” he continued. “You’re not ‘dragging me down.’ I’m with you—live or die. So *stop* trying to push me away.”","Ji Fei gaped. *[Is he... reading my mind?]*","Qin Xian almost smiled. “Call it intuition. The whole family has it. So *think*, Feifei. As hard as you can.”","Before Ji Fei could process that, Lu Meihe scoffed. “Pathetic last words. Qin Xian, *move*. Unless you want your pretty face melted off—my daughter *does* have standards.”","Instead, Qin Xian reached back, yanking Ji Fei against him in a crushing embrace. Gasoline soaked into his clothes.","“*Ah!*” Ji Fei gasped—but then she met his gaze. Steady. Unshakable. She gave a tiny nod.","“You *want* to die together?” Lu Meihe hissed.","*[If they can really hear me... the best shot is a fire extinguisher.]*","Ji Fei spotted Qin Rong and Qin Yan at the door, each clutching an extinguisher—but they didn’t dare step in. The distance was too great; by the time they’d act, the flames would already be on her.","“Too slow,” Qin Xian said flatly.","“*What?*” Lu Meihe frowned.","But Ji Fei understood. Following his glance, she saw it—the window behind them. Old, brittle, barely holding together.","*[Jump before the fire hits? But it’s four stories! Unless... a safety net? An inflatable—like those playground bounce pads!]*","Qin Xian nodded.","*[Someone needs to set it up—FAST!]*","Ji Fei seemed to hear commotion downstairs, along with Qin Zhao’s furious shouts. Her heart pounded like a drum. If this failed...","She knew Qin Xian had considered every possible plan. He had exchanged glances with his father—perhaps to subdue Lu Meihe, or maybe use a fire extinguisher. As a last resort, jumping from the window. Everything would depend on the moment.","Then, suddenly, a voice rang out. “Daughter, what are you doing? Stop this! How could you harm the young mistress’s children!” Grandma Lv’s horrified cry pierced the air.","Lu Meihe’s eyes glazed over instantly. Before anyone could react, she flung the lighter to the ground.","Time seemed to slow in that heartbeat.","Qin's Father lunged for the lighter but couldn’t reach it. A fire extinguisher sprayed too late, unable to outpace the flames erupting across the floor.","As the fire raced toward Ji Fei’s feet, a deafening *crash* echoed.","Qin Xian, clutching Ji Fei, shattered the window and plummeted downward.","Tears streamed past Ji Fei’s face as she felt their positions flip mid-air—his arms shielding her completely. She clung to him, her hands tightening around the man who enveloped her in protection.","Had they truly heard right? Were there cushions below? Was everything ready?","Her heart pleaded.","[*System, oh Reapers of the Underworld, spirits of all realms—I beg you, don’t let us come to harm. Please. I want to live. To grow old with Qin Xian.*]","The weightlessness gripped her. Then—a searing heat in her chest, a burst of agony in her skull, as if a flood of memories tore through her mind."]},{"number":442,"title":"Chapter 442: Final Chapter (Part 2)","paragraphs":["Ji Fei remembered many, many things—it felt like two lifetimes.","She had parents who adored her. She was once the pampered little princess of the Ji family. She had met Qin Xian before, but she was too young at the time and later forgot about him.","Life had been wonderful until she turned fifteen, when a car accident took her parents away and left her alone.","She nearly died that day. It was then that she saw the so-called Messenger from the Underworld.","The messenger told her to go back. She watched as her parents were led away, desperately trying to call out to them.","Then, it seemed a higher-ranking official appeared. He held a brush, marking a ledger as he murmured, \"You survived because you are destined by fate. In the future, you are meant to marry a man of immense fortune in this world. You will help him and those around him, and their influence will greatly impact this world. That’s why you can return to life.\"","\"What about my parents?\"","\"Their sins are grave. They must endure suffering in their next life to atone.\"","\"That’s impossible! My parents were good people—\"","\"They *were* good people, but this accident was caused by one of them drunk driving and the other ordering the driver to run a red light. Do you know how many lives were lost in that chain collision? How many families were torn apart? If not for the charity they’d done in their lives, the karma they’ve accrued would have taken them three lifetimes to repay. A single lifetime is already lenient.\"","\"I’m sorry... It’s all my fault. I was the one who suddenly fell ill, on the verge of shock, and my parents... Punish me instead, not them!\"","The messenger sighed. \"There *is* another way. In another world, a couple with abundant virtue wishes to exchange fate with their daughter, who died young. If you agree to give up your identity to her and endure a life of loneliness in that world, your parents’ sins will be absolved, and they can be reborn into ordinary families.\"","For Ji Fei, there was no hesitation. She agreed immediately and signed the contract.","Thus began what she thought was her life as an orphan.","But this life wasn’t supposed to end so soon.","The unauthorized exchange of fates disrupted the balance of this world.","Simply put, the man meant to inherit great fortune—Qin Xian—never fell in love with the replacement.","The replacement, aware of Ji Fei’s destined fate, tried relentlessly to make Qin Xian love her, only to push him further away. She also failed to connect with the others she was meant to influence.","Gradually, the role Ji Fei was supposed to play remained unfulfilled. She neither saved Qin Xian nor altered the fates of those she was meant to change. By the time the higher authorities noticed the growing imbalance, they urgently recalled the real Ji Fei.","The so-called Gossip System and mind-reading abilities were actually tools provided by the Messengers from the Underworld to help her catch up to the intended timeline.","Now, everything had finally aligned, and the world stabilized.","The system and mind-reading abilities had transformed into one last surge of power—no, *two*—to protect something precious to Ji Fei.","......","In the quiet hospital room, the sheer curtains fluttered in the breeze, the cool air brushing over Ji Fei’s trembling lashes. The man who had been staring at her in quiet devotion felt his heart surge with hope—only to ache again when her lashes stilled.","\"Fei Fei... when will you wake up? I...\"","The door creaked open.","Qin's Father and Qin's Mom entered, followed by Qin Yan, Qin Zhao, and Qin Rong, all carrying supplies. Their expressions softened with pity when they saw Qin Xian still keeping vigil by the bed.","A month had passed since the fall. Though the bouncy castle had cushioned her landing and spared her from the flames, Ji Fei had slipped into an inexplicable coma.","Qin Xian had abandoned everything else, devoting himself to her bedside day and night.","\"Brother, it’s time for lunch. Go rest—we’ll stay with Sister-in-law,\" Qin Rong urged gently.","Qin Yan unpacked food containers on the side table while Qin Zhao moved to close the window—the wind was picking up.","Qin's Father looked haggard, but Qin's Mom guided him to sit, chatting softly to Ji Fei and Qin Xian.","\"We just heard—Lu Meihe is dead. Grandma Lv, heartbroken, took Yu Lu away. The poor girl is still traumatized, her mind broken. Your grandfather didn’t stop them. He only said... he failed you. Yu Hongxian is in prison. I doubt he’ll last long there.\"","Qin Xian showed no reaction.","That day, after they jumped, Lu Meihe had lunged toward them in disbelief—only to stumble into the flames. She hadn’t died instantly but suffered a month of agony from her burns. As for Yu Hongxian, Qin Xian had already been investigating him. His team had uncovered evidence of his unethical hypnosis practices, though they hadn’t secured it yet. After the incident, those very charges sent Yu Hongxian to prison.","Strangely, Qin Xian had even pulled strings to keep Lu Meihe alive—though no one could tell whether he wanted her to live or die. By all accounts, her injuries were fatal, yet he had forced her to endure that torment for a full month.","The matter was settled, but Qin Xian felt nothing. He simply lifted Ji Fei’s hand, rubbing his stubbled jaw against her fingers—","Then, a soft murmur: *\"That tickles...\"*","The room froze.","Qin Xian went rigid. Her lashes fluttered again—this time, unmistakably—before her eyes slowly opened, meeting his.","\"Your beard... it’s scratching my hand.\"","Gasps filled the room.","\"Fei Fei!\" \"Second Sister-in-law!\" Voices overlapped in joyous disbelief.","But Qin Xian couldn’t speak. Tears blurred his vision as he choked back sobs.","Then, the hand in his grip twitched.","He instantly leaned closer, pressing his forehead to hers.","Though hoarse, Ji Fei’s voice was bright with energy. \"I remember now. You’re my Qin Xian. You promised to marry me. Did I wake up too late? Is our wedding date still good?\"","Qin Xian laughed through his tears, kissing her softly. \"Fei Fei... thank you. Thank you for coming back to me. Promise me—never leave again.\"","\"Then shave first. I like my men handsome,\" she teased playfully.","The entire room burst into relieved laughter.","Ji Fei turned to the others. \"Mom, Dad, Sister Qin Yan, Qin Zhao, Qin Rong—thank you.\"","She was grateful to this family. They had given her a new home.","\"Silly child,\" Qin's Mom sniffled, clasping Ji Fei’s other hand.","Qin's Father’s voice cracked. \"I’m sorry... this is all my fault.\"","\"Don’t say that. It was never your fault,\" Ji Fei said firmly.","Then she looked back at Qin Xian, her heart settling at the endless devotion in his eyes.","\"Oh—did something good happen? Wait, *two* things?\" She knew they couldn’t hear her thoughts anymore, so she asked aloud.","Everyone exchanged glances.","Ji Fei blinked. \"No? The system told me before it left.\"","After a pause, someone ventured uncertainly, \"Unless... it’s...?\"","Qin Xian’s face instantly flushed red as he whispered awkwardly into Ji Fei’s ear, \"Well, our wedding might have to be postponed a bit. You’ll need to fully recover before leaving the hospital.\"","\"Huh? But I feel fine—just a little hungry.\"","\"But... you’re pregnant.\"","Ji Fei: ...","\"What?\"","\"You’re pregnant. And... with twins.\"","Ji Fei: Aaaahhhhhhhhh!","\"How could this happen? I haven’t even started enjoying my new life yet! I haven’t had the chance to be all lovey-dovey with my husband, I haven’t even... This is all your fault! Who told you to... Ugh! You jerk!\"","Qin Xian could only endure his wife’s emotional outburst. It really was his fault—though truthfully, he hadn’t planned it either. All he wanted was to be with Ji Fei.","Meanwhile, the Qin family couldn’t stop smiling. Against all odds, the babies had survived despite the dangerous circumstances, and their condition remained stable. The only worry had been Ji Fei’s exhaustion from her coma. But now that she was awake, there was nothing left to fret about.","A month later, Ji Fei was discharged from the hospital.","Their friends immediately sprang into action—altering the wedding dress, booking the venue, and arranging the ceremony.","A wedding after surviving such a ordeal deserved to be even more joyful.","Surrounded by loved ones, Qin Xian finally took the hand of the little princess he’d promised to marry all those years ago.","As for Ji Fei, she never imagined that after all the twists and turns, the one leading her to the altar would be that silent, handsome boy from her childhood.","Sunlight bathed the newlyweds’ heads.","They would be happy.","And may everyone find their own happiness too!"]}]);
